ads and reset draft files.\n- Improved SOSConfirmation to persist requests and handle media uploads.\n- Adjusted ActiveJob and IncomingAlert to display media using new URL structure.\n- Added notifications table and related policies for user notifications.\n- Introduced uploadSosMedia function for handling evidence uploads.\n- Implemented RLS policies to secure access to technician profiles and requests.\n- Seeded initial family members data and ensured proper handling of existing records.","tree":{"sha":"e6a8d0e4b8b35b309fe0e1a57f6d8a6592ec6845","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/trees/e6a8d0e4b8b35b309fe0e1a57f6d8a6592ec6845"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/commits/d634394aa578b031c8b5e3381768aaa001ffd993","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/d634394aa578b031c8b5e3381768aaa001ffd993","node_id":"C_kwDOUTTEItoAKGQ2MzQzOTRhYTU3OGIwMzFjOGI1ZTMzODE3NjhhYWEwMDFmZmQ5OTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/3f3610fe19665a4644a651efe33366497c47c7f8","sha":"3f3610fe19665a4644a651efe33366497c47c7f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/3f3610fe19665a4644a651efe33366497c47c7f8"}],"sha":"d634394aa578b031c8b5e3381768aaa001ffd993","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/d634394aa578b031c8b5e3381768aaa001ffd993"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/3f3610fe19665a4644a651efe33366497c47c7f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T13:01:45Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T13:01:45Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"message":"feat: Add EditProfileModal component for user profile editing\n\n- Implemented EditProfileModal for users to edit their name and phone number.\n- Integrated validation for name and phone number inputs.\n- Added loading and error handling states during profile update.\n\nfeat: Create ClientLiveTrackingMap component for tracking\n\n- Created a new component to export ClientLiveTrackingMap from the client app.\n\nfeat: Implement useLiveTechnicianTracking hook for real-time tracking\n\n- Developed a custom hook to manage live tracking of technicians with WebSocket support.\n- Included functions for calculating distance, bearing, and ETA based on technician''s location.\n\nchore: Add read policies for staff on users and invoices\n\n- Created policies to allow authenticated staff to select users and invoices.\n\nfeat: Enhance onboarding and signup process for technicians\n\n- Updated functions to handle new authenticated users and complete their profiles.\n- Added insert permissions for technician profiles and locations.\n- Introduced an atomic RPC for technician onboarding.\n\nfeat: Enable technicians to update their own location\n\n- Created policies to allow authenticated technicians to update their location in the database.\n\nchore: Seed initial family members for a client\n\n- Inserted initial family member records with valid PostGIS coordinates.\n\nfeat: Add structured address fields and instructions to saved addresses and requests\n\n- Enhanced saved_addresses and requests tables with structured address fields.\n- Implemented triggers to synchronize legacy and structured address fields.\n- Created policies to allow authenticated clients to insert their own requests.","tree":{"sha":"df9f5ffa7b0548b2d6a8ab4f8217c61302fda007","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/trees/df9f5ffa7b0548b2d6a8ab4f8217c61302fda007"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/commits/3f3610fe19665a4644a651efe33366497c47c7f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/3f3610fe19665a4644a651efe33366497c47c7f8","node_id":"C_kwDOUTTEItoAKDNmMzYxMGZlMTk2NjVhNDY0NGE2NTFlZmUzMzM2NjQ5N2M0N2M3Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/99708dbb1706a0f9732288c62d823d64ebfef6e9","sha":"99708dbb1706a0f9732288c62d823d64ebfef6e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/99708dbb1706a0f9732288c62d823d64ebfef6e9"}],"sha":"3f3610fe19665a4644a651efe33366497c47c7f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/3f3610fe19665a4644a651efe33366497c47c7f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/99708dbb1706a0f9732288c62d823d64ebfef6e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:22:37Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:22:37Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"message":"docs: mark src/mocks/fixtures.ts deprecated, not deleted\n\nDeleting it would break every fixture-fallback path DataProvider''s hooks\nstill legitimately use (loading state, empty-for-this-user, and the\nRLS-impossible useTechnicians() case). Marked @deprecated with a clear\nexplanation instead, pointing future work at DataProvider.tsx.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1b76140a217e295386e48aa62a98a1650d831ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/trees/d1b76140a217e295386e48aa62a98a1650d831ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/commits/99708dbb1706a0f9732288c62d823d64ebfef6e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/99708dbb1706a0f9732288c62d823d64ebfef6e9","node_id":"C_kwDOUTTEItoAKDk5NzA4ZGJiMTcwNmEwZjk3MzIyODhjNjJkODIzZDY0ZWJmZWY2ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/4a68114b2441947756910b3f35bfb57c58f814eb","sha":"4a68114b2441947756910b3f35bfb57c58f814eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/4a68114b2441947756910b3f35bfb57c58f814eb"}],"sha":"99708dbb1706a0f9732288c62d823d64ebfef6e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/99708dbb1706a0f9732288c62d823d64ebfef6e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/4a68114b2441947756910b3f35bfb57c58f814eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:18:36Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:18:36Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"message":"feat: real Supabase queries and Realtime for Client, Technician, Admin (Task 2)\n\nReal queries for every hook where the schema actually supports one, and\nthree genuine Realtime subscriptions — not a rewrite of every hook\nunconditionally, since RLS makes some of them impossible as originally\nscoped (documented below, not silently skipped).\n\n- src/context/DataProvider.tsx (new): fetches once per session (categories,\n  and role-specific data for client/technician/staff), so every hook stays\n  a synchronous selector — no hook gained a loading state, matching\n  DispatchContext''s own existing precedent for the zero-white-screen rule.\n  Every array/record defaults to empty/null; hooks fall back to the\n  fixture only when data isn''t ready or is genuinely empty.\n- Real now: useServiceCategories/useServiceCategory/useScheduledCategories\n  (service_categories, open to any authenticated user), useSavedAddresses/\n  useFamilyMembers/useFamilyMember/useClientProfile/useClientStats (all\n  scoped to auth.uid()), useRequests/useRecentRequests/useFilteredRequests\n  (requests where client_id = auth.uid(), joined for technician name and\n  category), useTechnicianJobHistory (requests where technician_id =\n  auth.uid()).\n- Deliberately still fixture-backed, documented why in each hook rather\n  than silently left alone: useTechnicians() (a general \"browse all\n  technicians\" list has no real query behind it — RLS only exposes a\n  technician''s *name* once they''re actually assigned to one of the\n  caller''s requests; browsing verified-but-unassigned technicians by name\n  isn''t a supported access pattern, by design); useTechnicianProfile /\n  usePrimaryTechnician (the id they''re called with is still\n  DispatchContext''s locally-simulated one, never a real requests.\n  technician_id, so a real query by it would always return nothing —\n  wiring the query is trivial, the id is the actual gap); notifications,\n  diagnosticQuestions, invoiceLineItems (no backing table exists at all).\n- Realtime, all three surfaces:\n  - Client: subscribes to UPDATE on its own requests; refetches on any\n    change, and flags justCompletedRequestId when one hits ''completed'' so\n    App.tsx auto-navigates to the invoice screen — verified live, staying\n    on Home the whole time, no reload. (DigitalInvoice.tsx''s *content*\n    still renders from DispatchContext''s own job state, not this real\n    request — those two aren''t unified yet; the navigation trigger is\n    real, documented exactly where that boundary is.)\n  - Technician: subscribes to INSERT on pending requests. RLS\n    (requests_select_eligible_technician) already scopes delivery to that\n    technician''s own categories/radius — no client-side filter needed.\n  - Admin: subscribes to completed requests and to disputes, using the\n    staff-read policies added last round.\n- Fixed along the way, found while making Realtime actually work: this\n  CLI''s (2.84.2) bundled local Realtime server rejects the newer\n  sb_publishable_* anon key format for the websocket handshake\n  (\"MalformedJWT\" in its own logs) — accepted for REST/RPC, rejected only\n  there. src/lib/supabaseClient.ts now defaults to the legacy JWT-format\n  ANON_KEY; .env.example documents why. (.env and .env.local, both\n  gitignored, needed the same fix locally — not part of this diff, but\n  worth knowing if Realtime looks disconnected.)\n\nVerified against the live stack throughout, not assumed:\n- Real client profile (\"Abdullah Sheikh\", not the fixture''s \"Abdullah\n  Khan\"), real computed stats, the real saved address, and the real\n  booking history (all three seeded scenarios, correct technician names\n  and amounts) — all headless-screenshotted.\n- Realtime confirmed at the wire level (websocket frames showing each\n  status transition arriving) and at the DOM level (a booking''s status\n  updates live with zero page reload).\n- Auto-navigation to the invoice screen confirmed live from a background\n  settle_job_payment call while sitting on an unrelated screen.\n- Technician''s pending-feed channel confirmed subscribed.\n- The 19-check SQL harness and demo-live-loop.mjs both still pass\n  unmodified; tsc (including apps/technician and apps/clients, which the\n  root tsconfig doesn''t cover) reports 0 errors; default build passes;\n  security advisors, db lint, and the vendored 0028/0029 checks stay\n  clean. Local DB reset to the canonical seed state (A pending, B\n  en_route, C completed) afterward.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"427527f3c659f46bb6ab250be51f4051e2d2c2c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/trees/427527f3c659f46bb6ab250be51f4051e2d2c2c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/commits/4a68114b2441947756910b3f35bfb57c58f814eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/4a68114b2441947756910b3f35bfb57c58f814eb","node_id":"C_kwDOUTTEItoAKDRhNjgxMTRiMjQ0MTk0Nzc1NjkxMGIzZjM1YmZiNTdjNThmODE0ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/bc151e5421c18d06729ba1130cb61f8dba8b7f30","sha":"bc151e5421c18d06729ba1130cb61f8dba8b7f30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/bc151e5421c18d06729ba1130cb61f8dba8b7f30"}],"sha":"4a68114b2441947756910b3f35bfb57c58f814eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/4a68114b2441947756910b3f35bfb57c58f814eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/bc151e5421c18d06729ba1130cb61f8dba8b7f30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:48:20Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:48:20Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"message":"feat: real Haversine ETA, replacing the hardcoded \"12-17 min\" tooltip (Task 4)\n\n- src/lib/eta.ts (new): haversineDistanceKm, and\n  estimateEtaMinutes(d) = max(5, round((d/25)*60) + 4) exactly as specified\n  (25 km/h urban transit + 4 min traffic/gated-entry buffer). Documented as\n  Greater-Noida-specific, not a general routing estimate.\n- src/components/LeafletLocationMap.tsx: the literal hardcoded tooltip\n  (\"En-route technician (ETA: 12-17 min)\") is gone. New\n  `technicianCoordinates` prop computes a real distance-driven ETA and also\n  now positions the technician marker/route line from it — previously that\n  marker''s position was itself a hardcoded point, same as the ETA text.\n  Falls back to a fixed demo point (documented as such) when no real\n  coordinate is passed yet, so every caller gets a genuinely computed value\n  instead of a magic string, even before Task 2 wires live positions.\n- src/screens/sos/LiveTracking.tsx: the countdown''s starting value was a\n  bare `useState(15)`; now computed once from the client''s real\n  coordinates against the same fallback point. The progress bar''s `/ 15`\n  denominator is fixed to use that same starting value instead of the old\n  constant, since 15 is no longer guaranteed to be the actual start.\n\nDeviation worth flagging: the task''s own worked example (Amit \"~1.2 km\"\nfrom Abdullah) doesn''t match the haversine distance between the two\ncoordinate pairs it also gives (28.6083,77.4267) and (28.6105,77.4320) —\nthat''s actually ~0.57 km. Implemented the coordinates and the formula\nexactly as specified; the discrepancy is in the prose distance estimate,\nnot something to paper over by fudging the math.\n\nAlso fixed per your own flag: the display range''s low end (eta - 2) is\nclamped to the formula''s 5-minute floor, so a 5-minute ETA shows \"5-8\nmins\" rather than \"3-8 mins\".\n\nVerified: the formula reproduces the exact distance between the Task 3\ncoordinates; the floor case clamps correctly (checked outside the app,\nsince this is pure arithmetic); tsc reports 0 errors; default build\npasses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0ed520745dc081aa80a508ccb9c756a5830c7a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/trees/a0ed520745dc081aa80a508ccb9c756a5830c7a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/commits/bc151e5421c18d06729ba1130cb61f8dba8b7f30","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/bc151e5421c18d06729ba1130cb61f8dba8b7f30","node_id":"C_kwDOUTTEItoAKGJjMTUxZTU0MjFjMThkMDY3MjliYTExMz