"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/619cf1d710e4a1044e306829ba6a8524291e2947","node_id":"C_kwDOUTTEItoAKDYxOWNmMWQ3MTBlNGExMDQ0ZTMwNjgyOWJhNmE4NTI0MjkxZTI5NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/20f465a189388923644196d95931028648103f53","sha":"20f465a189388923644196d95931028648103f53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/20f465a189388923644196d95931028648103f53"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca","sha":"ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca"}],"sha":"619cf1d710e4a1044e306829ba6a8524291e2947","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/619cf1d710e4a1044e306829ba6a8524291e2947"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/eec3700a622026708c6bbf4fcc2f6c023184c5ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:41:17Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:41:17Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"message":"feat(db): platform_staff governance and real admin login (Task 3 completion)\n\nFinishes what the seed-rewrite commit deferred: the schema had no way to\nrepresent an admin at all (user_role is only client/technician, and\ndocs/DATABASE.md deliberately keeps staff out of the shared users table).\nThis is genuinely new schema, not a rewire, matching your choice to build\nit properly rather than shortcut it onto user_role.\n\n- supabase/migrations/20260913000007_platform_staff.sql: platform_staff\n  table (staff_role enum: support_moderator/super_admin), RLS select-self\n  only. handle_new_auth_user now branches on\n  raw_user_meta_data->>''staff_role'': present means insert into\n  platform_staff (no phone required — staff accounts skip that gate\n  entirely); absent is the unchanged client/technician path. Adds\n  private.is_platform_staff() and additive staff-read policies on requests\n  and disputes (Task 2''s admin console needs to see every request/dispute,\n  not just ones it''s a participant in). Also adds disputes.assigned_admin_id\n  now that platform_staff exists for it to reference, completing that\n  table''s documented shape.\n- supabase/seed.sql: admin@sewasync.in / AdminPassword@123, seeded via\n  auth.users with staff_role in raw_user_meta_data so the trigger routes it\n  correctly.\n- src/context/AuthContext.tsx: loads staffRole from platform_staff\n  alongside role from users (a signed-in user has exactly one, never both).\n- src/App.tsx: the admin target now checks staffRole, not just \"any\n  session\" — a signed-in client/technician sees \"Not authorised\" instead\n  of the console.\n\nVerified against the live stack: admin@sewasync.in reaches the Ops\nconsole; abdullah@sewasync.in (a real client) gets the not-authorised\nscreen instead, both headless-verified. Security advisors, db lint, and\nthe vendored 0028/0029 checks stay clean; the SQL test harness (19/19) and\ndemo-live-loop.mjs both still pass unmodified; tsc reports 0 errors;\ndefault build passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e923c450273212e5ed408722488b77b2efa542d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/trees/e923c450273212e5ed408722488b77b2efa542d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/commits/eec3700a622026708c6bbf4fcc2f6c023184c5ef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/eec3700a622026708c6bbf4fcc2f6c023184c5ef","node_id":"C_kwDOUTTEItoAKGVlYzM3MDBhNjIyMDI2NzA4YzZiYmY0ZmNjMmY2YzAyMzE4NGM1ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca","sha":"ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca"}],"sha":"eec3700a622026708c6bbf4fcc2f6c023184c5ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/eec3700a622026708c6bbf4fcc2f6c023184c5ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:30:13Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:30:13Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"message":"feat(db): real Indian-demographic demo personas (Task 3)\n\nNew credentials, phones and coordinates exactly as specified — client\nAbdullah Sheikh, technicians Amit Singh and Rahul Kumar (Request #2 /\nScenario B maps to \"Assigned to Request #2 (en_route)\").\n\n- All four seeded accounts move to @sewasync.in / Password@123 (was\n  @sewasync.test / SewaSync@2026). Amit and Rahul get their new phone\n  numbers; Abdullah''s is unchanged since the spec kept it identical.\n- Abdullah''s home moves to Flat 402, Tower B, Gaur City 2, Greater Noida\n  West, UP 201009 at (28.6083, 77.4267) — both default_location and the\n  saved_addresses row, plus every scenario''s service_location/address_line/\n  area and the Scenario C attachment EXIF coordinates, so the whole demo\n  stays internally consistent rather than mixing old and new addresses.\n- Amit moves to (28.6105, 77.4320) \"Near Gaur City 1\" (~1.2 km from\n  Abdullah); Rahul to (28.4727, 77.4893) Knowledge Park III.\n- Rahul''s categories trimmed from three (plumbing/ac/appliance) to the two\n  the spec names (Plumbing, AC Repair).\n- The admin persona (super_admin) is deliberately NOT seeded here: the\n  schema has no way to represent it yet (user_role is only client/\n  technician, and docs/DATABASE.md deliberately keeps staff out of\n  public.users) — lands with the platform_staff migration, next.\n- Vikram Sharma isn''t in the spec''s persona list but is kept (same new\n  domain/password, unchanged phone/coordinates/categories) — removing him\n  would silently break the security test harness''s idle-technician\n  fixture and the demo script''s \"sees 0 rows\" RLS check, neither of which\n  the spec had reason to ask for.\n- scripts/demo-live-loop.mjs: credentials, technician start coordinates,\n  and two comments describing the previous unauthenticated/no-auth state,\n  now stale after last commit''s auth foundation.\n\nVerified: supabase db reset applies cleanly; the SQL security/behaviour\nharness (19/19, unaffected by any of this — it doesn''t touch credentials)\nand the full demo-live-loop.mjs both pass against the new personas exactly\nas before, including the live-tracking deep link and Google Maps\ndestination now pointing at the new coordinates. Security advisors and\ndb lint stay clean; tsc reports 0 errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"270095b33b02e070a1c78c65f5d8cc4b0eeb23ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/trees/270095b33b02e070a1c78c65f5d8cc4b0eeb23ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/commits/ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca","node_id":"C_kwDOUTTEItoAKGVlOGIxNGRkNWVmYmQyOTUzMzNlMzZkMjQ1NTA3YWRhZmFlNmUwY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/416f54c1bfd301309f972f2684c2763088d8c41f","sha":"416f54c1bfd301309f972f2684c2763088d8c41f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/416f54c1bfd301309f972f2684c2763088d8c41f"}],"sha":"ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/ee8b14dd5efbd295333e36d245507adafae6e0ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/416f54c1bfd301309f972f2684c2763088d8c41f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:24:51Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:24:51Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"message":"feat(auth): real Supabase Auth session for Client, Technician and Admin\n\nFoundation for the rest of this mission: nothing in the app had a real\nsession before this. src/lib/supabase.ts''s callRpc always sent\nAuthorization: Bearer <anon key>, so auth.uid() was null on every RPC\ncall server-side no matter what the UI did — accept_request,\nadvance_request_status, and the settle_job_payment button added last\nround could never actually succeed.\n\n- src/lib/supabaseClient.ts (new): the one real @supabase/supabase-js\n  client for the browser, session persistence on.\n- src/lib/supabase.ts: callRpc now delegates to supabase.rpc(...), which\n  attaches the current session''s JWT automatically. No more hand-rolled\n  fetch, no more anon-key-only requests.\n- src/context/AuthContext.tsx (new): session state + public.users.role,\n  kept in sync via onAuthStateChange. signIn/signOut exposed to screens.\n- src/components/Login.tsx (new): shared sign-in form, light/dark themed\n  per surface. Not a Figma export, so CLAUDE.md''s frozen-styling rule\n  doesn''t apply to it.\n- src/App.tsx: wraps in AuthProvider; both the client and admin targets\n  now gate on a session before rendering (admin''s staff-role check is\n  still pending platform_staff — documented as the next step, not done\n  here). apps/technician/src/App.tsx gates the same way.\n- src/screens/Profile.tsx, src/screens/TechnicianPortal.tsx: wired the\n  previously-inert \"Sign Out\" button; the technician header now shows\n  the real signed-in email instead of a hardcoded \"Rahul Kumar\".\n\nVerified against the live stack with a real signed-in session, not just\nread: Amit signs in via the technician login, reaches the portal, and the\nsession survives a reload. Vikram signs in, and the exact function the\n\"Confirm & Settle Job\" button calls (settleJobPaymentRpc, unmodified)\ngenuinely reaches settle_job_payment as himself — a real request goes\npending -> accepted -> completed with a real invoice row and a real\ngenerated invoice number. That''s the concrete fix for last round''s caveat\nthat the button was correctly wired but unreachable. The remaining gap\n(documented in ActiveJob.tsx): DispatchContext still creates a locally\nsimulated job id, not a real requests row, so the button doesn''t work\nend-to-end from a live SOS request yet — that''s Task 2, next.\n\nLogin gates render correctly on all three ports (headless-verified);\nCSS asset diff is purely additive (only Login''s new classes); tsc and the\ndefault build both pass; security advisors stay clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3783c1a4d0f24af4356f14973f83909c49e15547","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/trees/3783c1a4d0f24af4356f14973f83909c49e15547"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/commits/416f54c1bfd301309f972f2684c2763088d8c41f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/416f54c1bfd301309f972f2684c2763088d8c41f","node_id":"C_kwDOUTTEItoAKDQxNmY1NGMxYmZkMzAxMzA5Zjk3MmYyNjg0YzI3NjMwODhkOGM0MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/1c4682b5250dac91f4875fbe5569617aac511916","sha":"1c4682b5250dac91f4875fbe5569617aac511916","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/1c4682b5250dac91f4875fbe5569617aac511916"}],"sha":"416f54c1bfd301309f972f2684c2763088d8c41f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/416f54c1bfd301309f972f2684c2763088d8c41f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/1c4682b5250dac91f4875fbe5569617aac511916/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T07:00:21Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:19:54Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"message":"Update technician port from 3000 to 3003 across the application\n\n- Changed the technician surface port in `CLAUDE.md`, `apps/technician/package.json`, and `docker-compose.yml` to 3003.\n- Updated the dispatch bridge URL in `src/context/DispatchContext.tsx` to reflect the new port.\n- Adjusted documentation in `docs/DEPLOYMENT_VERCEL.md` to mention the updated port for the technician surface.","tree":{"sha":"6e976224686d2fd1a0fff9d02b70512bcbdc03e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/trees/6e976224686d2fd1a0fff9d02b70512bcbdc03e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/commits/1c4682b5250dac91f4875fbe5569617aac511916","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/1c4682b5250dac91f4875fbe5569617aac511916","node_id":"C_kwDOUTTEItoAKDFjNDY4MmI1MjUwZGFjOTFmNDg3NWZiZTU1Njk2MTdhYWM1MTE5MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commit/eeb0b03e535e16fd43a4eb19b3b843ed7af9f02b","sha":"eeb0b03e535e16fd43a4eb19b3b843ed7af9f02b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/eeb0b03e535e16fd43a4eb19b3b843ed7af9f02b"}],"sha":"1c4682b5250dac91f4875fbe5569617aac511916","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/1c4682b5250dac91f4875fbe5569617aac511916"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nyharena25","id":224937004,"login":"nyharena25","node_id":"U_kgDODWhELA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/commits/eeb0b03e535e16fd43a4eb19b3b843ed7af9f02b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:04:26Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:04:26Z","email":"rnyharena25@gmail.com","name":"nyharena25"},"message":"feat(db): cache technician positions in Redis (Task 5)\n\nReal integration, not the deferred/documented-gap version: Postgres can''t\ncall ioredis directly, and the browser calls report_technician_location\nstraight through PostgREST with no server process in between — so this\nwires pg_net''s async http_post from inside that RPC to a new Edge Function\n(supabase/functions/cache-technician-location) that does the actual\nSETEX ... EX 90 against Redis.\n\n- supabase/migrations/20260913000006_technician_location_redis_cache.sql:\n  CREATE OR REPLACE on private.report_technician_location, unchanged except\n  for one added best-effort net.http_post call after the existing writes.\n  A pg_net dispatch failure is caught and logged, never raised — a Redis\n  outage must not fail position reporting; technician_locations remains\n  the source of truth.\n- supabase/functions/cache-technician-location/index.ts: Deno edge\n  function, no npm dependency (uses deno.land/x/redis to sidestep the\n  edge-runtime''s noNpm policy). Internal-only — reachable from containers\n  on supabase_network_SewaSyncx, never through Kong/the public API — so it\n  intentionally skips JWT verification (verify_jwt=false in config.toml),\n  documented in its header as a local-dev trade-off to revisit before\n  production.\n- docker-compose.yml: redis now also joins supabase_network_SewaSyncx (an\n  external network created by `supabase start`) so the edge-runtime\n  container can resolve and reach it by name. This makes `docker compose\n  up` require Supabase to already be running — a real, accepted trade-off\n  for this integration, not an oversight; documented inline.\n\nVerified against the live stack, not just read: net.http_post from psql to\nthe function returns 200 {\"ok\":true}; the key lands in Redis with the\nright JSON shape and a 90s TTL; running the real report_technician_location\nRPC (via demo-live-loop.mjs, unmodified) for all three seeded technicians\npopulates all three Redis keys with their real coordinates. Security\nadvisors, db lint and the vendored 0028/0029 checks all stay clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8053c0d74bf09c0f86dc6b55d7593b4e527d23b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/trees/8053c0d74bf09c0f86dc6b55d7593b4e527d23b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/azhanxsheikh/SewaSyncx/git/commits/eeb0b03e535e16fd43a4eb19b3b843ed7af9f02b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224937004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nyharena25/followers","following_url":"https://api.githu