":{"account":{"login":"Ashok-2004","providerType":"User"},"email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:35:34.716Z","repositoryId":1362611732,"sha":"53ce2a9718d62ddf04af025834454d8a14b68f65"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:35:34.716Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e35697e445ad84c52b09d36266b7dc802f7a241e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T04:07:24Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T04:07:24Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Pin the test timezone, so a date test cannot pass locally and fail on CI\n\ndateRange.test.ts guards against a custom range being read as UTC when it should\nbe read as local wall-clock time, and it did so by naming the UTC instant:\n\n    expect(from).toBe(new Date(2026, 8, 12, 9, 0, 0).toISOString())\n    expect(from).not.toBe(''2026-09-12T09:00:00.000Z'')\n\nThose two readings only differ at a non-zero offset. A GitHub runner is UTC, so\nthere the second line asserted that a value was not equal to itself and failed:\n\n    AssertionError: expected ''2026-09-12T09:00:00.000Z''\n                 not to be ''2026-09-12T09:00:00.000Z''\n\nNothing is wrong with resolveDateRange — it reads the time as local, which is\nwhat it should do. The test was simply unrunnable in UTC, and it passed here only\nbecause this machine is UTC+5:30. The file''s own header claimed the assertions\n\"have to hold in whatever zone CI happens to run in\"; that one did not.\n\nRather than weaken the guard — it is the only thing standing between us and the\nApproval Center bug it was written for — the zone is now pinned in vitest.config\nfor every package whose code touches dates. Local and UTC are then genuinely\ndifferent wherever the suite runs, so the guard means something and a CI failure\nreproduces off CI. host-bridge is left alone: it has no Date in it.\n\nAsia/Kuala_Lumpur, because it is the platform''s own zone and has no daylight\nsaving, so day boundaries do not move with the season.\n\nThe test also asserts the pin is in force before relying on it. Without that,\nremoving the pin would not fail the guard, it would quietly make it vacuous\nagain; now it fails on the precondition and says so.\n\nVerified: lint, typecheck and all 1010 tests pass with the shell at TZ=UTC (what\nthe runner does), unset, and at America/New_York.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f2380e98a72dd29d7a73aab45a6c0cc449c69715","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/f2380e98a72dd29d7a73aab45a6c0cc449c69715"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/e35697e445ad84c52b09d36266b7dc802f7a241e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/e35697e445ad84c52b09d36266b7dc802f7a241e","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGUzNTY5N2U0NDVhZDg0YzUyYjA5ZDM2MjY2YjdkYzgwMmY3YTI0MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/e119cf9285ba7cac3cafcaee458c1d0eb981ad74","sha":"e119cf9285ba7cac3cafcaee458c1d0eb981ad74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e119cf9285ba7cac3cafcaee458c1d0eb981ad74"}],"sha":"e35697e445ad84c52b09d36266b7dc802f7a241e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e35697e445ad84c52b09d36266b7dc802f7a241e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e119cf9285ba7cac3cafcaee458c1d0eb981ad74/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:41:00Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:41:00Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"product marketplace and lead ui enhanced","tree":{"sha":"66559ffbafc0306c6b1f5fc692c1903a75ae9a1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/66559ffbafc0306c6b1f5fc692c1903a75ae9a1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/e119cf9285ba7cac3cafcaee458c1d0eb981ad74","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/e119cf9285ba7cac3cafcaee458c1d0eb981ad74","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGUxMTljZjkyODViYTdjYWMzY2FmY2FlZTQ1OGMxZDBlYjk4MWFkNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/55aa27d46667dbde721abcd621ae6c2e7636d616","sha":"55aa27d46667dbde721abcd621ae6c2e7636d616","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/55aa27d46667dbde721abcd621ae6c2e7636d616"}],"sha":"e119cf9285ba7cac3cafcaee458c1d0eb981ad74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e119cf9285ba7cac3cafcaee458c1d0eb981ad74"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/55aa27d46667dbde721abcd621ae6c2e7636d616/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:30:27Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:30:27Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Release: new versions for the UI polish\n\nEvery app''s bundle changes here, including the two whose own source did not: the\nhost and Customer 360 both consume the shared package, and its Tabs, dropdown and\nrows-per-page styles changed. A version names one build forever, so each gets a\nnew one rather than reusing 1.1.0 for different content, which deploy.sh would\nrefuse if 1.1.0 had already been placed on a server.\n\n  host         1.1.0 -> 1.1.1\n  lead_mf      1.1.0 -> 1.1.1\n  products_mf  1.1.0 -> 1.1.1\n  customer360  1.0.1 -> 1.0.2\n  @omniconnect/ui 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0\n\nFrontend only. No backend image changes, so no tags move and nothing restarts;\nhost-bridge is untouched at 1.1.0 and all three remotes still declare ^1.0.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b73ad5570c54740fed27511fde76ac3d1864402","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/5b73ad5570c54740fed27511fde76ac3d1864402"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/55aa27d46667dbde721abcd621ae6c2e7636d616","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/55aa27d46667dbde721abcd621ae6c2e7636d616","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDU1YWEyN2Q0NjY2N2RiZGU3MjFhYmNkNjIxYWU2YzJlNzYzNmQ2MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/9b87a37c4874ac00027e2d53542a8533b5671b5f","sha":"9b87a37c4874ac00027e2d53542a8533b5671b5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/9b87a37c4874ac00027e2d53542a8533b5671b5f"}],"sha":"55aa27d46667dbde721abcd621ae6c2e7636d616","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/55aa27d46667dbde721abcd621ae6c2e7636d616"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/9b87a37c4874ac00027e2d53542a8533b5671b5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:27:37Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:27:37Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Host tests: give waitFor the suite''s own timeout budget\n\nvitest''s testTimeout is already sized for a loaded machine, but Testing Library''s\nwaitFor and findBy* give up after 1s whatever that is set to. A page needing 1.2s\nto settle under load failed its first waitFor with 19 seconds of test time unspent.\nIt showed as one Checker Assignment test failing now and then in a full run and\nnever on its own. A passing assertion returns as soon as it passes, so the longer\nlimit costs nothing on a quiet machine.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6e8802f27f8cf602cc8f20719b1c37ad191a23b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/6e8802f27f8cf602cc8f20719b1c37ad191a23b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/9b87a37c4874ac00027e2d53542a8533b5671b5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/9b87a37c4874ac00027e2d53542a8533b5671b5f","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDliODdhMzdjNDg3NGFjMDAwMjdlMmQ1MzU0MmE4NTMzYjU2NzFiNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/9f1abad5a9e1b2a614f95cd0797833e3780d5a1b","sha":"9f1abad5a9e1b2a614f95cd0797833e3780d5a1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/9f1abad5a9e1b2a614f95cd0797833e3780d5a1b"}],"sha":"9b87a37c4874ac00027e2d53542a8533b5671b5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/9b87a37c4874ac00027e2d53542a8533b5671b5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/9f1abad5a9e1b2a614f95cd0797833e3780d5a1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:27:37Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:27:37Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Create Lead: one card in three bands, and no empty box\n\nThe form opened with a large dashed \"Select a product\" panel under the three\npickers: an empty state that filled the card and only repeated what the dropdowns\nabove it already said. It is gone. Until a product is chosen the card is just the\nproduct step, with one quiet line where the form will open.\n\nThe card is now three bands. The product step heads it, with the chosen product\nshown as a chip that stays in view while the form is filled in. The fields sit on\nthe sunken body. The actions are a footer bar at the right, as a drawer has: the\nsubmit button was a full-width, large button at the bottom of the scroll, the\nheaviest element on a page whose every other control is ordinary size. Clear form\nsits beside it.\n\nWhile the chosen product''s field settings load, the sections are placeholders\nshaped like sections. Drawing the real ones straight away was wrong in a specific\nway: a field counts as visible until the settings say otherwise, so every field\nappeared and the ones an administrator had switched off then disappeared. The\nedit drawer had the same flash and gets the same fix.\n\nControls now match each other. Dropdowns take the text inputs'' height and fill\n(the shared field layer does this). The dial-code picker had its border and fill\nstripped to sit \"flush inside the phone field''s border\", a box that no longer\nexists; it is a field control of its own again, and no longer takes the row from\nthe number. The two consent choices are rows you can click anywhere on, tinted\nwhen chosen, instead of two bare 13px browser radios on the one question in the\nform that has legal weight.\n\nThe card does not clip, so the calendar can open past its edge; the bands round\ntheir own outer corners.\n\nDashboard cards and the chart chunks'' fallback draw a trend line, a ring with its\nlegend and bar rows instead of slabs and a blank white box.\n\nA catalogue response that is not JSON gets the plain \"could not be loaded\"\nmessage. It showed the parser''s own words to whoever was taking the lead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1cae17bfac4ae77fb3dc20bec5b81dc5a23a046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/d1cae17bfac4ae77fb3dc20bec5b81dc5a23a046"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/9f1abad5a9e1b2a614f95cd0797833e3780d5a1b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/9f1abad5a9e1b2a614f95cd0797833e3780d5a1b","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDlmMWFiYWQ1YTllMWIyYTYxNGY5NWNkMDc5NzgzM2UzNzgwZDVhMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/1349c6ba19efd158195f96bb03f114c780063f7c","sha":"1349c6ba19efd158195f96bb03f114c780063f7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/1349c6ba19efd158195f96bb03f114c780063f7c"}],"sha":"9f1abad5a9e1b2a614f95cd0797833e3780d5a1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/9f1abad5a9e1b2a614f95cd0797833e3780d5a1b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/1349c6ba19efd158195f96bb03f114c780063f7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:27:36Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:27:36Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Marketplace: one-row toolbar, a real Setup header, and loading that looks like the page\n\nToolbar. On Sub-categories and Products the filter row broke onto two lines, with\nReset / Rows / Refresh dropped below on their own. A flex row decides where to\nbreak from what each item ASKS for, not from how far it could shrink, and every\nfilter asked for 200px. Search and filters now ask for a small basis and grow into\nwhat is left; the actions never shrink. One row fits from ~975px with three\nfilters, which is the host at 1366px with its sidebar open. Below that the toolbar\nis a size container, so it responds to the width of the CARD rather than the\nwindow, and switches to a designed two-row layout: search across the first row,\nfilters and actions sharing the second.\n\nSetup. The three views are a segmented control in a bar of their own, the\ntreatment the host gives the same situation, instead of an underlined strip bare\non the page. Each card gets a proper header (icon tile, title, what it is for, its\naction) in place of a small rule-and-label borrowed from form groups, which read\nas an untitled card. The pickers are labelled. The sentence about live statuses is\nsaid once above the three status cards, not repeated in each.\n\nLoading. Stat tiles hold their row with shape-matched placeholders instead of\narriving after the table and pushing it down. The product grid shows product\ncards that have not loaded, not six blank slabs. The dashboard draws the outline\nof a bar chart, a ring with its legend and a feed; the drawers draw a form or a\ndetail panel.\n\nAlso:\n- Four tiles go 4 -> 2 -> 1 at the host''s breakpoints. Left to auto-fit they\n  broke 3 + 1, the fourth alone on its own row.\n- The category tabs head the card they filter. Their wrapper had overflow-x only,\n  which turned a one-pixel overhang into a vertical scrollbar with arrows.\n- A 2xx whose body is a web page is refused as a failure. A misrouted path\n  answers index.html with status 200; the page that asked for a list called .map\n  on a string and took the whole screen down. Found because a release build did\n  exactly that on the dev server.\n- \"33 productss\": the pagination nouns are singular now, with their plurals.\n- The standalone entry re-reads ?page= on popstate, like lead_mf''s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79049c49d731b16bfb87f6e27b69cf0677478d81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/79049c49d731b16bfb87f6e27b69cf0677478d81"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/1349c6ba19efd158195f96bb03f114c780063f7c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/1349c6ba19efd158195f96bb03f114c780063f7c","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDEzNDljNmJhMTllZmQxNTgxOTVmOTZiYjAzZjExNGM3ODAwNjNmN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/0cb98093ff4b79b3e39ba873705a3cb71dc4982b","sha":"0cb98093ff4b79b3e39ba873705a3cb71dc4982b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/0cb98093ff4b79b3e39ba873705a3cb71dc4982b"}],"sha":"1349c6ba19efd158195f96bb03f114c780063f7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/1349c6ba19efd158195f96bb03f114c780063f7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/0cb98093ff4b79b3e39ba873705a3cb71dc4982b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:27:16Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:27:16Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Shared UI: skeletons shaped like what they replace, a finished stat tile, one field look\n\nLoading felt unfinished in the remotes because a grey rectangle was all they\ndrew: one 320px slab where a form would be, another where a chart would be. The\nhost has always drawn the thing that is coming. This gives the shared package the\nsame vocabulary, for the pieces it owns:\n\n- StatTileSkeleton, the tile with its content replaced in place.\n- SkeletonForm, FormSection cards with a title rule over a label + control grid.\n- SkeletonDetail, DetailSection cards holding icon + label + value tiles.\n- SkeletonChart, as bars, a ring with its legend, or a trend line over gridlines.\n  The ring is punched with a mask so the shimmer still sweeps the band.\n- SkeletonList, a leading mark and two lines per row.\n\nEach copies its geometry from the component it stands in for, so content lands\nwhere its placeholder was and nothing jumps. Bar heights are fixed, not random: a\nskeleton that reshuffles on every render flickers.\n\nStatTile takes the host''s own summary-card treatment (it was the flatter of the\ntwo): a gradient rule that follows the card''s corners, a tinted icon tile with a\nhairline border, an uppercase label, a heavy tightly-set figure, the change as a\npill, a lift on hover. Two accents the host uses and the tokens lack, neutral and\nviolet, so a row of four tiles can be four colours.\n\nA dropdown inside a FormField now matches the text box beside it. Forms mixed\n46px tinted inputs with 36px white outlined dropdowns in one grid. FormField\npublishes the Input''s geometry as --omni-field-* properties and Combobox reads\nthem with its standalone look as the fallback, so toolbar filters are untouched.\n\nThree fixes found on the way:\n\n- Tabs relied on the host''s global reset to clear native button chrome, so a\n  remote rendered outside the host drew each tab as a grey bordered box.\n- RowsPerPage had a minimum width and no width, inside a box sized by its\n  content, so it fell back to the input''s intrinsic ~180px to show a two-digit\n  number. That alone pushed toolbars onto a second row.\n- Pagination appended an \"s\" to whatever it was given. The marketplace passed\n  plurals and showed \"33 productss\"; passing singulars would have produced\n  \"8 categorys\". It takes itemLabelPlural, and is tested.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0c6371338fd8ba1f2d6690663b1b7b8c5e1f46f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/b0c6371338fd8ba1f2d6690663b1b7b8c5e1f46f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/0cb98093ff4b79b3e39ba873705a3cb71dc4982b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/0cb98093ff4b79b3e39ba873705a3cb71dc4982b","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDBjYjk4MDkzZmY0Yjc5YjNlMzliYTg3MzcwNWEzY2I3MWRjNDk4MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/e151afb6512756ed4e6b941d3dd01e5bf70c45be","sha":"e151afb6512756ed4e6b941d3dd01e5bf70c45be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e151afb6512756ed4e6b941d3dd01e5bf70c45be"}],"sha":"0cb98093ff4b79b3e39ba873705a3cb71dc4982b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/0cb98093ff4b79b3e39ba873705a3cb71dc4982b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e151afb6512756ed4e6b941d3dd01e5bf70c45be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:44:26Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:44:26Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Release: version every app that changed, and the AuthService image\n\nA release version names one build forever — deploy.sh aborts if a version folder\nis already present with different content — so every app touched in this branch\nneeds a new one before any of it can ship.\n\n  host         1.0.0 -> 1.1.0   login hero, Checker Assignment, route redirects\n  lead_mf      1.0.0 -> 1.1.0   create-lead rebuild, refresh fixes\n  products_mf  1.0.0 -> 1.1.0   page anatomy, refresh, audit toolbar\n  customer360  1.0.0 -> 1.0.1   refresh fix only\n  @omniconnect/ui 0.0.0 -> 0.1.0  new form layer; a workspace dep, not released\n\npackages/host-bridge is untouched and stays at 1.1.0: nothing here changes the\nhost-to-remote contract, and every remote still declares ^1.0.0. `pnpm release`\nconfirms it — host 1.1.0 (bridge 1.1.0), all three remotes satisfied.\n\nBackend: only AuthService changed, so only AUTH_TAG moves. The other three images\nare byte-identical and `up -d` will not recreate their containers, which is what\nkeeps this from being a full-platform restart. No new env entries — the change is\na filter, a DTO field and a data migration, and reads no configuration that was\nnot already there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ee6c4e51091bfed9992761dc484c1b812c83621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/7ee6c4e51091bfed9992761dc484c1b812c83621"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/e151afb6512756ed4e6b941d3dd01e5bf70c45be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/e151afb6512756ed4e6b941d3dd01e5bf70c45be","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGUxNTFhZmI2NTEyNzU2ZWQ0ZTZiOTQxZDNkZDAxZTViZjcwYzQ1YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/ac36424fc41cb582bca8ba9a13cc8814ebd06099","sha":"ac36424fc41cb582bca8ba9a13cc8814ebd06099","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/ac36424fc41cb582bca8ba9a13cc8814ebd06099"}],"sha":"e151afb6512756ed4e6b941d3dd01e5bf70c45be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e151afb6512756ed4e6b941d3dd01e5bf70c45be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/ac36424fc41cb582bca8ba9a13cc8814ebd06099/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:40:43Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:40:43Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Products & Marketplace: the host''s page anatomy, not just its tokens\n\nThis remote was already the most token-pure code in the repo — not one hardcoded\nhex in any of its stylesheets, where the host reference itself has plenty. It was\nnever part of the shared-UI pass though, so it was built against the tokens and\nnot against the component set, and the misalignment was structural:\n\n- no page max-width, so it ran the full width of a wide monitor while every other\n  screen was capped at 1340px — the loudest tell in the whole app;\n- its own page padding on top of the host shell''s, sitting ~46px in where the\n  rest of the platform sits at 26-28px;\n- no entry animation, so moving from a host page to this one dropped the\n  transition;\n- 1px/12px card chrome against the platform''s 1.5px/18px;\n- the filter row floating on the page background instead of inside the card, with\n  the table bare underneath it;\n- tables that scrolled sideways rather than collapsing columns, so action buttons\n  left the screen on a narrow window;\n- no Refresh anywhere, no persisted rows-per-page, no active-filter chips, and no\n  headline figures except on the audit screen.\n\nThe list pages now have the Users-page anatomy end to end: PageHeader, stat tiles,\nFilterBar, then one card holding the toolbar and the table, with ResponsiveRows,\nreserveHeight so paging stops jumping, and a real empty state. ListToolbar keeps\nits five debounce behaviours (its tests are the spec for them) and gains a\ntrailing slot, which is what let Refresh and RowsPerPage land on four pages at\nonce rather than being retrofitted per page.\n\nThe tiles read `/dashboard/summary`, which counts on the server — deliberately\nnot the rows on screen, which is how \"Total products\" used to change when you\npaged. A failed summary read leaves the tiles out rather than showing a wrong\nnumber.\n\nFour local components move to @omniconnect/ui instead of being deleted: Field\nbecomes FormField, TextArea and KpiTile become StatTile, and ConfirmDialog goes\nacross whole, because its approval-pending and server-refusal handling is worth\nhaving platform-wide. RowMenu and StatusBadge stay — ui has no overflow menu, and\nStatusBadge resolves tone from the Setup store.\n\nTwo real bugs found on the way: the donut''s centre label was set at 2.6px inside a\n42-unit viewBox, about a third the proportional size of everything around it; and\nApp.tsx imported tokens.css after the page components, so the comment claiming it\ncame first was false and the tokens landed last in the bundle. Harmless only\nbecause tokens.css is @layer-wrapped — exactly the trap\ndocs/SHARED-UI-REFACTOR-STATUS.md warns about.\n\ndocs/AUDIT-EVENTS.md gains the ProductsService section it never had: it documented\nAuth, Lead and Customer360 only, and still said \"all five log screens\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a72404a1262b7c5998835cc600444a216b83871","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/6a72404a1262b7c5998835cc600444a216b83871"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/ac36424fc41cb582bca8ba9a13cc8814ebd06099","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/ac36424fc41cb582bca8ba9a13cc8814ebd06099","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGFjMzY0MjRmYzQxY2I1ODJiY2E4YmE5YTEzY2M4ODE0ZWJkMDYwOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/dd6707ce34111b3fd403994106f231d6b001ba96","sha":"dd6707ce34111b3fd403994106f231d6b001ba96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/dd6707ce34111b3fd403994106f231d6b001ba96"}],"sha":"ac36424fc41cb582bca8ba9a13cc8814ebd06099","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/ac36424fc41cb582bca8ba9a13cc8814ebd06099"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/dd6707ce34111b3fd403994106f231d6b001ba96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:37:02Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:37:02Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Create Lead: the platform''s card chrome, and the last of the legacy form CSS\n\nThe form was the one screen in this app still drawing its own chrome. Its card\ncame from the global `.form-card` in index.css — 12px radius, a 1px border and\nthe heavier `--shadow-card` — while Dashboard, View Leads, Audit Trail and Field\nSettings all use leadPage.module.css''s `.card` at 18px / 1.5px #e8edf5 /\n`0 2px 8px`. Next to any of them the form read as a different product. It now\ncomposes that same card instead of restating it.\n\nThe FormSections inside it were white on white. They are a faithful copy of the\nhost''s Create/Edit User form card, which works because the host''s form scrolls on\na tinted contentArea — the cards are lighter than what is behind them. Dropped on\na white page card there was nothing to be lighter than, and the form looked like\none flat sheet with faint lines on it. The form body is now sunken, one step\nbelow surface-alt: across a 1340px page a 2% tint is invisible, which is why this\nuses the same slate the platform already uses for a disabled input rather than\nthe drawer''s value. The empty state lifts to white for the same reason.\n\nDatePicker was the last component on the global classes — `.dropdown-trigger` and\n`.date-picker-*`, a third form vocabulary alongside the host''s and the shared\none. Its trigger now restates Input''s exact geometry (46px, 1.5px #e2e8f0,\nradius-lg, the same hover, focus ring and invalid colours), so the date field\nmatches the field beside it in the grid. Its local class names were leftovers\nused as arbitrary hooks — the clear button wore `calendarIcon`, the calendar icon\nwore `footerRow`, the month/year selects wore `clearBtn` and `todayBtn` — and now\nsay what they are. Picked up on the way: real day buttons instead of clickable\ndivs, labelled nav controls, a today marker, and Escape closing the calendar and\nreturning focus to the trigger.\n\nindex.css loses 177 more lines: the form/dropdown/date-picker blocks and four\ndead keyframes. `fadeInForm` moves into the module that uses it, rather than\nstaying a global animating a module class from outside — a link neither file\ndeclared and nothing checked. No .tsx references a global form class any more.\n\nAlso: a jest-dom matcher shim for packages/ui, which had no DOM tests until\nFormField and ConfirmDialog arrived, and a dev-only `?page=` in lead_mf''s\nstandalone entry so a screen other than the dashboard can be opened at :5002\nwithout a host session. Neither is in the Module Federation surface.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f83727bde9bbbfa32798eea3e3d5993e187fb95d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/f83727bde9bbbfa32798eea3e3d5993e187fb95d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/dd6707ce34111b3fd403994106f231d6b001ba96","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/dd6707ce34111b3fd403994106f231d6b001ba96","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGRkNjcwN2NlMzQxMTFiM2ZkNDAzOTk0MTA2ZjIzMWQ2YjAwMWJhOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/7bba3c1e3c74159133eb3ce11d26a769616d0b0d","sha":"7bba3c1e3c74159133eb3ce11d26a769616d0b0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/7bba3c1e3c74159133eb3ce11d26a769616d0b0d"}],"sha":"dd6707ce34111b3fd403994106f231d6b001ba96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/dd6707ce34111b3fd403994106f231d6b001ba96"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/7bba3c1e3c74159133eb3ce11d26a769616d0b0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T11:02:08Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T11:02:08Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Create Lead: real dropdowns, and a form layer the whole platform can share\n\nThe product picker was a two-step grid of cards with no search anywhere: you clicked a\ncategory, the grid was replaced by a grid of products, and you clicked one. That reads\nfine against six demo products and not at all against a real catalogue — a wall of cards,\nno way to type a name you already know, and a sub-category you could never select even\nthough Field Settings is organised by it. It is now three cascading comboboxes, each\ntype-to-search, with the sub-category derived from the products already fetched rather\nthan from a new endpoint.\n\nThe deeper reason the form \"looked like a different app\" was that `packages/ui` shipped\n`Input`, which carries its own label, and nothing for the controls that do not — selects,\ncomboboxes, textareas, date pickers. So three competing form systems grew up: the host''s\nown form layer, lead management''s 468 lines of global `.form-*`, and the marketplace''s\nlocal `Field`. This adds the missing layer — FormSection, FormGrid, FormField, TextArea,\nplus StatTile and ConfirmDialog promoted from the marketplace — all taken from the host,\nwhich is this package''s design reference.\n\nFormField is not only a wrapper for the look. This flow had no `htmlFor`, no `id`, no\n`aria-invalid` and no `aria-describedby` anywhere, so a screen reader announced an unnamed\nbox and never read the message that appeared under it. Passing a function to FormField\ngets all four right without the caller thinking about it; passing a plain node falls back\nto a named group, for the phone prefix beside its number and the two consent radios.\n\nEvery `isFieldVisible` guard, every `getFieldLabel` / `isFieldRequired` /\n`isFieldEditable` call and both section-level conditions are preserved — the fields are\nwritten out one by one because each is a different control over a different part of the\nform state, and the config only decides whether and how it appears. Validation is\nuntouched: still `leadFormats.ts` over the shared rule engine, not the host''s.\n\nSearchableDropdown (216 lines) is gone in favour of the shared Combobox, which portals its\nlist so a drawer''s overflow cannot clip it. DatePicker keeps its calendar but no longer\nrenders a label, a required marker or an error line of its own, and the inline style that\ngreyed out its trigger is now a class. The browser alert() behind the privacy-policy link\nis now the app''s own toast.\n\nWith the markup gone, 833 lines of lead_mf''s index.css could go with it — every rule that\nrequired a class nothing renders any more. Also repairs `host''\"''\"''s` in three stylesheet\ncomments, left by a shell-quoting accident in an earlier change.\n\nTests: ProductPicker''s eight cases were written entirely against the card markup and are\nrewritten for the comboboxes, with new ones for the cascade and the derived sub-category\nlist. LeadFormContainer had no test at all and now has eight, holding the thing a restyle\nbreaks most quietly — that a field switched off stays off and a renamed field appears under\nthe administrator''s name. FormField has its own, for wiring that is invisible on screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2baa85ed74575c0cac17e3cccca139ac5ad578b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/2baa85ed74575c0cac17e3cccca139ac5ad578b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/7bba3c1e3c74159133eb3ce11d26a769616d0b0d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/7bba3c1e3c74159133eb3ce11d26a769616d0b0d","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDdiYmEzYzFlM2M3NDE1OTEzM2ViM2NlMTFkMjZhNzY5NjE2ZDBiMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/c43f1f7867aa8be4ceb7daae7c6cceac02ae2774","sha":"c43f1f7867aa8be4ceb7daae7c6cceac02ae2774","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/c43f1f7867aa8be4ceb7daae7c6cceac02ae2774"}],"sha":"7bba3c1e3c74159133eb3ce11d26a769616d0b0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/7bba3c1e3c74159133eb3ce11d26a769616d0b0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/c43f1f7867aa8be4ceb7daae7c6cceac02ae2774/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:42:46Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:42:46Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Checker Assignment: only things a checker can actually hold, named after the task\n\nAudit Logs, System Logs and the dashboards were on offer in Checker Assignment, and\nassigning one did nothing: maker-checker holds a change until someone approves it, and\na log you can only read has no change to hold. Worse, the list read as though viewing a\nlog required approval. Read access is a permission question and is already answered in\nRoles & Permissions.\n\nA feature is now offered only if it declares a capability that changes something. The\nverb list lives in one place next to GetAssignableModulesAsync, so a new remote''s\nvocabulary is classified there rather than in three call sites, and a dotted key\n(\"chart.leads-by-branch\") can never be mistaken for a module-level action.\n\nEach row now also names the actions it gates — \"Leads · Create / Edit / Delete\" — which\nis what people were looking for when they came here to assign a checker for \"creating a\nlead\". It stays a list rather than one action per row because an assignment is stored\nonce per module, so one checker genuinely covers all of them; naming a row \"Create Lead\"\nalone would be a label that lies.\n\nFiltering the picker is not enough on its own. IsGatedAsync only asks whether a row\nexists for the module and never consults the assignable list, so an assignment made\nbefore this would have gone on gating invisibly — in the database, absent from every\nscreen. The migration deletes those rows, judging each against the catalog as it stands\nrather than a hardcoded list of keys so a remote''s own read-only modules are covered too.\n\nThe Approval Center is unaffected: its module filter is built from the queue''s own\nfacets, not from this endpoint, so a request raised against a now-excluded module stays\nfilterable.\n\nPermission grants needed no work — RoleAppService and UserAppService already route them\nthrough ApprovalGatingService under host.settings.roles / host.settings.users. There is\nnow a test holding that, so it cannot quietly regress.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5dbcbeca1a04dcbfb726258d64db3d6f9fc60124","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/5dbcbeca1a04dcbfb726258d64db3d6f9fc60124"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/c43f1f7867aa8be4ceb7daae7c6cceac02ae2774","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/c43f1f7867aa8be4ceb7daae7c6cceac02ae2774","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGM0M2YxZjc4NjdhYThiZTRjZWI3ZGFhZTdjNmNjZWFjMDJhZTI3NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/07a5ca7ef103e7855467b295a40682cd659b36fd","sha":"07a5ca7ef103e7855467b295a40682cd659b36fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/07a5ca7ef103e7855467b295a40682cd659b36fd"}],"sha":"c43f1f7867aa8be4ceb7daae7c6cceac02ae2774","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/c43f1f7867aa8be4ceb7daae7c6cceac02ae2774"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/07a5ca7ef103e7855467b295a40682cd659b36fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:14:05Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:14:05Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"A section you do not have sends you to the dashboard, not to a 404\n\nHiding is unchanged and still the thing that keeps a module private: the server\nbuilds the navigation tree and simply omits what the caller may not reach\n(NavigationTreeBuilder), and the Settings drawer filters the same way. What\nchanges is where a denied URL lands.\n\nRequireCapability and RemoteAppPage answered every denial with the 404 page, so\nan unauthorised route could not be told from a non-existent one. The people\nactually hitting it were following a bookmark or a colleague''s link, and were\ntold the platform was broken when their account simply does not have that\nsection — on a page with nothing they could do next. Both now redirect to the\ndashboard. A page segment inside an app the user DOES have goes to that app''s own\nfirst page instead, which is nearer to where they were heading.\n\nThe trade-off is stated in RequireCapability''s doc comment rather than left\nimplicit: a redirect does distinguish \"you may not open this\" from \"no such\npage\". The tree remains the non-disclosure boundary, and nothing here advertises\na section to someone not already guessing its URL.\n\nThat makes DashboardRoute''s last fallback matter more, since every denial now\npasses through it. An account with nothing assigned at all used to arrive at the\nsame 404; it gets NoAccessPage, which says what has happened and who can fix it.\n\nRemoved ForbiddenPage: no call sites, and its whole behaviour was to render the\n404 page, which is no longer what a denial does.\n\nTests: RequireCapability (allows, redirects, administrator bypass, and does NOT\nredirect while the session is still hydrating — that one would throw an entitled\nuser off the page on every refresh) and RemoteAppPage (unknown app, unknown page\nsegment, still-loading tree). Neither had any coverage before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76548cc85e0f81b096554c952d3df493b7aeecbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/76548cc85e0f81b096554c952d3df493b7aeecbe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/07a5ca7ef103e7855467b295a40682cd659b36fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/07a5ca7ef103e7855467b295a40682cd659b36fd","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDA3YTVjYTdlZjEwM2U3ODU1NDY3YjI5NWE0MDY4MmNkNjU5YjM2ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/f103e03b02dcc58bbbfb6d31cb67e4c5436c2862","sha":"f103e03b02dcc58bbbfb6d31cb67e4c5436c2862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/f103e03b02dcc58bbbfb6d31cb67e4c5436c2862"}],"sha":"07a5ca7ef103e7855467b295a40682cd659b36fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/07a5ca7ef103e7855467b295a40682cd659b36fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/f103e03b02dcc58bbbfb6d31cb67e4c5436c2862/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:10:33Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:10:33Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Refresh buttons that actually refetch\n\nEvery read in the three remotes goes through createRequestCache, which reuses a\nsuccessful result for 30s. That cache documents a `force` escape hatch and NONE\nof the three HTTP layers ever passed it, so a Refresh button re-sending an\nidentical URL was answered from memory and sent no request at all: the spinner\nturned, the same rows re-rendered, and the button looked broken because it was.\n\nEach remote now has one way for a caller to say \"ask the server\":\n\n- lead_mf  fetchWithAuth already honoured `cache: ''no-store''`; getLeads and\n  getAuditLogs take a `fresh` flag that sets it.\n- customer360_mf  request() had no bypass whatsoever. It now reads the same\n  `cache: ''no-store''` idiom and passes `force`, so the fresh answer also replaces\n  what was stored rather than stepping around it.\n- products_and_marketplace_mf  the caching axios adapter reads a `fresh` flag on\n  the request config (declaration-merged onto AxiosRequestConfig).\n\nWired up: both lead_mf buttons (which also gain the `disabled` guard the audit one\nwas missing), the customer360 Audit Trail button, and the products audit page''s\nlive-events banner and retry. The products page''s own Refresh button comes with\nits toolbar restructure.\n\nAlso stops lead_mf disguising a failed read as an empty result set: getLeads and\ngetAuditLogs returned an empty page for a 500 or a dropped connection, so a failed\nrefresh looked exactly like a table that had been emptied. They now throw, and the\nstore keeps the rows on screen and raises a toast.\n\ncustomer360''s Interactions refresh was working only because /v1/interactions is\nabsent from the REUSABLE regex and so gets ttlMs 0 — it now says what it means.\n\nTests: three new suites covering \"a second click sends a second request\", that a\nforced read leaves its answer cached for the next reader, that it refreshes only\nthe query asked about, and that a failed read is reported rather than blanked.\nThe products one stubs axios.getAdapter rather than httpClient.defaults.adapter,\nbecause assigning defaults.adapter replaces the caching adapter and tests nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d0635857149223fe5c36d0e0e05ee08d8971ecc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/d0635857149223fe5c36d0e0e05ee08d8971ecc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/f103e03b02dcc58bbbfb6d31cb67e4c5436c2862","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/f103e03b02dcc58bbbfb6d31cb67e4c5436c2862","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGYxMDNlMDNiMDJkY2M1OGJiYmZiNmQzMWNiNjdlNGM1NDM2YzI4NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/55ff8cfedf8c38e4c2a7943a3545325818a2b677","sha":"55ff8cfedf8c38e4c2a7943a3545325818a2b677","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/55ff8cfedf8c38e4c2a7943a3545325818a2b677"}],"sha":"f103e03b02dcc58bbbfb6d31cb67e4c5436c2862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/f103e03b02dcc58bbbfb6d31cb67e4c5436c2862"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/55ff8cfedf8c38e4c2a7943a3545325818a2b677/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:03:54Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:03:54Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Login hero: stop the connector beams at the card edge, not inside it\n\nThe beams read as drawn on top of the module cards on the deployed server while\nlooking correct on a developer''s machine. Two causes, neither of them z-index,\nwhich was already right:\n\n- Every beam was drawn to its card''s CENTRE, with a bright white terminal dot\n  painted there, so the line ran straight through the card.\n- The card was 86% transparent, and the only thing obscuring the part underneath\n  was backdrop-filter, which smears rather than hides and silently no-ops\n  wherever GPU compositing is unavailable (RDP and VDI sessions, hardware\n  acceleration off, driver blocklists). That is the dev/server difference.\n\nedgePoint() now walks the endpoint back from the card''s centre to the point where\nthe hub-to-centre ray leaves the card''s box, plus a 2px gap, and the terminal dot\nfollows it. A card overlapping the hub is clamped so the beam cannot flip past it.\nThe card surface is opaque, the beam layer drops below the hub, and it fades in\nonce the endpoints have been measured instead of appearing for one frame as five\nlines collapsed at the origin.\n\nVerified in the browser at 1440x900 with backdrop-filter force-disabled: the\nrendering is identical, so nothing now depends on that property.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"36e4221f1b623b797a20a506b7bb501b12638fe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/36e4221f1b623b797a20a506b7bb501b12638fe5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/55ff8cfedf8c38e4c2a7943a3545325818a2b677","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/55ff8cfedf8c38e4c2a7943a3545325818a2b677","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDU1ZmY4Y2ZlZGY4YzM4ZTRjMmE3OTQzYTM1NDUzMjU4MThhMmI2Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/17affab2b76eb1e4855e5290487e7f1c72ca07a8","sha":"17affab2b76eb1e4855e5290487e7f1c72ca07a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/17affab2b76eb1e4855e5290487e7f1c72ca07a8"}],"sha":"55ff8cfedf8c38e4c2a7943a3545325818a2b677","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/55ff8cfedf8c38e4c2a7943a3545325818a2b677"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/17affab2b76eb1e4855e5290487e7f1c72ca07a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:59:08Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:59:15Z","email":"udaychauhan246r@gmail.com","name":"Uday246r"},"message":"Tests: jest-dom matcher shims for the three remotes\n\nEach remote declares only the jest-dom matchers it actually uses, so a new\nassertion needs the shim extended before it typechecks. Adds\ntoHaveTextContent (lead), toBeEnabled (products) and a first shim for\ncustomer360.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3421b04a943ea1e0bba7fdf9f0628fd3c3a4a7bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/3421b04a943ea1e0bba7fdf9f0628fd3c3a4a7bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/17affab2b76eb1e4855e5290487e7f1c72ca07a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173535270?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r","id":173535270,"login":"uday246r","node_id":"U_kgDOClfwJg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/uday246r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/17affab2b76eb1e4855e5290487e7f1c72ca07a8","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDE3YWZmYWIyYjc2ZWIxZTQ4NTVlNTI5MDQ4N2U3ZjFjNzJjYTA3YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/ec7eeb590d265bd7227166edad0fdd40cb701eef","sha":"ec7eeb590d265bd7227166edad0fdd40cb701eef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/ec7eeb590d265bd7227166edad0fdd40cb701eef"}],"sha":"17affab2b76eb1e4855e5290487e7f1c72ca07a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/17affab2b76eb1e4855e5290487e7f1c72ca07a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/ec7eeb590d265bd7227166edad0fdd40cb701eef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:20:56Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:20:56Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Fix broken detail drawers, overflowing tables and unstyled UI before go-live\n\n- Audit \"Activity details\" drawer (user Audit Log tab and System Audit Trail) and the\n  Approval Center request drawer were built on SettingsDrawer.module.css classes that a\n  later redesign removed: the header rendered as a squashed column with invisible white\n  text. Both now use the shared @omniconnect/ui Drawer and render through a portal.\n- Entrance animations kept `transform: translateY(0)` after finishing (fill-mode both),\n  which made the page the containing block for position:fixed overlays and clipped\n  drawers to the tab. Keyframes now end at `transform: none` (same look, no trap).\n- ResponsiveRows also checks the room the table actually has: when it would still\n  overflow, low- then high-priority columns move into the row expander, so row actions\n  (e.g. the Audit Log \"View\" button) are never scrolled out of sight.\n- Approval Center: on an Update, the fields that change are marked and summarised so a\n  checker sees the change at a glance; the reject reason label is tied to its field.\n- Audit drawer leads with the outcome and a one-sentence account of the event instead of\n  repeating time/actor/outcome across a summary and a synthetic timeline.\n- Styles for classes components used but never defined (approval avatars, unassigned\n  chip, modify diff, nested values, profile admin chip, role picker pieces).\n- Tests: change detection; two page tests set a token expiry (they were signed out\n  mid-test); two export tests resolve same-origin URLs against a base.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"53b02f0621261365778606434836476ad23a50a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/53b02f0621261365778606434836476ad23a50a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/ec7eeb590d265bd7227166edad0fdd40cb701eef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/ec7eeb590d265bd7227166edad0fdd40cb701eef","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGVjN2VlYjU5MGQyNjViZDcyMjcxNjZlZGFkMGZkZDQwY2I3MDFlZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/aa92e8af20db5a9487168ff911780c08829420a9","sha":"aa92e8af20db5a9487168ff911780c08829420a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/aa92e8af20db5a9487168ff911780c08829420a9"}],"sha":"ec7eeb590d265bd7227166edad0fdd40cb701eef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/ec7eeb590d265bd7227166edad0fdd40cb701eef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/aa92e8af20db5a9487168ff911780c08829420a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T04:16:10Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T04:16:10Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Run the platform on rootful Podman (Windows Server 2022 guide and scripts)\n\nThe deployment now targets Podman, as the company requires, while compose.yml\nand the scripts stay engine-neutral (Docker still works):\n\n- compose.yml: restart: always everywhere. Podman has no daemon; at boot\n  podman-restart.service starts only containers whose policy is exactly\n  \"always\" (checked in Podman 4.9.3''s unit file), so the previous\n  unless-stopped would have left the platform down after every reboot.\n- Health checks for the four services declared in compose.yml, not only in the\n  Dockerfiles: Podman''s default OCI build format drops HEALTHCHECK, and\n  depends_on/`up --wait` need them.\n- Fully qualified image names (docker.io/...); local images are\n  localhost/omniconnect/*.\n- lib.sh selects the engine (CONTAINER_ENGINE, default podman when installed)\n  and re-runs scripts with sudo under Podman, since a rootless podman sees an\n  empty store. New scripts/build-images.sh builds with the engine''s own builder\n  (podman build --format docker) instead of compose-through-the-socket.\n- nginx local-proxy mode also trusts loopback: Podman''s port forwarding may\n  present the local proxy as 127.0.0.1 rather than the network gateway.\n- Guide: Ubuntu 24.04 (Podman 4.9.3, docker-compose-v2 2.24.6 from Ubuntu''s\n  own archive as podman compose''s provider, podman.socket and\n  podman-restart.service enabled), sudo podman commands throughout, a check\n  that Audit Logs show visitors'' real IPs, and Podman troubleshooting rows.\n  Windows scripts default to Ubuntu-24.04 and query Podman as root.\n\nRe-verified with Docker on the workstation (the user chose not to install a\nWSL distribution here): build-images.sh, deploy.sh with the local database in\nlocal-proxy mode (18 smoke checks), restart=always and healthy on every\ncontainer, real-IP chain through a Caddy stand-in, shellcheck, nginx -t in\nboth modes, PowerShell parse/ASCII, compose config. Podman itself is first\nexercised on the server; the guide checks each Podman-specific point there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f528a4f6f998dad352c42597f996160d64137d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/5f528a4f6f998dad352c42597f996160d64137d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/aa92e8af20db5a9487168ff911780c08829420a9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/aa92e8af20db5a9487168ff911780c08829420a9","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGFhOTJlOGFmMjBkYjVhOTQ4NzE2OGZmOTExNzgwYzA4ODI5NDIwYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/17d5b1a9ae4103d6f13e70069a5cadb072ba16d1","sha":"17d5b1a9ae4103d6f13e70069a5cadb072ba16d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/17d5b1a9ae4103d6f13e70069a5cadb072ba16d1"}],"sha":"aa92e8af20db5a9487168ff911780c08829420a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/aa92e8af20db5a9487168ff911780c08829420a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/17d5b1a9ae4103d6f13e70069a5cadb072ba16d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T04:00:40Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T04:00:40Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Windows Server 2022 deployment: WSL2 + Docker, Caddy HTTPS edge, local PostgreSQL\n\nA step-by-step guide (docs/DEPLOY-WINDOWS-SERVER-2022.md) for deploying on a\nWindows Server 2022 machine reached over VPN and Remote Desktop, written for\nsomeone new to deployment, plus the tooling it uses:\n\n- deploy/windows/check-server.ps1 (pre-flight: OS build, admin, nested\n  virtualization, RAM/disk, outbound HTTPS, ports 80/443 incl. IIS),\n  setup-windows.ps1 (Caddy download with SHA-512 check, Caddyfile, Windows\n  service, firewall, boot keep-alive and nightly backup tasks), status.ps1.\n  ASCII only: Windows PowerShell 5.1 misreads anything else.\n- Caddy on Windows is the HTTPS edge instead of netsh portproxy: a TCP\n  port-forward would have hidden every visitor''s address, putting the whole\n  company in one 10-per-minute login bucket and recording the server''s own\n  address in the audit log. nginx now has edge modes (EDGE_PROXY):\n  local-proxy trusts X-Forwarded-For from the compose network and is\n  published on 127.0.0.1 only (PUBLIC_BIND); none is the previous behaviour.\n- scripts/init-env.sh generates every secret (RS256 pair, per-service keys,\n  catalogue and release-agent keys, DB password) into .env and env/*.env so\n  shared values cannot disagree; refuses to overwrite an installation.\n- PostgreSQL on the same machine (COMPOSE_PROFILES=localdb) now keeps its data\n  in a named volume (it had none), restarts with Docker, and deploy.sh starts\n  it before migrations. backup-db.sh / restore-db.sh (typed confirmation).\n\nRehearsed in Linux containers: init-env (all shared keys match, key pair\nvalid, refuses a second run), deploy.sh with localdb in local-proxy mode (18\nsmoke checks), a Caddy stand-in proving the audit records the address the\nedge saw and ignores a spoofed X-Forwarded-For, nginx unreachable from the\nLAN, data surviving down/up, and backup → delete → restore. check-server.ps1\nrun on Windows; all .ps1 files parse; shellcheck clean; nginx -t in both edge\nmodes. Not testable here: WSL2 on Server 2022 itself, the boot task, and Let''s\nEncrypt for the real domain — the guide checks each on the server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"daea19377a964dc0025f21ac0b9bf79dfaf44642","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/daea19377a964dc0025f21ac0b9bf79dfaf44642"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/17d5b1a9ae4103d6f13e70069a5cadb072ba16d1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/17d5b1a9ae4103d6f13e70069a5cadb072ba16d1","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDE3ZDViMWE5YWU0MTAzZDZmMTNlNzAwNjlhNWNhZGIwNzJiYTE2ZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/e85fc37cfc406b6f6fa4f4b50a3ef37c7a1f77e9","sha":"e85fc37cfc406b6f6fa4f4b50a3ef37c7a1f77e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e85fc37cfc406b6f6fa4f4b50a3ef37c7a1f77e9"}],"sha":"17d5b1a9ae4103d6f13e70069a5cadb072ba16d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/17d5b1a9ae4103d6f13e70069a5cadb072ba16d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e85fc37cfc406b6f6fa4f4b50a3ef37c7a1f77e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:01:10Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:01:10Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Incremental releases: rebuild only what changed since the last release\n\n- pnpm release --since <ref> works out which apps changed (a change to the\n  shared packages, lockfile, workspace/TS config or the release script counts\n  for all of them) and rebuilds only those; --reuse now also takes the\n  previous release''s .tar.gz (checked against its .sha256).\n- A rebuilt app whose version equals the reused release''s but whose content\n  differs fails the build (\"Bump version\"). Builds were verified byte-for-byte\n  reproducible (host and lead, two builds each), so the guard has no false\n  positives: a rebuild of unchanged code matched the previous release.\n- release.yml finds the previous v* tag, downloads that release''s artifact\n  and runs an incremental release; with no previous release it builds all.\n\nVerified locally: nothing changed → all reused; shared change → all rebuilt\nand identical; Lead changed without a bump → refused; bumped → only Lead\nrebuilt.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"38bd5798c2d33a22bdec76767d335f7d4a047ab1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/38bd5798c2d33a22bdec76767d335f7d4a047ab1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/e85fc37cfc406b6f6fa4f4b50a3ef37c7a1f77e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/e85fc37cfc406b6f6fa4f4b50a3ef37c7a1f77e9","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGU4NWZjMzdjZmM0MDZiNmY2ZmE0ZjRiNTBhM2VmMzdjN2ExZjc3ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/40331018c5fa73a560ebbc8a7507f0996e99cc73","sha":"40331018c5fa73a560ebbc8a7507f0996e99cc73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/40331018c5fa73a560ebbc8a7507f0996e99cc73"}],"sha":"e85fc37cfc406b6f6fa4f4b50a3ef37c7a1f77e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e85fc37cfc406b6f6fa4f4b50a3ef37c7a1f77e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/40331018c5fa73a560ebbc8a7507f0996e99cc73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:45:16Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:45:16Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Tests: a timeout budget that survives `pnpm -r test` running every package\n\nSuites that re-import their module graph per test (vi.resetModules, for a\nfresh request cache) took well under a second alone but crossed Vitest''s 5s\ndefault when every package ran in parallel — the first test timed out and its\npending request leaked into the next test''s call count. Found by the release\ngate (2 failures in about one parallel run in three); 20s budget, then five\nconsecutive parallel runs with no failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95ca526d16420430e279a30e3416b38837b99fae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/95ca526d16420430e279a30e3416b38837b99fae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/40331018c5fa73a560ebbc8a7507f0996e99cc73","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/40331018c5fa73a560ebbc8a7507f0996e99cc73","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDQwMzMxMDE4YzVmYTczYTU2MGViYmM4YTc1MDdmMDk5NmU5OWNjNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/15b9e7fe4d4afe971a985be01f4db8b7a81bb529","sha":"15b9e7fe4d4afe971a985be01f4db8b7a81bb529","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/15b9e7fe4d4afe971a985be01f4db8b7a81bb529"}],"sha":"40331018c5fa73a560ebbc8a7507f0996e99cc73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/40331018c5fa73a560ebbc8a7507f0996e99cc73"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/15b9e7fe4d4afe971a985be01f4db8b7a81bb529/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:23:32Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:23:32Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Docs: release runbook, ADR, and current deployment/setup guides\n\n- docs/RUNBOOK-RELEASE.md: the release model, versions, first-time server\n  setup, releasing, what open tabs see, promote/rollback, roll-forward-only\n  (this release: LeadService drops its Products table — dump first),\n  maintenance and bypass, GC, a workstation rehearsal, troubleshooting.\n- docs/adr/0001-release-by-pointer.md: why builds are versioned folders and\n  going live is a pointer move, and the alternatives rejected.\n- docs/DEPLOYMENT.md rewritten for the single-origin topology; the old\n  Vercel/Render setup is marked retired.\n- ADDING-A-REMOTE-APP, SETUP, CLAUDE.md and the frontend .env examples:\n  same-origin defaults, the dev proxy, versioned manifest paths, package.json\n  release metadata, host-bridge, Products registration and its catalogue key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee367dd4ed74e77a8fbe54a3068954183f33b1eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/ee367dd4ed74e77a8fbe54a3068954183f33b1eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/15b9e7fe4d4afe971a985be01f4db8b7a81bb529","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/15b9e7fe4d4afe971a985be01f4db8b7a81bb529","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDE1YjllN2ZlNGQ0YWZlOTcxYTk4NWJlMDFmNGRiOGI3YTgxYmI1Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/e8d6b3f0d30d90c41095456665f2d932c1d50f62","sha":"e8d6b3f0d30d90c41095456665f2d932c1d50f62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e8d6b3f0d30d90c41095456665f2d932c1d50f62"}],"sha":"15b9e7fe4d4afe971a985be01f4db8b7a81bb529","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/15b9e7fe4d4afe971a985be01f4db8b7a81bb529"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e8d6b3f0d30d90c41095456665f2d932c1d50f62/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:20:37Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:20:37Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"CI/CD: GitHub Actions for checks, immutable images, and a gated deploy\n\n- ci.yml (PRs and main): frontend lint/typecheck/test plus the real release\n  assembly with every guard; backend tests per service; image builds; deploy\n  config checks (compose with the example settings, nginx -t, shellcheck).\n- release.yml (tag or manual): images pushed to GHCR tagged by commit SHA, the\n  frontend artifact attached to the GitHub Release, then a deploy job on the\n  \"production\" environment — its required reviewers are the human approval —\n  that ships deploy/ (never the server''s secrets) and runs deploy.sh.\n- deploy.sh: mapfile and an exit function, per shellcheck.\n\nValidated locally: both workflows parse, compose configs are valid with the\nexample settings, nginx -t passes, shellcheck is clean. Not yet run on GitHub:\nActions, the production environment and its secrets need the repository\nowner''s settings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d83c8824ddc7501903626502ef5e6aff7730db0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/8d83c8824ddc7501903626502ef5e6aff7730db0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/e8d6b3f0d30d90c41095456665f2d932c1d50f62","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/e8d6b3f0d30d90c41095456665f2d932c1d50f62","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGU4ZDZiM2YwZDMwZDkwYzQxMDk1NDU2NjY1ZjJkOTMyYzFkNTBmNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/1530ca66dd378260d4db8e76a52cd7081dee0627","sha":"1530ca66dd378260d4db8e76a52cd7081dee0627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/1530ca66dd378260d4db8e76a52cd7081dee0627"}],"sha":"e8d6b3f0d30d90c41095456665f2d932c1d50f62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/e8d6b3f0d30d90c41095456665f2d932c1d50f62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/1530ca66dd378260d4db8e76a52cd7081dee0627/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:18:52Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:18:52Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"deploy/: nginx single origin, compose stack, release scripts — rehearsed end to end\n\n- nginx (unprivileged) is the only public port: the live host''s index.html at /,\n  immutable /host/<v>/ and /modules/<key>/<v>/, the four services under their\n  path prefixes, SignalR on both hubs, internal and capability routes 404 from\n  outside, X-Forwarded-For overwritten, query strings kept out of access logs\n  (SignalR tokens), security headers on every response (CSP report-only), and\n  an internal listener (web-internal:8081) for AuthService''s manifest probes.\n- compose.yml: fixed private subnet trusted for forwarded headers, no backend\n  ports, cap_drop ALL, no-new-privileges, migrations off at startup, quiet EF\n  logging. Env templates per service; secrets are git-ignored.\n- `--migrate-only` on every service: the deploy runs migrations once, as a\n  single writer, and stops on failure instead of starting new code on an old\n  schema. AuthService''s image takes arguments like the others.\n- scripts: deploy.sh (verify → add folders, refusing changed content for an\n  existing version → migrate → up --wait → register → promote → atomic swap of\n  `current` → smoke test, undoing every moved pointer on failure), promote.sh,\n  rollback.sh (refuses to step back past a roll-forward-only release), gc.sh\n  (never removes what a recent release or a live/recent build needs),\n  smoke.sh (18 checks).\n- .gitattributes pins scripts and deploy files to LF.\n\nFound by the rehearsal and fixed: promoting a release opened a transaction\noutside the retrying execution strategy, which Npgsql refuses (500); release\nids collided for two releases from one commit.\n\nRehearsed on a workstation (compose.verify.yml): fresh install, idempotent\nre-deploy, Marketplace product → Lead form, a Lead-only release with no\ncontainer restarted and an open tab offered a reload, instant rollback,\nmaintenance bypass, spoofed X-Forwarded-For ignored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1010a13fdda775f06f19e11044c889c6bcd5ebfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/1010a13fdda775f06f19e11044c889c6bcd5ebfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/1530ca66dd378260d4db8e76a52cd7081dee0627","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/1530ca66dd378260d4db8e76a52cd7081dee0627","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDE1MzBjYTY2ZGQzNzgyNjBkNGRiOGU3NmE1MmNkNzA4MWRlZTA2Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/40a3e9de71e485b65161fff272144dae787a8e7f","sha":"40a3e9de71e485b65161fff272144dae787a8e7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/40a3e9de71e485b65161fff272144dae787a8e7f"}],"sha":"1530ca66dd378260d4db8e76a52cd7081dee0627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/1530ca66dd378260d4db8e76a52cd7081dee0627"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/40a3e9de71e485b65161fff272144dae787a8e7f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:56:28Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:56:28Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Release assembly: one artifact, every app in its own immutable folder\n\npnpm release builds the host and each remote separately, then lays them out\nas host/<version>/ and modules/<key>/<version>/ with release-manifest.json\n(versions, container names, requiredHostBridge, shared ranges, per-folder\nsha256, commit, an optional roll-forward-only reason) and a checksummed\ntarball. A deploy only adds folders; going live is a pointer move.\n\nGuards: API URLs forced same-origin and local .env files refused in CI (and\nreported locally); remote JS may not reference /assets/ absolutely; manifest\nversion must equal package version; the host must have built for its\nversioned base; every remote must accept the host''s bridge version. Remote\nstandalone index.html and mf-stats.json are not shipped. --only/--reuse\nrebuild just the apps that changed.\n\nThe host''s base comes from OMNI_HOST_BASE: pnpm passes a literal \"--\" to the\nscript, so a --base flag was silently ignored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cccd23f03494aff370a008f6f64d29fea4020741","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/cccd23f03494aff370a008f6f64d29fea4020741"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/40a3e9de71e485b65161fff272144dae787a8e7f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/40a3e9de71e485b65161fff272144dae787a8e7f","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDQwYTNlOWRlNzFlNDg1YjY1MTYxZmZmMjcyMTQ0ZGFlNzg3YThlN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/6d2230d4d4da2b65991663758782af6518d80627","sha":"6d2230d4d4da2b65991663758782af6518d80627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/6d2230d4d4da2b65991663758782af6518d80627"}],"sha":"40a3e9de71e485b65161fff272144dae787a8e7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/40a3e9de71e485b65161fff272144dae787a8e7f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/6d2230d4d4da2b65991663758782af6518d80627/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:52:02Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:52:02Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"@omniconnect/host-bridge: one versioned contract, checked before a remote mounts\n\n- New workspace package holding the host↔remote bridge contract (types,\n  HOST_BRIDGE_VERSION 1.1.0, the RemoteAppProps incl. subPath), a SemVer\n  checker that runs the same parity table as AuthService, and a typed fake for\n  tests. The host implements it (and now reports bridgeVersion); the three\n  remotes import it instead of their own copies, which had drifted (roleName\n  and permissions the host never sends).\n- Each remote''s package.json declares its version and\n  omniconnect.requiredHostBridge; federation-config writes both into\n  mf-manifest.json (metaData.omniconnect) and sets the manifest''s buildVersion\n  from it instead of the plugin''s constant \"1.0.0\". A remote without them\n  fails to build.\n- The host reads a remote''s manifest once per URL before mounting and refuses\n  an incompatible build with its own non-retrying error state.\n- Test fakes now come from the shared contract; drift no longer compiles.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d7b936698194c3ed143bc4633fdbf899c517f6f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/d7b936698194c3ed143bc4633fdbf899c517f6f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/6d2230d4d4da2b65991663758782af6518d80627","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/6d2230d4d4da2b65991663758782af6518d80627","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDZkMjIzMGQ0ZDRkYTJiNjU5OTE2NjM3NTg3ODJhZjY1MThkODA2Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/d7b856b1565318da8947de838e125979a5826ef4","sha":"d7b856b1565318da8947de838e125979a5826ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/d7b856b1565318da8947de838e125979a5826ef4"}],"sha":"6d2230d4d4da2b65991663758782af6518d80627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/6d2230d4d4da2b65991663758782af6518d80627"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/d7b856b1565318da8947de838e125979a5826ef4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:45:24Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:45:24Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Maintenance bypass as a capability, and no manifest URL for those without it\n\n- New host capability host.settings.applications:MaintenanceBypass (seeded\n  into existing databases too). Holders, and administrators, get the app in\n  state \"maintenance-bypass\" and can open it to verify a fix; everyone else\n  gets \"maintenance\".\n- A caller who cannot bypass is no longer sent the app''s manifest URL: there is\n  nothing for them to load, and it previously told every user where the build\n  under maintenance lived.\n- The sidebar marks maintenance for bypass holders as well.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1bba2b1053b88d4e26dc8acfe0c63f97040cca3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/1bba2b1053b88d4e26dc8acfe0c63f97040cca3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/d7b856b1565318da8947de838e125979a5826ef4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/d7b856b1565318da8947de838e125979a5826ef4","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGQ3Yjg1NmIxNTY1MzE4ZGE4OTQ3ZGU4MzhlMTI1OTc5YTU4MjZlZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/82359ff6709f5ad8925c4730f76ebacd20fe9203","sha":"82359ff6709f5ad8925c4730f76ebacd20fe9203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/82359ff6709f5ad8925c4730f76ebacd20fe9203"}],"sha":"d7b856b1565318da8947de838e125979a5826ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/d7b856b1565318da8947de838e125979a5826ef4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/82359ff6709f5ad8925c4730f76ebacd20fe9203/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:43:24Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:43:24Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Host runtime: pick up releases, stop endless retries, deep links\n\n- remoteLoader remembers each remote''s URL, not just its key: a promoted or\n  rolled-back build was ignored for the life of the tab. A new URL replaces the\n  registration if nothing loaded yet; if the old build is already running, the\n  page offers a reload rather than running two builds of one app.\n- A mounted remote keeps the build it started with, so a release never swaps\n  code under a half-filled form.\n- Fixes a dead remote being re-fetched every 2s forever: the error boundary was\n  remounted per attempt (key={attempt}), resetting its retry budget. Now one\n  load plus three automatic retries (the new test fails on the old code with\n  20 attempts a minute). A retry also re-reads the navigation tree.\n- The navigation tree is re-read when AuthService broadcasts a change and when\n  a tab returns to view after a minute.\n- maintenance-bypass state renders the app with a notice; a null manifest URL\n  renders the maintenance page.\n- /apps/:key/:page/* deep links pass the rest as subPath, and page-view audit\n  attributes them to their page instead of dropping them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"00be538eae969bb43389a884f3cf309ac7f7c861","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/00be538eae969bb43389a884f3cf309ac7f7c861"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/82359ff6709f5ad8925c4730f76ebacd20fe9203","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/82359ff6709f5ad8925c4730f76ebacd20fe9203","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDgyMzU5ZmY2NzA5ZjVhZDg5MjVjNDczMGY3NmViYWNkMjBmZTkyMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/c765d7177c19c175624e74da748cc2c3ccf67a6d","sha":"c765d7177c19c175624e74da748cc2c3ccf67a6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/c765d7177c19c175624e74da748cc2c3ccf67a6d"}],"sha":"82359ff6709f5ad8925c4730f76ebacd20fe9203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/82359ff6709f5ad8925c4730f76ebacd20fe9203"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/c765d7177c19c175624e74da748cc2c3ccf67a6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:37:37Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:37:37Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Release remotes by moving a pointer: versioned manifests and release history\n\nA remote build is published to its own immutable folder,\n/modules/<key>/<version>/, and going live is one row: RemoteApp.ManifestUrl\nmoves to that folder. The host is not rebuilt, no container restarts, no other\nremote is touched, and a tab with the old version open keeps loading it.\n\n- ManifestUrlPolicy: a manifest URL is /modules/<own key>/<version>/\n  mf-manifest.json; absolute http(s) URLs only in Development (or when\n  RemoteApps:AllowAbsoluteManifestUrls is set). Closes a Linux quirk where a\n  relative path passed the old \"absolute URL\" check as file://.\n- RemoteManifestClient resolves relative URLs against RemoteApps:InternalBaseUrl\n  and reads buildVersion and requiredHostBridge from the manifest.\n- RepointAsync: any change of manifest URL (admin edit or promotion) must\n  probe healthy and declare the same container; UpdateAsync skipped both.\n- ReleaseRecords table + /internal/releases (register, promote, rollback,\n  list), accepted only from the ReleaseAgent key. A remote the live host''s\n  bridge cannot run is refused, as is a host that would break a live remote;\n  a version cannot be republished with different content.\n- Navigation changes (promotion, re-point, maintenance) are broadcast to open\n  tabs; maintenance toggles previously never reached them.\n- SemVerRange with a parity table shared with the browser check.\n- Seeder permission sources configurable (RemoteApps:BuiltIn), products added;\n  ''host'' is reserved as an app key.\n- The Applications form accepts the versioned path shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b6d6055c8d3939e288bdeaf2a807036df292787","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/2b6d6055c8d3939e288bdeaf2a807036df292787"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/c765d7177c19c175624e74da748cc2c3ccf67a6d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/c765d7177c19c175624e74da748cc2c3ccf67a6d","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKGM3NjVkNzE3N2MxOWMxNzU2MjRlNzRkYTc0OGNjMmMzY2NmNjdhNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/973626ebe134273f008ba0668b0b3db595bcea0f","sha":"973626ebe134273f008ba0668b0b3db595bcea0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/973626ebe134273f008ba0668b0b3db595bcea0f"}],"sha":"c765d7177c19c175624e74da748cc2c3ccf67a6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/c765d7177c19c175624e74da748cc2c3ccf67a6d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/973626ebe134273f008ba0668b0b3db595bcea0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:09:17Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:09:17Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Frontends: same-origin APIs and a host dev proxy\n\n- Every API base URL now defaults to a path on the host''s own origin\n  (/api, /api/lead-service, /api/customer360-service, /api/products-service),\n  so one build runs in every environment and no localhost URL can be baked into\n  a production bundle. VITE_* overrides still work for a cross-origin backend.\n- The host dev server proxies backends and /modules/<key>/<version>/* to the\n  local remote build servers (dev-proxy.ts), mirroring production nginx; the\n  browser only ever talks to :5173.\n- Remotes build with base ''./'' and content-hashed assets, so a version can live\n  in any folder and be cached immutably; their servers bind to 127.0.0.1 and\n  preview sends no-store.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4b05325741f704c99b6b8bc0e7606a4d776a5e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/e4b05325741f704c99b6b8bc0e7606a4d776a5e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/973626ebe134273f008ba0668b0b3db595bcea0f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/973626ebe134273f008ba0668b0b3db595bcea0f","node_id":"C_kwDOUTfOFNoAKDk3MzYyNmViZTEzNDI3M2YwMDhiYTA2NjhiMGIzZGI1OTViY2VhMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commit/61adca0198c96ffa7ca94807b761ea985259cfaa","sha":"61adca0198c96ffa7ca94807b761ea985259cfaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/61adca0198c96ffa7ca94807b761ea985259cfaa"}],"sha":"973626ebe134273f008ba0668b0b3db595bcea0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/973626ebe134273f008ba0668b0b3db595bcea0f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/commits/61adca0198c96ffa7ca94807b761ea985259cfaa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:09:17Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:09:17Z","email":"manishmishra8970@gmail.com","name":"Ashok-2004"},"message":"Backends: one proxy edge, path bases, health and container images\n\nEvery service now starts with OmniConnect.Hosting''s UsePlatformEdge:\n- X-Forwarded-For is believed only from ForwardedHeaders:KnownNetworks (one\n  hop). Unset keeps the old trust-anyone behaviour for managed platforms, with\n  a startup warning outside Development; a malformed CIDR fails startup.\n- Hosting:PathBase, defaulting to /api/lead-service, /api/products-service and\n  /api/customer360-service (AuthService stays at the root for its /api/auth\n  cookie). Unprefixed paths keep working for server-to-server callers.\n\nAlso:\n- Database:ApplyMigrationsOnStartup on every service, so a deployment can run\n  migrations as one single-writer step.\n- Customer360Service gets /health and /health/live.\n- ProductsService gets a Dockerfile; every image listens on 8080 and has a\n  HEALTHCHECK that runs the service''s own binary (--healthcheck), as the aspnet\n  image has no curl.\n- .dockerignore excluded only Backend/.env; **/.env now keeps every service''s\n  local secrets out of the build context.\n- ProductsService no longer stores uploads; the stale Storage__UploadsPath\n  setting is removed from .env.example.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f851b85654415b266b7ce446cd0c9b469f926c8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/trees/f851b85654415b266b7ce446cd0c9b469f926c8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/uday246r/OmniConnectt/git/commits/61adca0198c96ffa7ca94807b761ea985259cfaa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169604595?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Ashok-2004","id":169604595,"login":"Ashok-2004","node_id":"U_kgDOChv18w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ashok-2004/orgs","received_e