ha":"ab3ffd956114e4ef56c143d27c367c29ea028ab1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/commits/ab3ffd956114e4ef56c143d27c367c29ea028ab1"}],"sha":"cf748fd454926c6ccc3f3cd8c1d68f6c122a6c2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/commits/cf748fd454926c6ccc3f3cd8c1d68f6c122a6c2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274412626?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/banupriyap2495/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/banupriyap2495/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/banupriyap2495/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/banupriyap2495/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/banupriyap2495","id":274412626,"login":"banupriyap2495","node_id":"U_kgDOEFs0Ug","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/banupriyap2495/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/banupriyap2495/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/banupriyap2495/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/banupriyap2495/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/banupriyap2495/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/banupriyap2495","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/commits/ab3ffd956114e4ef56c143d27c367c29ea028ab1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T05:21:52Z","email":"banupriya.palanivel@sai-tex.com","name":"banupriya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T05:21:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Confirm and fix CRM Sprint 2 specs against the running app (#2)\n\n* Fix tsconfig.json''s ignoreDeprecations value so tsc actually runs\n\nignoreDeprecations was set to \"6.0\", which the installed TypeScript\n5.9.3 rejects outright (TS5103: Invalid value for\n''--ignoreDeprecations'') before checking a single file — both `npx tsc`\nand `npm run typecheck` have been exiting with a config error, not a\nclean pass, since this was introduced. Corrected to \"5.0\" to match the\ninstalled compiler; `npm run typecheck` now runs a real check (clean,\nzero errors) instead of crashing at the config-parsing step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Confirm and fix CRM Sprint 2 specs against the running app\n\nAdds page objects, locators, test-case docs, and regression specs for\nthe eight remaining Sprint 2 CRM user stories (Log a Communication,\nGenerate/View/Notify Key Meeting Notes, Contacts tab in Customer\nDetails, Qualified Lead -> Prospect, View Logged Communications,\nScan&Create Customer/Contact, Biz Doc) — all previously best-guess\nscaffolding built from ClickUp text, now driven against a real running\nenvironment and corrected wherever the app''s actual behavior differed.\n\nNotable corrections made along the way: several \"Save\"/entry-point\nbutton labels, roles, and modal shapes didn''t match the ClickUp guess\n(e.g. Scan & Create lives inside a \"More actions\" dropdown, not its\nown button; linking a Contact goes through a combobox, not a dialog;\nseveral assumed fields/dropdowns don''t exist at all). Getting\nScan&Create''s real extraction tests running also required an\nenvironment fix: retargeting litellm''s vision-default binding onto a\nlocal Ollama model (docker/litellm/config.yaml in the flooros repo)\nand raising svc-crm''s extraction timeout, since the cloud binding had\nno working API key.\n\nGenuinely cross-module or environment-limited cases (email delivery,\nother Floor OS modules'' own UI, camera capture, missing seed data) are\nmarked test.fixme()/test.skip() with the specific confirmed reason\nrather than forced to a false pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix locator bugs in Contact List/Create Contact, extend smoke suite\n\n- contact-list.locators.ts: the linked-Customer cell is a `button`, not\n  a `link` — the old role-based locator never matched, timing out\n  TC:9/TC:10. TC:9/TC:10 also now create real Contact/Customer records\n  instead of relying on unconfirmed placeholder seed-data names.\n- create-contact.locators.ts: phoneInput''s getByLabel(''Phone'') matched\n  two elements (the field itself plus the adjacent \"Phone country\n  code\" combobox) — added exact: true.\n- smoke-recent.spec.ts: adds three smoke-level checks ported from their\n  regression spec''s own confirmed-passing TC:3 (Contacts tab delink,\n  Generate Key Meeting Notes AI generation, Log a Communication save).\n- .env.example: removed a real-looking corporate email/password from\n  CRM_USER_DEV/CRM_PASSWORD_DEV (this file ships with placeholders,\n  unlike gitignored .env).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Blank CRM_EXECUTIVE credentials in .env.example (PR review)\n\nfayaz.ahmad / \"Saitex#2026\" in this template file read as a real\nseeded account, not a placeholder (unlike alice/password used\nelsewhere in the same file) — flagged in PR #2 review. .env.example\nships with placeholders only; the real value belongs solely in each\ndeveloper''s own gitignored .env.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add CRM Sprint 4 smoke tests: Notify Internally, Lead Qualification, External Events\n\nAdds three new smoke checks confirmed directly against the running app\n(both local and dev):\n\n- Notify Internally about a Logged Communication: extends\n  log-communication.page.ts with notifyInternally()/\n  selectNotifyManager()/sendNotification(), mirroring the same dialog\n  shape already confirmed for Key Meeting Notes'' own Notify Internally.\n- Lead Qualification screen (Convert Lead -> Qualified Lead): new\n  lead-qualification.locators.ts/page.ts. Confirmed the ClickUp text''s\n  \"Convert bar shows all four chips\" premise doesn''t hold — Convert\n  enables after the FIRST saved department review, not all four.\n- Create External Event: new external-events.locators.ts/page.ts.\n  Confirmed the Feedback Form has three more required fields (\"What\n  went well?\", \"What could have been better?\", \"Attend next editions?\")\n  than the ClickUp text names as mandatory, and that Submit doesn''t\n  persist directly — a second \"Save event\" confirm step does.\n\nAlso fixes 4 pre-existing smoke tests that broke against dev\nspecifically: Create Customer''s Management section there now has a\nrequired \"Company\" combobox that didn''t exist when those tests were\nwritten. Added a defensive fillCompanyIfPresent() helper (only acts\nwhen the field exists, so local is unaffected) rather than assuming\neither environment''s shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add CRM Sprint 3 regression coverage: External Events List/Details, Alerts\n\nNew page objects (AlertsPage), extended ExternalEventsPage/locators for\nthe list and details/workspace screens, and 3 new regression specs (21\nTCs total) covering all Sprint 3 user stories, confirmed against a live\nrunning app:\n\n- 22-external-events-list.spec.ts (6/6 passing): status tabs, hidden\n  AI Relevance column sort, debounced search, and a genuine\n  business-logic discovery around compound \"Planning · Elapsed\" status\n  double-counting tab totals.\n- 23-external-event-details.spec.ts (7 TCs + 1 fixme): full Planning ->\n  To Attend/Attended lifecycle, Feedback Form/Leads content-gating\n  (not HTML-disabled, corrected from the original locator strategy),\n  registration link, and decline-with-reason validation/cancel flows.\n  Guards the environment''s fixed, non-replenishable Planning seed pool\n  via findFreshPlanningEvent().\n- 24-alert-detail-screen.spec.ts (5/7 passing, 3 fixme): Check/Uncheck\n  toggle, delete confirmation gate (never confirms — no Create Alert\n  path exists to replenish the fixed 6-alert pool), Official Source\n  link, and blank-recipient validation on the Internal share dialog.\n\nEach story''s test-case doc lives under test-cases/crm/, matching the\nexisting convention, with corrections and pool-consumption notes for\nwhoever runs this next.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address PR review: sanity/smoke scope, test data uniqueness, audit assertion\n\nResolves the three items left open from the last review round on this\nPR (the earlier credential concern was already fixed in a6a7fc8):\n\n- Moved the six capability-specific happy-path tests (Contacts tab,\n  Generate Key Meeting Notes, Log a Communication, Notify Internally,\n  Lead Qualification, External Events) from tests/smoke/crm/ to\n  tests/sanity/crm/, restoring the smoke suite to its original\n  Login/Create Customer/Create Contact scope per this repo''s own\n  smoke-vs-sanity precedent.\n- Fixed non-unique Contact-name test data in\n  17-contacts-tab-customer-details.spec.ts. Confirmed directly: Contact\n  Name (unlike Customer Name) rejects digits (\"Alphabets only\"\n  validation), so a plain Date.now() suffix doesn''t work here — added an\n  alphabetic-only base-26 suffix instead, and removed the .first()\n  workaround its non-uniqueness required.\n- Fixed the audit-stamping assertion gap in 13-log-a-communication.spec.ts\n  TC-3: confirmed the logged entry''s own Details screen genuinely shows a\n  Created On/By stamp, and added a real assertion for it. Also found and\n  fixed a genuine CSS text-transform timing race on these label blocks\n  (same identical screen render \"Created On\" in one run, \"CREATED ON\" in\n  another) — switched the new assertion, and the equivalent one on the\n  External Events Overview/System section, to case-insensitive matching.\n\nAlso includes three finished CRM Sprint 4 stories, verified independently\nof the above and not blocking on any in-progress work:\n\n- Create External Event [created by user manually] (28, 5/5 passing)\n- External Events [created by user manually] Details screen (29, 4/6\n  passing — 2 fixme''d for a confirmed app bug (Leads-tab Create Customer\n  locks a required Origin field) and an unreachable un-attended state for\n  manually-created events)\n- Notify Internally about a Logged Communication (25, 4/5 passing — 1\n  fixme''d, no audit-history feature exists on that screen)\n\nEach has a matching test-cases/crm/*.md doc.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add CRM Sprint 4 regression coverage: Lead Qualification, Customer Communication\n\nCompletes the Sprint 4 automation batch (Create External Event, External\nEvent Manual Details, and Notify Internally were pushed separately in\ne7cdeb0):\n\n- 26-lead-qualification-screen.spec.ts (6/6 passing): department review\n  save/edit-in-place, Manager-only lead conversion, the tab''s total\n  absence (not just locking) once CRM Stage moves past Lead, blank-field\n  validation, the zero-review disabled-Convert tooltip, and an\n  Executive-role restriction check via a genuinely separate seeded login.\n  Several corrections to the original ClickUp premise, notably: Convert\n  unlocks after ONE saved review (not four), the Manager picker isn''t\n  Department-filtered, and re-submitting the top form duplicates a row\n  instead of editing it (the row''s own \"Edit review\" button is the real\n  edit path).\n\n- 27-customer-communication-screen.spec.ts (6/8 passing, 2 fixme''d):\n  confirms the Communication tab is the same Logged Communications/Key\n  Meeting Notes/Emails trio from Sprint 2, now composed under one tri-tab\n  container with live badge counts, newest-first sorting, detail-view\n  navigation, and a real dirty-form navigation guard. TC:2/TC:5 (email\n  participant filtering) are fixme''d for a genuine environment blocker —\n  no Outlook integration is configured here, so the Emails sub-tab never\n  renders any list to check. TC:7 surfaces a real, confirmed timestamp-\n  formatting inconsistency (a Logged Communication''s own \"Date\" and\n  \"Created On\" fields use two different formats) — documented explicitly\n  rather than silently asserted as consistent.\n\nBoth verified against a live app run together with the rest of this\nSprint''s specs, plus the sanity and smoke suites; test-case docs added\nunder test-cases/crm/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"895c2d472fc9a2b00b8bb3c94b282136ef9c01ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/git/trees/895c2d472fc9a2b00b8bb3c94b282136ef9c01ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/git/commits/ab3ffd956114e4ef56c143d27c367c29ea028ab1","verification":{"payload":"tree 895c2d472fc9a2b00b8bb3c94b282136ef9c01ef\nparent 00c5bd01f0829b2b321635e1c79a3e3e489ad300\nauthor banupriya <banupriya.palanivel@sai-tex.com> 1790745712 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790745712 +0530\n\nConfirm and fix CRM Sprint 2 specs against the running app (#2)\n\n* Fix tsconfig.json''s ignoreDeprecations value so tsc actually runs\n\nignoreDeprecations was set to \"6.0\", which the installed TypeScript\n5.9.3 rejects outright (TS5103: Invalid value for\n''--ignoreDeprecations'') before checking a single file — both `npx tsc`\nand `npm run typecheck` have been exiting with a config error, not a\nclean pass, since this was introduced. Corrected to \"5.0\" to match the\ninstalled compiler; `npm run typecheck` now runs a real check (clean,\nzero errors) instead of crashing at the config-parsing step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Confirm and fix CRM Sprint 2 specs against the running app\n\nAdds page objects, locators, test-case docs, and regression specs for\nthe eight remaining Sprint 2 CRM user stories (Log a Communication,\nGenerate/View/Notify Key Meeting Notes, Contacts tab in Customer\nDetails, Qualified Lead -> Prospect, View Logged Communications,\nScan&Create Customer/Contact, Biz Doc) — all previously best-guess\nscaffolding built from ClickUp text, now driven against a real running\nenvironment and corrected wherever the app''s actual behavior differed.\n\nNotable corrections made along the way: several \"Save\"/entry-point\nbutton labels, roles, and modal shapes didn''t match the ClickUp guess\n(e.g. Scan & Create lives inside a \"More actions\" dropdown, not its\nown button; linking a Contact goes through a combobox, not a dialog;\nseveral assumed fields/dropdowns don''t exist at all). Getting\nScan&Create''s real extraction tests running also required an\nenvironment fix: retargeting litellm''s vision-default binding onto a\nlocal Ollama model (docker/litellm/config.yaml in the flooros repo)\nand raising svc-crm''s extraction timeout, since the cloud binding had\nno working API key.\n\nGenuinely cross-module or environment-limited cases (email delivery,\nother Floor OS modules'' own UI, camera capture, missing seed data) are\nmarked test.fixme()/test.skip() with the specific confirmed reason\nrather than forced to a false pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix locator bugs in Contact List/Create Contact, extend smoke suite\n\n- contact-list.locators.ts: the linked-Customer cell is a `button`, not\n  a `link` — the old role-based locator never matched, timing out\n  TC:9/TC:10. TC:9/TC:10 also now create real Contact/Customer records\n  instead of relying on unconfirmed placeholder seed-data names.\n- create-contact.locators.ts: phoneInput''s getByLabel(''Phone'') matched\n  two elements (the field itself plus the adjacent \"Phone country\n  code\" combobox) — added exact: true.\n- smoke-recent.spec.ts: adds three smoke-level checks ported from their\n  regression spec''s own confirmed-passing TC:3 (Contacts tab delink,\n  Generate Key Meeting Notes AI generation, Log a Communication save).\n- .env.example: removed a real-looking corporate email/password from\n  CRM_USER_DEV/CRM_PASSWORD_DEV (this file ships with placeholders,\n  unlike gitignored .env).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Blank CRM_EXECUTIVE credentials in .env.example (PR review)\n\nfayaz.ahmad / \"Saitex#2026\" in this template file read as a real\nseeded account, not a placeholder (unlike alice/password used\nelsewhere in the same file) — flagged in PR #2 review. .env.example\nships with placeholders only; the real value belongs solely in each\ndeveloper''s own gitignored .env.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add CRM Sprint 4 smoke tests: Notify Internally, Lead Qualification, External Events\n\nAdds three new smoke checks confirmed directly against the running app\n(both local and dev):\n\n- Notify Internally about a Logged Communication: extends\n  log-communication.page.ts with notifyInternally()/\n  selectNotifyManager()/sendNotification(), mirroring the same dialog\n  shape already confirmed for Key Meeting Notes'' own Notify Internally.\n- Lead Qualification screen (Convert Lead -> Qualified Lead): new\n  lead-qualification.locators.ts/page.ts. Confirmed the ClickUp text''s\n  \"Convert bar shows all four chips\" premise doesn''t hold — Convert\n  enables after the FIRST saved department review, not all four.\n- Create External Event: new external-events.locators.ts/page.ts.\n  Confirmed the Feedback Form has three more required fields (\"What\n  went well?\", \"What could have been better?\", \"Attend next editions?\")\n  than the ClickUp text names as mandatory, and that Submit doesn''t\n  persist directly — a second \"Save event\" confirm step does.\n\nAlso fixes 4 pre-existing smoke tests that broke against dev\nspecifically: Create Customer''s Management section there now has a\nrequired \"Company\" combobox that didn''t exist when those tests were\nwritten. Added a defensive fillCompanyIfPresent() helper (only acts\nwhen the field exists, so local is unaffected) rather than assuming\neither environment''s shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add CRM Sprint 3 regression coverage: External Events List/Details, Alerts\n\nNew page objects (AlertsPage), extended ExternalEventsPage/locators for\nthe list and details/workspace screens, and 3 new regression specs (21\nTCs total) covering all Sprint 3 user stories, confirmed against a live\nrunning app:\n\n- 22-external-events-list.spec.ts (6/6 passing): status tabs, hidden\n  AI Relevance column sort, debounced search, and a genuine\n  business-logic discovery around compound \"Planning · Elapsed\" status\n  double-counting tab totals.\n- 23-external-event-details.spec.ts (7 TCs + 1 fixme): full Planning ->\n  To Attend/Attended lifecycle, Feedback Form/Leads content-gating\n  (not HTML-disabled, corrected from the original locator strategy),\n  registration link, and decline-with-reason validation/cancel flows.\n  Guards the environment''s fixed, non-replenishable Planning seed pool\n  via findFreshPlanningEvent().\n- 24-alert-detail-screen.spec.ts (5/7 passing, 3 fixme): Check/Uncheck\n  toggle, delete confirmation gate (never confirms — no Create Alert\n  path exists to replenish the fixed 6-alert pool), Official Source\n  link, and blank-recipient validation on the Internal share dialog.\n\nEach story''s test-case doc lives under test-cases/crm/, matching the\nexisting convention, with corrections and pool-consumption notes for\nwhoever runs this next.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address PR review: sanity/smoke scope, test data uniqueness, audit assertion\n\nResolves the three items left open from the last review round on this\nPR (the earlier credential concern was already fixed in a6a7fc8):\n\n- Moved the six capability-specific happy-path tests (Contacts tab,\n  Generate Key Meeting Notes, Log a Communication, Notify Internally,\n  Lead Qualification, External Events) from tests/smoke/crm/ to\n  tests/sanity/crm/, restoring the smoke suite to its original\n  Login/Create Customer/Create Contact scope per this repo''s own\n  smoke-vs-sanity precedent.\n- Fixed non-unique Contact-name test data in\n  17-contacts-tab-customer-details.spec.ts. Confirmed directly: Contact\n  Name (unlike Customer Name) rejects digits (\"Alphabets only\"\n  validation), so a plain Date.now() suffix doesn''t work here — added an\n  alphabetic-only base-26 suffix instead, and removed the .first()\n  workaround its non-uniqueness required.\n- Fixed the audit-stamping assertion gap in 13-log-a-communication.spec.ts\n  TC-3: confirmed the logged entry''s own Details screen genuinely shows a\n  Created On/By stamp, and added a real assertion for it. Also found and\n  fixed a genuine CSS text-transform timing race on these label blocks\n  (same identical screen render \"Created On\" in one run, \"CREATED ON\" in\n  another) — switched the new assertion, and the equivalent one on the\n  External Events Overview/System section, to case-insensitive matching.\n\nAlso includes three finished CRM Sprint 4 stories, verified independently\nof the above and not blocking on any in-progress work:\n\n- Create External Event [created by user manually] (28, 5/5 passing)\n- External Events [created by user manually] Details screen (29, 4/6\n  passing — 2 fixme''d for a confirmed app bug (Leads-tab Create Customer\n  locks a required Origin field) and an unreachable un-attended state for\n  manually-created events)\n- Notify Internally about a Logged Communication (25, 4/5 passing — 1\n  fixme''d, no audit-history feature exists on that screen)\n\nEach has a matching test-cases/crm/*.md doc.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add CRM Sprint 4 regression coverage: Lead Qualification, Customer Communication\n\nCompletes the Sprint 4 automation batch (Create External Event, External\nEvent Manual Details, and Notify Internally were pushed separately in\ne7cdeb0):\n\n- 26-lead-qualification-screen.spec.ts (6/6 passing): department review\n  save/edit-in-place, Manager-only lead conversion, the tab''s total\n  absence (not just locking) once CRM Stage moves past Lead, blank-field\n  validation, the zero-review disabled-Convert tooltip, and an\n  Executive-role restriction check via a genuinely separate seeded login.\n  Several corrections to the original ClickUp premise, notably: Convert\n  unlocks after ONE saved review (not four), the Manager picker isn''t\n  Department-filtered, and re-submitting the top form duplicates a row\n  instead of editing it (the row''s own \"Edit review\" button is the real\n  edit path).\n\n- 27-customer-communication-screen.spec.ts (6/8 passing, 2 fixme''d):\n  confirms the Communication tab is the same Logged Communications/Key\n  Meeting Notes/Emails trio from Sprint 2, now composed under one tri-tab\n  container with live badge counts, newest-first sorting, detail-view\n  navigation, and a real dirty-form navigation guard. TC:2/TC:5 (email\n  participant filtering) are fixme''d for a genuine environment blocker —\n  no Outlook integration is configured here, so the Emails sub-tab never\n  renders any list to check. TC:7 surfaces a real, confirmed timestamp-\n  formatting inconsistency (a Logged Communication''s own \"Date\" and\n  \"Created On\" fields use two different formats) — documented explicitly\n  rather than silently asserted as consistent.\n\nBoth verified against a live app run together with the rest of this\nSprint''s specs, plus the sanity and smoke suites; test-case docs added\nunder test-cases/crm/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvJxxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+BwQAB6wx9tFVYbEcCcL9hR9BInH\n9miey5WU+Q2o4VRo5JNW6Sr+WZ4pgGIK8uj0/jcskhY3bzxSec1J5OQZ8Zs1s0zR\nr8HCt+on9l0d9B48FBpkJOTZZy12VJhiua994ghI3MMRibFG5Fs8WZpxGMOxgY8K\n7V4t2kMG4K8wlXFe8/VfX775mw8qh36HpLqBE9XYognzicsNhYcla3NTtoQ135GZ\neWDD2/cumncqriWRKYv35Vb++i+hgQiatwlrDIfr1hiHES2OWQSfR+dmW8QAmdd8\nhwUz3QeuVF3uqpmPCEGAi+Ha7+wUpEdJAJCov9mw6HzHr8drMSx47NB6G8db2kMg\ncACRgTj0jXGauZyTH0vy2xlS5AJ+TBoiPENVDw7tKtMqP4bk+fpH+15Ud32M9XvI\n1byEj5LzQw41TMfNvJCQsGXIKGVDkayYNlH7QEgcsKDUuLt99RlbmgHV2YLa0vtF\nu8esKXNhL53+DYO9vfT+uBFDan+0ejRq59EI8qe6vft6Wt3RxUMpuAQlHGuZHhhp\nV60Ol8J5qpol4FpLjT+zngy2ej3GceJxAsWOqb3cQNUnTUGS+RR3doPWYT5TDNik\ngLzObF9+6edBRoV4srKHe4FSQgovQDiqWilUQqg1OPIiUEuXZj2CHFUgSUmSIJVE\nqf4ZDcEYlgFMWXVxSq8G\n=KjTC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T05:21:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/commit/ab3ffd956114e4ef56c143d27c367c29ea028ab1","node_id":"C_kwDOUUduBdoAKGFiM2ZmZDk1NjExNGU0ZWY1NmMxNDNkMjdjMzY3YzI5ZWEwMjhhYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/commit/00c5bd01f0829b2b321635e1c79a3e3e489ad300","sha":"00c5bd01f0829b2b321635e1c79a3e3e489ad300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/commits/00c5bd01f0829b2b321635e1c79a3e3e489ad300"}],"sha":"ab3ffd956114e4ef56c143d27c367c29ea028ab1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/commits/ab3ffd956114e4ef56c143d27c367c29ea028ab1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/315803840?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RKsaitex/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RKsaitex/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RKsaitex/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RKsaitex/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RKsaitex","id":315803840,"login":"RKsaitex","node_id":"U_kgDOEtLIwA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RKsaitex/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RKsaitex/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RKsaitex/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RKsaitex/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RKsaitex/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RKsaitex","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/commits/00c5bd01f0829b2b321635e1c79a3e3e489ad300/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:53:26Z","email":"rohithkrishna.radhakrishnan@sai-tex.com","name":"RKsaitex"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:53:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add Master Data smoke coverage: Departments, Employees, Sites (#5)\n\n* Add Master Data Departments smoke coverage (Create Department)\n\nPage objects, locators, and fixture wiring for the top-level Master\nData module''s Department Master screen (/master-data/system-management/\ndepartments), plus one happy-path smoke test: create a department with\na single primary site. Confirmed live against dev before committing —\nDefault working calendar and at least one \"Operates at\" site row are\nboth required to save, and the Site/Role/Calendar comboboxes need\nexact-match locators (substring name collisions between them).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Start agent-notes/master-data-module.md with Departments findings\n\nFirst per-module notes file for Master Data, following this repo''s\nexisting pattern for Planning/Techpack. Captures what was confirmed\nlive while building Create Department smoke coverage: two\nnot-obviously-required fields, a combobox exact-match locator trap,\nand the real success toast text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add Master Data Employees smoke coverage (Create Employee)\n\nPage objects, locators, and fixture wiring for the top-level Master\nData module''s Employees screen (/master-data/system-management/\nemployees), plus one happy-path smoke test: create an employee with\nFull Name + Department. Confirmed live against dev before committing.\n\nDepartment is a real, live-sourced, searchable combobox (not a plain\nselect) — clicking it opens a dialog with department options as plain\nbuttons, not role=listbox/option, so a role=option locator hangs\nforever instead of failing fast. Success toast text differs subtly\nfrom Departments'' own (\"Employee created\" vs \"Department created.\").\nNotes captured in agent-notes/master-data-module.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add Master Data Sites smoke coverage (Create Site)\n\nPage objects, locators, and fixture wiring for the top-level Master\nData module''s Site Master screen (/master-data/system-management/\nsites), plus one happy-path smoke test: create a site with just code\n+ name. Confirmed live against dev before committing.\n\nCountry and Timezone look required on the form but aren''t enforced —\nmatches this repo''s own historical TC-CS-07 finding, already filed as\na bug, so the smoke test deliberately doesn''t set them. No legal-entity\nrow is required either (unlike Departments, which hard-blocks save\nwithout at least one site row). Notes captured in\nagent-notes/master-data-module.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Master Data landing view''s heading locator and load timeout\n\nMasterDataLocators/MasterDataPage were still the untouched TODO stub\n— never actually run before since MASTER_DATA credentials didn''t\nexist in .env until this session. Confirmed live via the failing\n\"loads after shell login\" smoke test (failed 3 of 4 runs): two real\nbugs, not flakiness.\n\n- The stub guessed an <h1>; the real landing view''s heading is an\n  <h2> (\"Master Data\" / \"Select a master from the left navigation.\")\n  — a level-1 heading never appears on this page, so the old locator\n  could never have matched regardless of timing.\n- Even after fixing that, the view can still sit on \"Loading Master\n  Data...\" past the default 15s assertion timeout on a slow dev\n  moment, same shape as this app''s other slow module bundles. Bumped\n  to 60s, matching the other Master Data list pages built this\n  session.\n\nConfirmed with 3 isolated runs plus 2 full-suite runs, all clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add missing Allure tags; fix agent-notes/README.md dangling references\n\nAddresses review feedback on PR #5:\n\n- master-data.smoke.spec.ts had zero allure.epic()/feature()/owner()\n  calls, same gap already fixed on Planning''s and Techpack''s smoke\n  suites after their own reviews. Adds a beforeEach matching that\n  pattern (epic ''Master Data'', feature ''Smoke'', owner ''Master Data QA'').\n- agent-notes/README.md described progress.md, environment-notes.md,\n  and techpack-module.md as existing files, but none of those are part\n  of this branch (they''re mixed-scope, covering Planning/Techpack work\n  too, and deliberately weren''t committed here). Trimmed the README to\n  describe only what this branch actually ships (itself +\n  master-data-module.md), with a note that sibling branches may add\n  the others once they land.\n\nConfirmed lint and the full smoke suite (5/5) still pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Rohithkrishna R <rk@Rohithkrishnas-MacBook-Air.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"870c4fa0cf8ce8794327008c314a36c9967826af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/git/trees/870c4fa0cf8ce8794327008c314a36c9967826af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/git/commits/00c5bd01f0829b2b321635e1c79a3e3e489ad300","verification":{"payload":"tree 870c4fa0cf8ce8794327008c314a36c9967826af\nparent 2ff2e9d4384e0909da7a943facce74bf3050fdeb\nauthor RKsaitex <rohithkrishna.radhakrishnan@sai-tex.com> 1790672006 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790672006 +0530\n\nAdd Master Data smoke coverage: Departments, Employees, Sites (#5)\n\n* Add Master Data Departments smoke coverage (Create Department)\n\nPage objects, locators, and fixture wiring for the top-level Master\nData module''s Department Master screen (/master-data/system-management/\ndepartments), plus one happy-path smoke test: create a department with\na single primary site. Confirmed live against dev before committing —\nDefault working calendar and at least one \"Operates at\" site row are\nboth required to save, and the Site/Role/Calendar comboboxes need\nexact-match locators (substring name collisions between them).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Start agent-notes/master-data-module.md with Departments findings\n\nFirst per-module notes file for Master Data, following this repo''s\nexisting pattern for Planning/Techpack. Captures what was confirmed\nlive while building Create Department smoke coverage: two\nnot-obviously-required fields, a combobox exact-match locator trap,\nand the real success toast text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add Master Data Employees smoke coverage (Create Employee)\n\nPage objects, locators, and fixture wiring for the top-level Master\nData module''s Employees screen (/master-data/system-management/\nemployees), plus one happy-path smoke test: create an employee with\nFull Name + Department. Confirmed live against dev before committing.\n\nDepartment is a real, live-sourced, searchable combobox (not a plain\nselect) — clicking it opens a dialog with department options as plain\nbuttons, not role=listbox/option, so a role=option locator hangs\nforever instead of failing fast. Success toast text differs subtly\nfrom Departments'' own (\"Employee created\" vs \"Department created.\").\nNotes captured in agent-notes/master-data-module.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add Master Data Sites smoke coverage (Create Site)\n\nPage objects, locators, and fixture wiring for the top-level Master\nData module''s Site Master screen (/master-data/system-management/\nsites), plus one happy-path smoke test: create a site with just code\n+ name. Confirmed live against dev before committing.\n\nCountry and Timezone look required on the form but aren''t enforced —\nmatches this repo''s own historical TC-CS-07 finding, already filed as\na bug, so the smoke test deliberately doesn''t set them. No legal-entity\nrow is required either (unlike Departments, which hard-blocks save\nwithout at least one site row). Notes captured in\nagent-notes/master-data-module.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix Master Data landing view''s heading locator and load timeout\n\nMasterDataLocators/MasterDataPage were still the untouched TODO stub\n— never actually run before since MASTER_DATA credentials didn''t\nexist in .env until this session. Confirmed live via the failing\n\"loads after shell login\" smoke test (failed 3 of 4 runs): two real\nbugs, not flakiness.\n\n- The stub guessed an <h1>; the real landing view''s heading is an\n  <h2> (\"Master Data\" / \"Select a master from the left navigation.\")\n  — a level-1 heading never appears on this page, so the old locator\n  could never have matched regardless of timing.\n- Even after fixing that, the view can still sit on \"Loading Master\n  Data...\" past the default 15s assertion timeout on a slow dev\n  moment, same shape as this app''s other slow module bundles. Bumped\n  to 60s, matching the other Master Data list pages built this\n  session.\n\nConfirmed with 3 isolated runs plus 2 full-suite runs, all clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add missing Allure tags; fix agent-notes/README.md dangling references\n\nAddresses review feedback on PR #5:\n\n- master-data.smoke.spec.ts had zero allure.epic()/feature()/owner()\n  calls, same gap already fixed on Planning''s and Techpack''s smoke\n  suites after their own reviews. Adds a beforeEach matching that\n  pattern (epic ''Master Data'', feature ''Smoke'', owner ''Master Data QA'').\n- agent-notes/README.md described progress.md, environment-notes.md,\n  and techpack-module.md as existing files, but none of those are part\n  of this branch (they''re mixed-scope, covering Planning/Techpack work\n  too, and deliberately weren''t committed here). Trimmed the README to\n  describe only what this branch actually ships (itself +\n  master-data-module.md), with a note that sibling branches may add\n  the others once they land.\n\nConfirmed lint and the full smoke suite (5/5) still pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Rohithkrishna R <rk@Rohithkrishnas-MacBook-Air.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu3yGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuKIQAKedoRBuPrPWU9LEJEgp5oZH\nl5HlPdFDUZYX4MA766iBjUc8KhapeuiuzX1rXgxjh8kWgowNY2r/CIOcSQJspOX8\noUMfleex2zEiAeujGxiPovk1RPfYaa/6t15XXBxAwJTVlRZPQf5e8fB8VoM