janQAlead/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sathishnagarajanQAlead/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sathishnagarajanQAlead/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sathishnagarajanQAlead","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/commits/f0f5cfe02a371200de853d37a28afe60eaafed4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:10:37Z","email":"sathish.nagarajan@sai-tex.com","name":"Sathish Nagarajan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:10:37Z","email":"sathish.nagarajan@sai-tex.com","name":"Sathish Nagarajan"},"message":"Fix gotoAuthenticated() to not assume the sign-in gate always reappears\n\nA second gotoAuthenticated() call within an already-authenticated tab\n(e.g. a smoke test that navigates twice) can land straight in the app\nwith no gate at all -- confirmed via a headed dev run where a 60s wait\nfor \"Sign in\" timed out while the page snapshot showed the fully\nauthenticated shell already loaded. The gate-always-shows assumption\nfrom the last fix wasn''t quite right. Now races the gate against the\nshell''s Notifications button (present on every authenticated page) and\nacts on whichever appears first, only failing if neither does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4e67b8b6e6aca2dee6950d3ed5e89770808dfa04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/git/trees/4e67b8b6e6aca2dee6950d3ed5e89770808dfa04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saitex-ai/Floor-OS-Test-Automation/git/commits/f0f5cfe02a371200de853d37a28afe60eaafed4b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/321365753?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sathishnagarajanQAlead/events{/privacy}","followers_url"