uthor":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:38:17Z","email":"jojou112@gmail.com","name":"Roman Suleymanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:38:17Z","email":"jojou112@gmail.com","name":"Roman Suleymanov"},"message":"feat(backend): groups — party/raid rights model (B3, #15)\n\nSix group routes replace the 501 stubs: create, edit info, add/remove\nmembers, member rights, ownership transfer — implemented identically in\nMem and PG stores (zero migrations; role+rights columns predate in 0002).\n\n- Owner implicit superuser; member rows carry five boolean rights\n- Contacts-only invites, gated on the inviter''s outgoing contacts\n- Owner leaves only via atomic transferOwnership (demote+promote in tx)\n- Existence privacy: strangers get 404 on every group route, and the\n  actor gate always runs before target resolution — a 403 would leak\n  \"chat exists / target is a member / target is the owner\"\n- Pin/delete in groups honor pinMessages/deleteMessages; pin, edit and\n  delete now require membership at the store level (was handler-only)\n- chat.new to newly-added members, chat.updated on every change —\n  including the removed member via the pre-removal roster\n\nTests: 6 API contract tests + PG roundtrip with a stranger-privacy\ntable across all group ops; live smoke over the full lifecycle.\n\nJournal 08 documents the design and the review findings (check-order\nleaks, LEFT JOIN NULL trap, Mem/PG parity surface).\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"84ead70b69fbb74059fd854edf740cd971aef30e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jojouHZ/openglass/git/trees/84ead70b69fbb74059fd854edf740cd971aef30e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jojouHZ/openglass/git/commits/b730798dc892b1bbab841cf9ce54c4ede9b75fdb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.gith