e5fa41cd5b7ef0777a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/e6c66aaa06bc09d2f493c5e5fa41cd5b7ef0777a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/b932cb40542e0b8fc2f1ded0dd05c50f77a34fed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:53:28Z","email":"smonier@Jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:53:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: put the page drawer back against the right edge (#29)\n\nThe page drawer opens in the top left corner, at the height of its own\ncontent, instead of as a full-height panel against the right edge the\nway page-audit''s does.\n\n## Where it came from\n\n1.4.0 changed nothing in the drawer or its stylesheet. The regression is\nolder: **#14 turned the drawer from `<aside className={styles.drawer}>`\ninto `<dialog className={styles.drawer}>` and kept the stylesheet\nexactly as it was.** That stylesheet was written for a `<div>`-like\nelement, and `<dialog>` comes with a UA rule it never countered:\n\n```css\ndialog {\n  inset-inline-start: 0;   /* = left: 0 in LTR */\n  height: fit-content;\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nThe rule already cleared `padding`, `margin`, `border`, `color` and\n`max-height`. It did not clear `left` or `height`, and those two are the\nones that decide where the panel lands:\n\n- the box has `left: 0` (UA), `right: 0` and `width: 820px`. An\nabsolutely positioned box given both insets **and** a width is\nover-constrained, so in LTR the used value of `right` is ignored. The\npanel goes to x=0.\n- the same box has `top: 0`, `bottom: 0` and `height: fit-content` (UA).\nOver-constrained again, so `bottom` is ignored. The panel is as tall as\nits text.\n\nTogether: top left corner, content-sized. Exactly what is reported.\n\n## The fix\n\nTwo properties back to `auto`, so `right` and `bottom` are the ones that\ndecide:\n\n```css\nleft: auto;\nheight: auto;\n```\n\nNo change to the markup, so the accessibility work in #14 is untouched:\nit stays a real `<dialog>`, keeps the implicit role, the Escape handler\nand the focus trap.\n\n## Measured, not assumed\n\nDeployed to a live jContent on the luxe site, 1440x900 viewport, reading\nthe element''s own box:\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `getComputedStyle().left` | `0px` | `620px` |\n| rendered x | 0 | 620 |\n| right edge | 821 | **1440**, flush |\n| height | 189 | **900**, full |\n\nThe `height` half was found the same way. After fixing `left` the panel\nwas flush right but only 189px tall, and setting `height: auto` on the\nlive element took it to 900px, which is what sent me back for the second\nUA property rather than shipping half a fix.\n\n## Worth knowing for the next one\n\nAny element we style from a CSS module is styled as if the UA gave it\nnothing. That holds for `div`, `aside` and `section`, and it does not\nhold for `dialog`, which is the only element in this module with a UA\nrule that positions and sizes it. If a later change moves another panel\nto `<dialog>`, the same four properties (`left`, `right`, `height`,\n`width`) need stating explicitly rather than half of them.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3fadad7a8ec37cbf1332bef3cbc15f4ec39e50f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/d3fadad7a8ec37cbf1332bef3cbc15f4ec39e50f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/b932cb40542e0b8fc2f1ded0dd05c50f77a34fed","verification":{"payload":"tree d3fadad7a8ec37cbf1332bef3cbc15f4ec39e50f\nparent 7a4e896bf3b634d6059cbabba6d435a7fd732a5e\nauthor Stephane Monier <smonier@Jahia.com> 1790862808 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790862808 +0200\n\nfix: put the page drawer back against the right edge (#29)\n\nThe page drawer opens in the top left corner, at the height of its own\ncontent, instead of as a full-height panel against the right edge the\nway page-audit''s does.\n\n## Where it came from\n\n1.4.0 changed nothing in the drawer or its stylesheet. The regression is\nolder: **#14 turned the drawer from `<aside className={styles.drawer}>`\ninto `<dialog className={styles.drawer}>` and kept the stylesheet\nexactly as it was.** That stylesheet was written for a `<div>`-like\nelement, and `<dialog>` comes with a UA rule it never countered:\n\n```css\ndialog {\n  inset-inline-start: 0;   /* = left: 0 in LTR */\n  height: fit-content;\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nThe rule already cleared `padding`, `margin`, `border`, `color` and\n`max-height`. It did not clear `left` or `height`, and those two are the\nones that decide where the panel lands:\n\n- the box has `left: 0` (UA), `right: 0` and `width: 820px`. An\nabsolutely positioned box given both insets **and** a width is\nover-constrained, so in LTR the used value of `right` is ignored. The\npanel goes to x=0.\n- the same box has `top: 0`, `bottom: 0` and `height: fit-content` (UA).\nOver-constrained again, so `bottom` is ignored. The panel is as tall as\nits text.\n\nTogether: top left corner, content-sized. Exactly what is reported.\n\n## The fix\n\nTwo properties back to `auto`, so `right` and `bottom` are the ones that\ndecide:\n\n```css\nleft: auto;\nheight: auto;\n```\n\nNo change to the markup, so the accessibility work in #14 is untouched:\nit stays a real `<dialog>`, keeps the implicit role, the Escape handler\nand the focus trap.\n\n## Measured, not assumed\n\nDeployed to a live jContent on the luxe site, 1440x900 viewport, reading\nthe element''s own box:\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `getComputedStyle().left` | `0px` | `620px` |\n| rendered x | 0 | 620 |\n| right edge | 821 | **1440**, flush |\n| height | 189 | **900**, full |\n\nThe `height` half was found the same way. After fixing `left` the panel\nwas flush right but only 189px tall, and setting `height: auto` on the\nlive element took it to 900px, which is what sent me back for the second\nUA property rather than shipping half a fix.\n\n## Worth knowing for the next one\n\nAny element we style from a CSS module is styled as if the UA gave it\nnothing. That holds for `div`, `aside` and `section`, and it does not\nhold for `dialog`, which is the only element in this module with a UA\nrule that positions and sizes it. If a later change moves another panel\nto `<dialog>`, the same four properties (`left`, `right`, `height`,\n`width`) need stating explicitly rather than half of them.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvmXYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQukQADF73eDBic5xyWdkl2lEu/81\nR0+1Kl+3OzugQhAQSeGDXdPailxi5vvIvmCuKuXMfuiz1VB1vmsR19jJftyLbR37\nWC/CoSX9//LhyE9kpmwdN6/JPEp48MMian6flIj1foB52NVs4VVf8b5WnTnDCo7v\nWgUbYFuZ72d3D6IGHnnCz0kyQKdprNqk5+BXwoI8+zZBvpmR9acmTAgYFmdV5wdx\nHLJkCOT8aeKMoKt1q7eeUBwaukqhykRODR9rgRdhMErUhE/JYPyvQc5cRMXK0OnV\nxco3VqgyVca2uyKFbvzvH5fnTYtJAXF6qfPmaCxDDPIr4rmpoPntb2+Bk4qfIG9W\n+pt3SuDwF7VxsgozpSJGN/gV3Yg5fCjEMBssEfUgIXyatw1808XzB2iNKyNKTVoT\n5wyKdk0uGvL0xrRtrR0TkyfBS5UFrJL4C2sBsp10ViRfWoe2+gexMkeX3aaRi1Oc\nB3kI08ah+wwSdqRWxwrAKcjbSuuXijV+Rns+u9Nped/0DVts+wHKGVHqBPaN/3hY\n86QUEgICUe9Z2XbFiS/NBvvmJcyuQ5omAdaQs6WxS0N2eN2iREspPdexSX/bJ83i\n4RVbtpvtvoJeTDnLkHD8ZzSxnkD4fEyZppN8xDQvqRzIuBcsZyfPH3x6sYtjd/vW\n5c3vqqNYJQbNc14YnfpH\n=8BcD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T13:53:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/b932cb40542e0b8fc2f1ded0dd05c50f77a34fed","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGI5MzJjYjQwNTQyZTBiOGZjMmYxZGVkMGRkMDVjNTBmNzdhMzRmZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/7a4e896bf3b634d6059cbabba6d435a7fd732a5e","sha":"7a4e896bf3b634d6059cbabba6d435a7fd732a5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/7a4e896bf3b634d6059cbabba6d435a7fd732a5e"}],"sha":"b932cb40542e0b8fc2f1ded0dd05c50f77a34fed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/b932cb40542e0b8fc2f1ded0dd05c50f77a34fed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/7a4e896bf3b634d6059cbabba6d435a7fd732a5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:37:21Z","email":"smonier@Jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:37:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: let a changelog fragment be named after its change (#30)\n\nThe fragment guide asks for a **random** file name. Nobody follows it,\nincluding the releases that shipped:\n\n| Named after the change | Random |\n|---|---|\n| `robots-dollar-anchor.md`, `unused-imports.md`,\n`accessibility-aaa.md`, `servlet-base-class.md`, `fetch-guard-sink.md`,\nand 14 more | `tan-owls-invent.md`, `9724ba58e5732e3f.md` |\n\nNineteen of twenty-one. The two random ones look like `chachalog`''s own\ngenerator rather than a deliberate choice.\n\nA blind review of #29 picked this up: it read the guide, saw\n`drawer-position.md`, and reported the descriptive name as a deviation.\nIt was right about the rule and the rule is wrong about the repository,\nwhich is the kind of convention that quietly costs a reviewer''s\nattention on every pull request that touches a fragment.\n\nThe constraint the rule was reaching for is real but narrower: two pull\nrequests in flight must not add the same path. A name that describes its\nown change satisfies that about as well as a random string, and reads\nbetter in a diff and in `git log`. This states both as allowed and says\nwhy, rather than mandating the one nobody picked.\n\nNo behaviour changes. `chachalog` never reads the file name: the release\npull request consumes the fragment and deletes it, and only the text\ninside reaches `CHANGELOG.md`.","tree":{"sha":"9a8dbc04a6b5dec295e07860aa1d735e4551696a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/9a8dbc04a6b5dec295e07860aa1d735e4551696a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/7a4e896bf3b634d6059cbabba6d435a7fd732a5e","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a8dbc04a6b5dec295e07860aa1d735e4551696a\nparent 67b2090802c76af97e6e76e584e8d04b28a1435b\nauthor Stephane Monier <smonier@Jahia.com> 1790861841 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790861841 +0200\n\ndocs: let a changelog fragment be named after its change (#30)\n\nThe fragment guide asks for a **random** file name. Nobody follows it,\nincluding the releases that shipped:\n\n| Named after the change | Random |\n|---|---|\n| `robots-dollar-anchor.md`, `unused-imports.md`,\n`accessibility-aaa.md`, `servlet-base-class.md`, `fetch-guard-sink.md`,\nand 14 more | `tan-owls-invent.md`, `9724ba58e5732e3f.md` |\n\nNineteen of twenty-one. The two random ones look like `chachalog`''s own\ngenerator rather than a deliberate choice.\n\nA blind review of #29 picked this up: it read the guide, saw\n`drawer-position.md`, and reported the descriptive name as a deviation.\nIt was right about the rule and the rule is wrong about the repository,\nwhich is the kind of convention that quietly costs a reviewer''s\nattention on every pull request that touches a fragment.\n\nThe constraint the rule was reaching for is real but narrower: two pull\nrequests in flight must not add the same path. A name that describes its\nown change satisfies that about as well as a random string, and reads\nbetter in a diff and in `git log`. This states both as allowed and says\nwhy, rather than mandating the one nobody picked.\n\nNo behaviour changes. `chachalog` never reads the file name: the release\npull request consumes the fragment and deletes it, and only the text\ninside reaches `CHANGELOG.md`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvmIRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuU8QADZ3W6NhlfH3kkNDP6HzXweL\nGDNQR7RZOBoQSDS/6CrY2ZYsVqmVhbXcfpkUNQbLs1F0ppp0Idhbb7wuolqOp2AC\ndrCCty3Jlsjlcn82g24dOqEYerrR/Vb5SegGFfScBnYpsHiw2q9grjAncaK8xYoP\nSUwc2ZYhvK0ABTrW+yjK+m3L88xYyZcrRg0ZgG1fVkVnCa4WzMa0S/0/pFfahais\n81VpUvcEpQE3yBdU6Ut/K6anWHrOXt40ZkxXadWMtMkXD7fQ9cwZkBWFZmmsQN2H\nEod6QIeeNZtrsV+Bu9cawVJQDI0+bYViYsM/VC1QiWO8HScn8L0ATp7r2hyIu6Rp\nM8cRncjWVaLgi9AK0T/Su1rMmBQV+2KNBL1IMchBM7CywcWA7BtTXwmbS/fOHz6/\nNdUr3QSLpJUKCquXTyb9+a5AFcR3noPzL4o9F9Km7tDRNXH0ddEs3v2XT6xfvjXT\nz4LaCEaBaxq0g/RFP9RSohmmbPJrSPqOkbK9OpE7uD4oyoezhqEbP60l4eqIBF95\n8szpbiXBS/mNbEdFjkz8+sgoD0qEDNb4F9JvU9h71LoAFmB/FvAiwnfq8qTKca4b\nVEokIW/4R3Jod2bDsTurinXJMC4C//jsru6U/mVZnS5EblsMP3dOCs18WfMMMbFj\nZ1dseTqd4yT0K035Jkaq\n=ECHX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T13:37:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/user