chable|Blocked/` is now `/\\d+ of \\d+ checks passed/`. Both\nstrings are in `en.json`, but neither reaches the page once a check has\nrun, so that assertion spent its whole 180s budget against a drawer that\nhad finished and was showing its results. The score line is computed\nfrom the same crawler fetches and proves the same thing — that a result\nrendered rather than a spinner. Flagging it because weakening an\nassertion quietly would be the wrong way to get green.\n\n**The contributor test** now asserts it can reach the SEO section\n*before* asserting the entry is absent from it. `tests/README.md`\nflagged that a red there had two opposite meanings; measured, a\ncontributor is offered Page models and SEO but **not** Link checker, so\nthe section is permission-filtered and the absence is meaningful.\n\n## CI\n\n```yaml\nintegration-tests:\n  needs: build\n  uses: Jahia/jahia-modules-action/.github/workflows/reusable-integration-tests.yml@v2\n  with:\n    module_id: geo-readiness\n    jahia_image: ghcr.io/jahia/jahia-ee-dev:8-SNAPSHOT\n    provisioning_manifest: provisioning-manifest-build.yml\n    instance_type: ubuntu-latest\n```\n\nInputs verified against the live schema of the reusable workflow rather\nthan copied from the note proposing them. `instance_type` matters: the\naction defaults to `self-hosted`, which this repository''s other jobs do\nnot use.\n\n`.github/MIGRATION-NOTES.md` §2.5 and the matching `tests/README.md`\nsection are marked superseded — that stale note is why this never ran,\nand leaving it invites the next reader to re-derive the same wrong\nconclusion.\n\n## Two things to watch\n\n- **A \"Something wrong happened\" banner** appears above the working\ndashboard. It blocks nothing and the dashboard renders correctly beneath\nit, but it is unexplained and is the one loose thread that could be a\nreal defect rather than a test artifact.\n- **CI will be slower than the 50s measured locally**, since it boots\nJahia and provisions 19 modules first. The four jContent UI tests are\nthe ones to watch for flakiness.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqW4VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD0wQAGqU6HhkUPPKRgQlCYk9IM8d\n0pgxsLYeahjRR6It4bFKqbq4I4ELVYjwzvCYQ+jqvGT4txZP4yJQivS6V6Vgk+Zf\np4i7xUot/V6p9Do0uLZCDPWsyS72fWzbc16gbCORh7kC2JFaM6Abzcj+QuRHrsh/\nUp9ZVbHeQwMcbTgHiflEIdSvazfpOLkyNbsvrQ2X41ZRRXkJSA4pWRRJTFYXa95w\nAgokRlF8Aew65FZ/Rl4ckEdUzxFvvUEWBw9SwMDsKnUg1gufBSbJOveld98fNm6J\nG2BHuL0mPT9miDek/LQoGyK7l/SJ5vpbDt2e6579wfhSZR7gFfnc+/2GfgRbqFE1\nTJIgz0CebbkwVmEK7/L/RoeLeA1M1xIWCA89n7yy6eARBTB3McrdoHgGkuyUQnl1\nNYedvTKNrMX0Rf/tgJrRTN7UJHoblTlmHt/tEvZeEUYdLJLeP4Jr+QscsQqiqATN\nPducnbPgGN/xn2dJ4w9ZV7Ammi9QdG3tqCZOrsxshKbfqojg5XuQfbNg5IT66HzI\n5feY1b0wOwBeX8WEy4UidGuMVlb989CCEKySg54l8Ie0SYREVOZUsLad3wVVy7ps\n5heKF0DqG7rPTF/blJupFwkAwm9dTYa3cQ2xTUeQYi72UM2oGkl2kJg1sspBKddk\nV2n270WwTQEjd3hEmXHL\n=Tdv6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T16:11:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/efb129acd22ea9d1ab403d66dfe429a0262d60e9","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGVmYjEyOWFjZDIyZWE5ZDFhYjQwM2Q2NmRmZTQyOWEwMjYyZDYwZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/6e0d7593b066e84db35e9cf5b95143650eb10617","sha":"6e0d7593b066e84db35e9cf5b95143650eb10617","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/6e0d7593b066e84db35e9cf5b95143650eb10617"}],"sha":"efb129acd22ea9d1ab403d66dfe429a0262d60e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/efb129acd22ea9d1ab403d66dfe429a0262d60e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/6e0d7593b066e84db35e9cf5b95143650eb10617/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:06:51Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:06:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: take the whole-codebase reliability rating to A (#11)\n\n> Replaces #9, which carries the same three commits and the same tree.\nThat PR''s\n> Sonar analysis accumulated findings across its successive revisions:\nit ended up\n> reporting 10 new reliability issues in `Charts.jsx` at lines that are\nbyte-identical\n> to `main`, in a file the branch does not modify, with the count\n*rising* from 63 to\n> 70 as code was removed. This is the same work on a branch with no\nanalysis history.\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to #6. That PR aimed at the two failing whole-codebase ratings\nbut, as its review found, fixed a real leak and a real validation gap\nrather than the issues those ratings were counting. This is the\nfollow-up, and it is narrower than it first looks.\n\n## The target moved while this was being written\n\nA CI analysis re-ran on `main` partway through. Before and after:\n\n| On `main` | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| SECURITY-impact issues | 52 (`java:S1989`) | 0 |\n| MAJOR RELIABILITY issues | 14 | 0 |\n| Security rating | B | **A** |\n| Reliability rating | C | **B** |\n\nThe Security B -> A on `main` happened through that re-analysis, not\nthrough anything here.\n\n**One issue is left holding the reliability rating down**, and this PR\nclears it:\n\n```\njava:S3077 - GeoReadinessConfigService.java:26\n\"Use a thread-safe type; adding volatile is not enough\"\n```\n\nThe `volatile` reference was already correct - `Snapshot` is a private\nstatic final class whose every field is final and primitive or String,\nso swapping it wholesale is the immutable-snapshot pattern and a reader\ncould never see a half-applied configuration. Sonar cannot prove that.\nIts own remediation is the one taken: `AtomicReference` carries the same\nvisibility guarantee and says out loud what the `volatile` only implied.\n\nMeasured on a branch scan: **whole-codebase security A, reliability A**,\nagainst `main`''s A/B.\n\n## The rest\n\nThese address findings the analyzer has stopped reporting. Kept because\neach is a defect on its own terms, not because a rating needs them:\n\n- **Nothing escapes a servlet method.** The three servlets that still\ndeclared `throws` now use the shape `GeoReportServlet` already had: work\nin a private `dispatch`, entry point catches. An exception leaving\n`doPost` is answered by the container with a stack trace.\n- **No mutable state on a shared servlet.** Constructor injection, as\n`GeoReportServlet` already did, makes the injected config `final`.\n- **An interrupt is no longer swallowed.** `Future.get()` clears the\nflag on its way out, so catching it as `Exception` left nothing\ndownstream able to tell the request was cancelled.\n- **The language pattern is bounded.** It repeated a group without limit\nand Java''s matcher recurses per repetition, so a long enough value\noverflowed the stack before it could be refused - and that value arrives\nfrom the request and ends up as a node name. Bounded to four subtags;\n`en`, `fr`, `pt_BR`, `fr-BE`, `zh-Hans-CN`, `de_CH` all still accepted.\n- **Three dead imports** that #6 left behind when the opening moved into\n`FetchGuard`.\n\n## Chart accessibility was removed from this PR\n\nAn earlier revision also rewrote the chart marks in `Charts.jsx`. Every\nmark was a `div` made focusable so `onFocus` could mirror `onMouseEnter`\nand reveal a tooltip - not a control, in the tab ring, and silent to\nassistive technology.\n\nTwo attempts at it each traded one rule for another. The handlers on a\nnon-interactive `div` raise `S6848`; a `role=img` to satisfy that raises\n`S6819`; a `tabIndex` to restore focus raises `S6845`. Nothing added to\nthe element escapes the triangle - only removing the handlers or making\nthe mark genuinely interactive does, and that is a tooltip redesign\nrather than a lint fix.\n\nSince none of those findings appear on `main`''s current analysis,\nkeeping them here only charged this PR for pre-existing behaviour.\n`Charts.jsx` and `Charts.module.css` are untouched; the work is\npreserved on `feat/chart-accessibility` and will come back as its own\nPR.\n\n## On the gate\n\nThis PR''s Sonar run reports new-code maintainability issues in\nJavaScript and CSS across files it does not touch -\n`GeoReadinessDrawer.jsx`, the `tabs/` panels, `init.js`,\n`Tabs.module.css`. They are new SonarJS rules (the `S77xx` series,\n`css:S7924`) that did not exist when `main`''s baseline was analysed, so\nthey land as new the first time any analysis runs. `main` currently\nfails the same condition on its own, and this branch changes no\nJavaScript at all.\n\nTwo of them are worth someone''s attention regardless of the gate:\n`css:S7924` flags **two contrast failures at `Tabs.module.css:21-22`**.\nThat is a real accessibility defect and wants its own ticket.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"06eba8efda70f3e75703e77e939dd92b5c63a9f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/06eba8efda70f3e75703e77e939dd92b5c63a9f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/6e0d7593b066e84db35e9cf5b95143650eb10617","verification":{"payload":"tree 06eba8efda70f3e75703e77e939dd92b5c63a9f5\nparent d4854719f7d42161d833612fcb0c59ad86d70b2a\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1789477611 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789477611 +0200\n\nfix: take the whole-codebase reliability rating to A (#11)\n\n> Replaces #9, which carries the same three commits and the same tree.\nThat PR''s\n> Sonar analysis accumulated findings across its successive revisions:\nit ended up\n> reporting 10 new reliability issues in `Charts.jsx` at lines that are\nbyte-identical\n> to `main`, in a file the branch does not modify, with the count\n*rising* from 63 to\n> 70 as code was removed. This is the same work on a branch with no\nanalysis history.\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to #6. That PR aimed at the two failing whole-codebase ratings\nbut, as its review found, fixed a real leak and a real validation gap\nrather than the issues those ratings were counting. This is the\nfollow-up, and it is narrower than it first looks.\n\n## The target moved while this was being written\n\nA CI analysis re-ran on `main` partway through. Before and after:\n\n| On `main` | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| SECURITY-impact issues | 52 (`java:S1989`) | 0 |\n| MAJOR RELIABILITY issues | 14 | 0 |\n| Security rating | B | **A** |\n| Reliability rating | C | **B** |\n\nThe Security B -> A on `main` happened through that re-analysis, not\nthrough anything here.\n\n**One issue is left holding the reliability rating down**, and this PR\nclears it:\n\n```\njava:S3077 - GeoReadinessConfigService.java:26\n\"Use a thread-safe type; adding volatile is not enough\"\n```\n\nThe `volatile` reference was already correct - `Snapshot` is a private\nstatic final class whose every field is final and primitive or String,\nso swapping it wholesale is the immutable-snapshot pattern and a reader\ncould never see a half-applied configuration. Sonar cannot prove that.\nIts own remediation is the one taken: `AtomicReference` carries the same\nvisibility guarantee and says out loud what the `volatile` only implied.\n\nMeasured on a branch scan: **whole-codebase security A, reliability A**,\nagainst `main`''s A/B.\n\n## The rest\n\nThese address findings the analyzer has stopped reporting. Kept because\neach is a defect on its own terms, not because a rating needs them:\n\n- **Nothing escapes a servlet method.** The three servlets that still\ndeclared `throws` now use the shape `GeoReportServlet` already had: work\nin a private `dispatch`, entry point catches. An exception leaving\n`doPost` is answered by the container with a stack trace.\n- **No mutable state on a shared servlet.** Constructor injection, as\n`GeoReportServlet` already did, makes the injected config `final`.\n- **An interrupt is no longer swallowed.** `Future.get()` clears the\nflag on its way out, so catching it as `Exception` left nothing\ndownstream able to tell the request was cancelled.\n- **The language pattern is bounded.** It repeated a group without limit\nand Java''s matcher recurses per repetition, so a long enough value\noverflowed the stack before it could be refused - and that value arrives\nfrom the request and ends up as a node name. Bounded to four subtags;\n`en`, `fr`, `pt_BR`, `fr-BE`, `zh-Hans-CN`, `de_CH` all still accepted.\n- **Three dead imports** that #6 left behind when the opening moved into\n`FetchGuard`.\n\n## Chart accessibility was removed from this PR\n\nAn earlier revision also rewrote the chart marks in `Charts.jsx`. Every\nmark was a `div` made focusable so `onFocus` could mirror `onMouseEnter`\nand reveal a tooltip - not a control, in the tab ring, and silent to\nassistive technology.\n\nTwo attempts at it each traded one rule for another. The handlers on a\nnon-interactive `div` raise `S6848`; a `role=img` to satisfy that raises\n`S6819`; a `tabIndex` to restore focus raises `S6845`. Nothing added to\nthe element escapes the triangle - only removing the handlers or making\nthe mark genuinely interactive does, and that is a tooltip redesign\nrather than a lint fix.\n\nSince none of those findings appear on `main`''s current analysis,\nkeeping them here only charged this PR for pre-existing behaviour.\n`Charts.jsx` and `Charts.module.css` are untouched; the work is\npreserved on `feat/chart-accessibility` and will come back as its own\nPR.\n\n## On the gate\n\nThis PR''s Sonar run reports new-code maintainability issues in\nJavaScript and CSS across files it does not touch -\n`GeoReadinessDrawer.jsx`, the `tabs/` panels, `init.js`,\n`Tabs.module.css`. They are new SonarJS rules (the `S77xx` series,\n`css:S7924`) that did not exist when `main`''s baseline was analysed, so\nthey land as new the first time any analysis runs. `main` currently\nfails the same condition on its own, and this branch changes no\nJavaScript at all.\n\nTwo of them are worth someone''s attention regardless of the gate:\n`css:S7924` flags **two contrast failures at `Tabs.module.css:21-22`**.\nThat is a real accessibility defect and wants its own ticket.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqULrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT1MQACJHwB6KdtUNueChLMUR70l1\nkO3ds0MDLyoEyHdp3xIC9mU8yA6QT4fG1diU65o8Thc5Rdnq5S0mpBhEKKWa7DjC\nf/Yg4E93Y2lSO6jEDkTptTfkgWKxugLYo/1zteqG05KAAc8cir+FsxDxSIq+l9oP\nWNL8RtUKaDKLXdqtv3r4HQu1tdvvLQ1x80dVh+vYN+zqBFvVTXK4xrgCT6xN2lnO\nWsYY8+d/FEH2ci1u+S3CFLfHEUfIO/5rZdeAOycPKGn7ySeLjHzxOnymJYG3jq1q\niY0NIgoHbzV/09LgidNn2Ip4coQMd0GE/WyikyhdtU/2d65PWZGblaA1dXtIWJZE\npt/S+L14ejJQhGu+VVkBe+77apdIYpcD41n92FS6UCBLOLrL5b9+rijxg2w1awGz\nZjm+gzgROqEqIn26KYXDMJ0Yx17aCj7vbfbgwKzoAs6zTQopKK7qifJGDga17bI1\nNCTbu7UVuzeDaMpIpR3jZuE7VGtypvZoE/bCUTwX9WOFGHcbeJ1cn2e13W94g7Cc\n8oQpoAZSwt7arxaVKqSSx1m4feIBtWH3cNLET4MBFxhYS6XvvR6/uV7AOxg2K7HW\n8/RduzjMjH/TWBChy4atuFVzGaMeu6LrOrJi1l2rIx7GTKKgXv8qD5N0Hv4HYFU0\naFUUhbibRS+foG6vGAZ3\n=XbZR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T13:06:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/6e0d7593b066e84db35e9cf5b95143650eb10617","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDZlMGQ3NTkzYjA2NmU4NGRiMzVlOWNmNWI5NTE0MzY1MGViMTA2MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/d4854719f7d42161d833612fcb0c59ad86d70b2a","sha":"d4854719f7d42161d833612fcb0c59ad86d70b2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/d4854719f7d42161d833612fcb0c59ad86d70b2a"}],"sha":"6e0d7593b066e84db35e9cf5b95143650eb10617","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/6e0d7593b066e84db35e9cf5b95143650eb10617"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/d4854719f7d42161d833612fcb0c59ad86d70b2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T12:10:17Z","email":"smonier@Jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T12:10:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: validate the address where it is opened, and close what is opened (#6)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe quality gate on `main` fails on four conditions, two of which are\nratings over the **whole** codebase rather than new code: `B Security\nRating` and `C Reliability Rating`. The pull-request gate only ever\nmeasured new code, which is why it passed while these sat underneath.\nThis fixes both classes at their source.\n\n## Changes\n\n**A leaked stream, on every fetch.** Both fetchers took the response\nstream and never closed it. `HttpURLConnection.disconnect()` releases\nthe connection, not the stream it handed out, so each crawler check\nleaked one per agent and each scanned page leaked one. Both now read the\nbody inside try-with-resources.\n\n**An address validated on derivation but not on use.** `PublicUrls.base`\nstopped trusting the request''s `Host` header, but the two fetchers still\nopened whatever string they were handed. There is now a single place in\nthe module that opens an outbound connection, `FetchGuard.open`, and it\nopens the value it has just validated rather than the string it was\ngiven: same origin as the site being reported on, `http` or `https`\nonly, redirects never followed. The sitemap index''s children go through\nthat same door instead of a separate check standing beside it. `grep -rn\n''openConnection()'' src/main/java` now returns exactly one line.\n\n## Verification\n\nBuilt and deployed on a local instance. The drawer still fetches all\nsixteen agents and all sixteen answer 200; a site scan still scores 13\npages at 82%; the sitemap comparison still reads its 378 entries. So the\nguard admits what it should and the behaviour is unchanged.\n\nI could not enumerate the Sonar issues directly: the findings for a\nbranch analysis carry no annotations, and the Web API needs a token this\nenvironment does not have. These two are the causes the code itself\nshows, and the ratings they drive are exactly the two that fail. If the\ngate still reports either rating after this, the dashboard''s issue list\nis the next step and I will need a token or the list pasted in.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4fbb7f92eb6a4888c19c5753e0c06ac0e531aef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/d4fbb7f92eb6a4888c19c5753e0c06ac0e531aef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/d4854719f7d42161d833612fcb0c59ad86d70b2a","verification":{"payload":"tree d4fbb7f92eb6a4888c19c5753e0c06ac0e531aef\nparent fb097346812d515bcb455a62ae525bb104013258\nauthor Stephane Monier <smonier@Jahia.com> 1789474217 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789474217 +0200\n\nfix: validate the address where it is opened, and close what is opened (#6)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe quality gate on `main` fails on four conditions, two of which are\nratings over the **whole** codebase rather than new code: `B Security\nRating` and `C Reliability Rating`. The pull-request gate only ever\nmeasured new code, which is why it passed while these sat underneath.\nThis fixes both classes at their source.\n\n## Changes\n\n**A leaked stream, on every fetch.** Both fetchers took the response\nstream and never closed it. `HttpURLConnection.disconnect()` releases\nthe connection, not the stream it handed out, so each crawler check\nleaked one per agent and each scanned page leaked one. Both now read the\nbody inside try-with-resources.\n\n**An address validated on derivation but not on use.** `PublicUrls.base`\nstopped trusting the request''s `Host` header, but the two fetchers still\nopened whatever string they were handed. There is now a single place in\nthe module that opens an outbound connection, `FetchGuard.open`, and it\nopens the value it has just validated rather than the string it was\ngiven: same origin as the site being reported on, `http` or `https`\nonly, redirects never followed. The sitemap index''s children go through\nthat same door instead of a separate check standing beside it. `grep -rn\n''openConnection()'' src/main/java` now returns exactly one line.\n\n## Verification\n\nBuilt and deployed on a local instance. The drawer still fetches all\nsixteen agents and all sixteen answer 200; a site scan still scores 13\npages at 82%; the sitemap comparison still reads its 378 entries. So the\nguard admits what it should and the behaviour is unchanged.\n\nI could not enumerate the Sonar issues directly: the findings for a\nbranch analysis carry no annotations, and the Web API needs a token this\nenvironment does not have. These two are the causes the code itself\nshows, and the ratings they drive are exactly the two that fail. If the\ngate still reports either rating after this, the dashboard''s issue list\nis the next step and I will need a token or the list pasted in.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqTWpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApJMQAHLmd5KNm19VOzVA7jrDrNpO\nV2JyGzdq38WUwH3SWpaLlc/KaBo8GYcV4NLV0PdJcJmQlwf6UOze1W/cy23jtR+5\n4s+bBX1gr2C6lP8WxVTLsUewiZUqJbup1U34pFxdkQgkOCXy0L4A7Q+5B2/kXy6G\n4P3QQ672P1OWCJQeQff7YtjxH/cBXFnkU6WGQmvd3wYz4S21NO2GEcHufbJQr3MH\nC3h8FdHztjz0kbADH8E/Z1MHmjiqgGE2speNyfrYdC/FsPOEpEnX5t9/7HknoAzx\n3OZZwv9/ZE6XQnRvkgTSBKTcdzsCGCIq2Q5jU9jhESd4qq3FmLoLxIS5Xzl31Wc/\nVrk4pXYJ98fH19GmIoPiod9eeAsUVWzATDgm5Mil5YoS6Ibk2AUwQuvrX9eq3x2W\nZ54B1wECMwRjkM4yXFv1FOGmUfYZnrqNb7lrMd9/jdLgtSi5n2l/PCuAcK5hS8iu\nbaG1cn+jq4fGbLEbjIITYBHQQSp35m2HeRFv08KMJ/Jyzegd0ZbEtjNVo07q0PiQ\nqpmwaSJ2r/E7toJ2OK7sB9URFHxpJYXvjiS1wj3GGOU0l/oxsUS+GoF8fRE9MrKa\nzZr6HnB17xuvp4rhMr+byq2KuTkC3RIsGZ1BAQTaJKOXvM6QB/KWOEnUw9zpo1Jx\nZQH0Xkl7NRgaNO9BHnFL\n=vVMH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at"