bb5d67fb6f2dd3066ec0"}],"sha":"c71a84de86d02c328ce414709cbab5ea2ab18a70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/c71a84de86d02c328ce414709cbab5ea2ab18a70"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/0c4cf90e82df325ba50bbb5d67fb6f2dd3066ec0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:34:37Z","email":"smonier@Jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:34:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: a written GEO report from a configured provider, with export (#3)\n\nEverything else on the dashboard is measured and says so. This adds the one place a model is asked for judgement: a Report tab under Overview that reads a digest of the measurements and writes where the site stands for AI crawlers, a compliance status per area, what to fix first with who can fix it and the effort, quick wins, and a now/next/later roadmap. It can be exported as Markdown or JSON.\n\nThe tab exists only when a provider, a model and a key are configured. Anthropic, OpenAI and DeepSeek are supported, through the same configuration keys page-audit uses. It answers only on a click because each answer is paid for, generations are metered per user, and the report is stored per language so it reads back at once. The provider receives the measurements, never page bodies and never the key; the answer is parsed into a fixed shape and rendered as text, and a page reference is kept only when the digest listed that page.\n\nThe endpoint sits behind the dashboard''s own permission gate. A Cypress spec covers everything around the paid call it never makes.","tree":{"sha":"863c8704a18f330e68f197fce094e47bfac55734","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/863c8704a18f330e68f197fce094e47bfac55734"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/0c4cf90e82df325ba50bbb5d67fb6f2dd3066ec0","verification":{"payload":"tree 863c8704a18f330e68f197fce094e47bfac55734\nparent 93f51501d67370d130fa598b288d9c6c9915fc42\nauthor Stephane Monier <smonier@Jahia.com> 1789378477 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789378477 +0200\n\nfeat: a written GEO report from a configured provider, with export (#3)\n\nEverything else on the dashboard is measured and says so. This adds the one place a model is asked for judgement: a Report tab under Overview that reads a digest of the measurements and writes where the site stands for AI crawlers, a compliance status per area, what to fix first with who can fix it and the effort, quick wins, and a now/next/later roadmap. It can be exported as Markdown or JSON.\n\nThe tab exists only when a provider, a model and a key are configured. Anthropic, OpenAI and DeepSeek are supported, through the same configuration keys page-audit uses. It answers only on a click because each answer is paid for, generations are metered per user, and the report is stored per language so it reads back at once. The provider receives the measurements, never page bodies and never the key; the answer is parsed into a fixed shape and rendered as text, and a page reference is kept only when the digest listed that page.\n\nThe endpoint sits behind the dashboard''s own permission gate. A Cypress spec covers everything around the paid call it never makes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp7+tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADE0QAG/VajW2ChAeRt1+1ovwCoAu\nyawe+u8+CFX9PHImlQdM4xPjcjWbeZj/2tGKCixfjodeDvn/I+EaNp6tedJPmLD3\n3sfsyCQ0Q5a7PKtpeWZR4ylykdEam9e2h/WoS5eO0df90XNzi+97JW79gUuuhv+U\nfixlhgUSFiUAW/PeB74bTQx1gl77rBml05LAncgmiWW6jVDHIMARIecj4gz2ixPO\n8duhLN1Zjy+IyXiyrW1FoGrshUsv7+uVJz7QqDUBpy4xuuDh1b/RFy/fUBkWupZ8\n8KHnNM/TYmD5e5evLrPSgQcdH1mYj99NhhhIuBPcOp2451hjGpbBsL5SNu8v4kAd\nCgF/pG4EF+gnJadPdGAg2lEotd67nXErnfk2qyk9cxfupwdQTKaCiSJeu9QYBE8v\nrTIEP0BAu+Z5c3rb3brSSZvKTZCgGiy/sb4ZOSD94+91lm97NEa86BX4XR1vZ/NB\nv8lui06EA3bs85Jx9jyF3faX7q2FgB+fbI4jDoy0uslDTVKqXGx+FwG6ClEKFlM3\nfM12ABtoYFxqPn1RK1kHpLc4CEEMW2hwcRfWAGgkVfq1Kr0GeNpUE9U+7+ztnhV5\nWtp4yzOORdzcImSkUXgyo7ny5WLZ/pPIUdVCh3gRn/RkvdYi6Kz4Dz7425pZwJFP\n4KPg7yJXckd05rwc1mjR\n=2wiT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T09:34:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com