s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/6a1b48ea52a98d7337bbfae92b0f1da422714b48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:41:59Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:41:59Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Prepare 1.1.0: the visual release\n\nNothing new is measured. What was already measured is now drawn where a\nnumber has a shape worth seeing - a meter, section bars, an age\nhistogram with newest-to-oldest ranges, coverage beside score per\nlanguage, a stacked coverage bar, and the failure matrix - and no\nfindings list is capped any more. Docs describe the paging rule as it\nfinally landed: full up to twenty-five, a control from ten, pages beyond.","tree":{"sha":"24da028dcafe14d2dd15e8a8eab7ee33f1af3474","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/24da028dcafe14d2dd15e8a8eab7ee33f1af3474"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/6a1b48ea52a98d7337bbfae92b0f1da422714b48","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/6a1b48ea52a98d7337bbfae92b0f1da422714b48","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDZhMWI0OGVhNTJhOThkNzMzN2JiZmFlOTJiMGYxZGE0MjI3MTRiNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/9b75dcd52d307bb647bc1def57a22d96d309335b","sha":"9b75dcd52d307bb647bc1def57a22d96d309335b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/9b75dcd52d307bb647bc1def57a22d96d309335b"}],"sha":"6a1b48ea52a98d7337bbfae92b0f1da422714b48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/6a1b48ea52a98d7337bbfae92b0f1da422714b48"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/9b75dcd52d307bb647bc1def57a22d96d309335b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:33:21Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:33:21Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Show lists in full up to 25 rows; show the pager from 10\n\nTen was the old display cap carried straight over as the page size, so\na twelve-row list that used to show ten still showed ten - with a pager\ninstead of \"and 2 more\". Nothing got better for a small site, and it\nread as a cap, which is exactly how it was reported.\n\nTwo thresholds now, on purpose. A list is shown in full up to the\ncurrent page size, 25 by default, so nothing on a small site is ever\ncut. The control appears once a list passes the smallest page size, ten,\nso a denser view can be chosen and paged even when nothing is being\nwithheld - otherwise a list of twelve could never be paged at all, and\nnobody could see that paging works. Below ten rows there is no control,\nbecause there is nothing it could do.\n\nThe failure matrix follows the same rule. Verified on luxe: the twelve\nstale sitemap dates show in full with \"1-12 of 12\"; the thirteen-row\nmatrix shows in full at 25, and at 10 pages to \"11-13 of 13\" with next\nand last disabled; the four-row noindex group shows no control.","tree":{"sha":"ee41b76e3c55e9585439ae3eb0c17402f60a06d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/ee41b76e3c55e9585439ae3eb0c17402f60a06d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/9b75dcd52d307bb647bc1def57a22d96d309335b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/9b75dcd52d307bb647bc1def57a22d96d309335b","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDliNzVkY2Q1MmQzMDdiYjY0N2JjMWRlZjU3YTIyZDk2ZDMwOTMzNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/75af1264917842a65c6c5b4faa6e3d966d6a9de5","sha":"75af1264917842a65c6c5b4faa6e3d966d6a9de5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/75af1264917842a65c6c5b4faa6e3d966d6a9de5"}],"sha":"9b75dcd52d307bb647bc1def57a22d96d309335b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/9b75dcd52d307bb647bc1def57a22d96d309335b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/75af1264917842a65c6c5b4faa6e3d966d6a9de5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:18:58Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:18:58Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Say \"Showing 1-10 of 12\" above a paged list, not only below it\n\nA group header said 12 and ten rows followed. The pagination control\nthat reconciles the two sat below the rows, so a reader met the\ncontradiction before the explanation and read it as a bug - which is\nexactly how it was reported. The range line now sits between the group''s\nexplanation and its first row, only when the list is actually paged, so\na short list stays as it was.","tree":{"sha":"59ed332ee1f9592ddb4a2055041d1df40b1d5e12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/59ed332ee1f9592ddb4a2055041d1df40b1d5e12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/75af1264917842a65c6c5b4faa6e3d966d6a9de5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/75af1264917842a65c6c5b4faa6e3d966d6a9de5","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDc1YWYxMjY0OTE3ODQyYTY1YzZjNWI0ZmFhNmUzZDk2NmQ2YTlkZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/4ad0f31bfbbed3f0bd006d42774eeacd9a1c8642","sha":"4ad0f31bfbbed3f0bd006d42774eeacd9a1c8642","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/4ad0f31bfbbed3f0bd006d42774eeacd9a1c8642"}],"sha":"75af1264917842a65c6c5b4faa6e3d966d6a9de5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/75af1264917842a65c6c5b4faa6e3d966d6a9de5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/4ad0f31bfbbed3f0bd006d42774eeacd9a1c8642/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:40:52Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:40:52Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Page every findings list; none is capped any more\n\nSitemap findings, unlinked pages, address conflicts and invisible\ncontent stopped at ten rows with an \"and N more\" line. That told the\nreader something was withheld and gave them no way to reach it: on a\nsite with two hundred stale sitemap dates, a hundred and ninety were\ninvisible. Invisible content had the opposite problem - no cap at all,\nso a large gated section rendered every row.\n\nOne Paged wrapper does it for all of them, with Moonstone''s\nTablePagination, ten rows at a time and 10/25/50 to choose from. It\nrenders no control when a group fits in one view, so a short list looks\nexactly as it did, and it returns to page one when the row count changes\nbecause the old page may no longer exist after a rescan.\n\nVerified on luxe: the twelve stale sitemap dates page as 1-10 then\n11-12 of 12 with next and last disabled, while the four-row noindex\ngroup beside them shows no control.","tree":{"sha":"980051b462633cfa3308f5f6a6a443112b1f3a3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/980051b462633cfa3308f5f6a6a443112b1f3a3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/4ad0f31bfbbed3f0bd006d42774eeacd9a1c8642","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/4ad0f31bfbbed3f0bd006d42774eeacd9a1c8642","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDRhZDBmMzFiZmJiZWQzZjBiZDAwNmQ0Mjc3NGVlYWNkOWExYzg2NDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/509505a8f2483c1e4fe55876c24a89b6387b91b2","sha":"509505a8f2483c1e4fe55876c24a89b6387b91b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/509505a8f2483c1e4fe55876c24a89b6387b91b2"}],"sha":"4ad0f31bfbbed3f0bd006d42774eeacd9a1c8642","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/4ad0f31bfbbed3f0bd006d42774eeacd9a1c8642"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/509505a8f2483c1e4fe55876c24a89b6387b91b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:19:14Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:19:14Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Page the failure matrix with Moonstone''s TablePagination\n\nThe matrix was capped at twenty-five rows by a slice. A scan keeps up to\nfive hundred pages with findings, and a five-hundred-row matrix is a\nwall; twenty-five silently dropped the rest. Ten per view now, with\nMoonstone''s own control - first, previous, next, last, and a rows-per-\nview choice of 10, 25 or 50 - shown only when there is more than one\npage of rows.\n\nThe column set is computed over every finding, not the current page, so\nthe columns and their order stay put while paging: a template-wide\nfailure is the leftmost solid column on page one and on page fifty.\nChanging rows-per-view returns to page one, since the old page number\nwould otherwise point past the end.\n\nVerified on luxe: 1-10 of 13, then 11-13 of 13 with the same eleven\ncolumns and next/last disabled.","tree":{"sha":"1c5184a1940093302a3051ff1baf2d97d615dc1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/1c5184a1940093302a3051ff1baf2d97d615dc1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/509505a8f2483c1e4fe55876c24a89b6387b91b2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/509505a8f2483c1e4fe55876c24a89b6387b91b2","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDUwOTUwNWE4ZjI0ODNjMWU0ZmU1NTg3NmMyNGE4OWI2Mzg3YjkxYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/10dffdbc309eba7d49809a065093936af7b15127","sha":"10dffdbc309eba7d49809a065093936af7b15127","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/10dffdbc309eba7d49809a065093936af7b15127"}],"sha":"509505a8f2483c1e4fe55876c24a89b6387b91b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/509505a8f2483c1e4fe55876c24a89b6387b91b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/10dffdbc309eba7d49809a065093936af7b15127/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:13:10Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:13:10Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Pages with findings as a matrix: pages down, failing checks across\n\nA list of \"15/17\" chips said how many things were wrong on each page. It\ncould not say which things, or that two of them are wrong on every page\n- and that second fact is the whole point of the template roll-up. One\ncell per page and check, colored by severity, with columns ordered by\nhow many pages fail them: a column that is solid top to bottom is a\ntemplate, not thirteen authors, and it is visible before anyone reads a\nnumber. On luxe, structured data and modification date form two solid\ncolumns; the gated privacy policy lights up across its row at 6/17 with\ntwo critical cells.\n\nSeverity was not on the aggregate - the scan keeps failed check ids per\npage and trims the full checks array - so SiteScorer now records\nid -> severity once per scan, the same eighteen for every page. Cells,\ncolumn headers and pass cells all carry a hover and keyboard tooltip,\nverified by dispatching the events and reading the tooltip back; every\nstatus color ships with its word in the legend.\n\nOne trap on the way, recorded: the locale JSON is bundled, so a literal\nbackslash-n appended to both files failed yarn build:production, and\nunder mvn -q the message was invisible. Run yarn directly to see\nwebpack''s own error.","tree":{"sha":"0bd043f18a984f20cfa6bbe59401531a4ef90e35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/0bd043f18a984f20cfa6bbe59401531a4ef90e35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/10dffdbc309eba7d49809a065093936af7b15127","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/10dffdbc309eba7d49809a065093936af7b15127","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDEwZGZmZGJjMzA5ZWJhN2Q0OTgwOWEwNjUwOTM5MzZhZjdiMTUxMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/1e8f47593f8a560cfd2670d5a61c0232c11f12ae","sha":"1e8f47593f8a560cfd2670d5a61c0232c11f12ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/1e8f47593f8a560cfd2670d5a61c0232c11f12ae"}],"sha":"10dffdbc309eba7d49809a065093936af7b15127","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/10dffdbc309eba7d49809a065093936af7b15127"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/1e8f47593f8a560cfd2670d5a61c0232c11f12ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:14:13Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:14:13Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Draw the numbers that have a shape: charts in four panels, no library\n\nA meter under the site score whose fill carries severity; horizontal\nbars for the score by section; a histogram of content age and a range\nbar per type and section from newest to oldest with the median marked;\ntranslated coverage beside readiness score per language; one stacked bar\nfor structured-data coverage. Every mark carries a hover and keyboard\ntooltip, value first.\n\nNo chart library. Inside a Module Federation bundle that is weight every\njContent page pays, plus a second theme to keep in step with Moonstone,\nand the forms needed here are bars and a meter, which CSS draws better\nthan a canvas. Colors are Moonstone''s own tokens and were validated\nrather than chosen by eye: the dark accent and purple pass the\ncolorblind and normal-vision floors as an adjacent pair on Moonstone''s\nlight surface; the plain accent fails 3:1 and is never a mark; gray is a\ntrack, not a series. An unmeasured language renders as words, never as a\nzero-length bar.\n\nThree bugs found while verifying, all recorded in .agents/README.md. The\nhashed CSS-module class ends in \"=\", which is not a valid selector, so\nthe tooltip anchor threw and no tooltip ever appeared - anchored on a\ndata attribute now. Tone classes lost to every mark''s default at equal\nspecificity, so both series rendered in one color - scoped under .chart.\nAnd the Meter sat outside the .chart scope that defines the tokens, so\nits colors resolved to nothing - it carries the scope now.\n\npom moves to 1.1.0-SNAPSHOT: 1.0.0 is released and tagged.","tree":{"sha":"aebd2dd972f8cccf00dbc935d984943f501fb0a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/aebd2dd972f8cccf00dbc935d984943f501fb0a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/1e8f47593f8a560cfd2670d5a61c0232c11f12ae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/1e8f47593f8a560cfd2670d5a61c0232c11f12ae","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDFlOGY0NzU5M2Y4YTU2MGNmZDI2NzBkNWE2MWMwMjMyYzExZjEyYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/332cb9618134c685312a517f4d0268e83c7e8cd7","sha":"332cb9618134c685312a517f4d0268e83c7e8cd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/332cb9618134c685312a517f4d0268e83c7e8cd7"}],"sha":"1e8f47593f8a560cfd2670d5a61c0232c11f12ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/1e8f47593f8a560cfd2670d5a61c0232c11f12ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/332cb9618134c685312a517f4d0268e83c7e8cd7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:27:31Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:27:31Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Prepare 1.0.0: version, and documentation that matches what shipped\n\nSets the module version to 1.0.0 and dates the changelog. The jar builds\nat 329 KB carrying the front end, installs ACTIVE/STARTED, and every\nsurface answers: drawer 16/18 with context, links and schema; dashboard\nwith sitemap, links, vanity, llms and freshness; languages measuring two;\nschema mapping 189 of 189.\n\nThe README needed the most work, because it described the module as it\nwas nine stories ago: four tabs, a drawer that only reported sixteen\nfetches, and no mention of the sitemap comparison, the link graph,\naddresses, freshness, languages or structured data. It now describes the\nten panels in their four groups, and what the drawer says about where a\npage stands.\n\nOne of its \"known gaps\" had also stopped being true. Vanity URLs were\nlisted as host-dependent, falling back to the /sites/<key>/... form -\nwhich GEO-25 fixed by reading the default vanity from the repository.\nShipping a release that documents a fixed bug as a limitation is worse\nthan documenting nothing, so it is replaced by the three gaps that are\nreal: one language per scan for the link graph and freshness, redirects\ninvisible inside the sitemap''s own entries, and structured data that is\ngenerated but never injected.\n\nThe docs index no longer sends a reader to the backlog to pick work.\nAll nine stories are built, and several record a deliberate refusal -\nnot guessing a content type''s meaning from its name, not shipping a check\nthat cannot fire - which a later story should not quietly reverse.","tree":{"sha":"eb95d0153684c96c9756362cd5e29d22ec356aa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/eb95d0153684c96c9756362cd5e29d22ec356aa5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/332cb9618134c685312a517f4d0268e83c7e8cd7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/332cb9618134c685312a517f4d0268e83c7e8cd7","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDMzMmNiOTYxODEzNGM2ODUzMTJhNTE3ZjRkMDI2OGU4M2M3ZThjZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/8f76ec82e061bd578aa6656ca846a4dfe920bb7d","sha":"8f76ec82e061bd578aa6656ca846a4dfe920bb7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/8f76ec82e061bd578aa6656ca846a4dfe920bb7d"}],"sha":"332cb9618134c685312a517f4d0268e83c7e8cd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/332cb9618134c685312a517f4d0268e83c7e8cd7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/8f76ec82e061bd578aa6656ca846a4dfe920bb7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:24:25Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:24:25Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Group the dashboard''s ten panels into four\n\nTen tabs is a list, not a structure. They now sit under the same three\ngroups the drawer already sorts its checks into - can a crawler reach it,\nis what arrives usable, site-level files - so an editor learns one\nvocabulary in the drawer and meets it again here instead of a second\ntaxonomy invented for the dashboard. The site score stands outside them,\nbeing the summary of all three.\n\nSecond-level tabs render inside the panel under a divider, and a group\nholding one panel gets no second row at all, where a row of one tab would\nonly be furniture.\n\nOne rename: Sitemap becomes \"Sitemap vs reality\". That panel never writes\nanything - it is a comparison - and its old name collided hardest with\nthe Sitemap entry the sitemap module puts in the same left-hand nav.\nrobots.txt and llms.txt keep their names, because those tabs really are\nthose files and renaming them would make them harder to find.\n\nWorth recording rather than fixing here: the robots and llms modules are\nboth installed on the test instance, so their own editors sit in that nav\nbeside ours, which edit the same two files. That is functional overlap\nand a product decision, not something grouping can solve.","tree":{"sha":"d55c8265b7b911d4bde3aa2187a9bcf18205c8af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/d55c8265b7b911d4bde3aa2187a9bcf18205c8af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/8f76ec82e061bd578aa6656ca846a4dfe920bb7d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/8f76ec82e061bd578aa6656ca846a4dfe920bb7d","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDhmNzZlYzgyZTA2MWJkNTc4YWE2NjU2Y2E4NDZhNGRmZTkyMGJiN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/ef76a252449cb22b30b124cea7dce45ca146fe88","sha":"ef76a252449cb22b30b124cea7dce45ca146fe88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/ef76a252449cb22b30b124cea7dce45ca146fe88"}],"sha":"8f76ec82e061bd578aa6656ca846a4dfe920bb7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/8f76ec82e061bd578aa6656ca846a4dfe920bb7d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/ef76a252449cb22b30b124cea7dce45ca146fe88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:12:24Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:12:24Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-23: derive structured data from the content model\n\nEvery other tool infers schema.org output from the words on a page. The\ncontent type already says what the content is - a type carrying price,\nimages and address is a product listing whatever the prose reads like -\nso it is derived instead, which is both cheaper and more accurate and is\nthe one thing here nothing outside the CMS can do.\n\nDefaults exist only for Jahia''s own types, where the answer is not a\nmatter of opinion. A custom type is somebody''s model, and deciding that\nluxe:estate is a Product from the word \"estate\" would be reading intent\nout of a string: the same mistake refused in GEO-24 for classifying\nevergreen content by type name. Custom types start unmapped, are reported\nas unmapped, and are mapped by whoever defined them.\n\nProperty sources are the other half, and there conventions do hold.\ntitle, description, image, date, price, address, phone and email mean the\nsame thing across almost every model, so a candidate list per schema\nproperty found all five luxe types with no property configuration at all,\nincluding a price wrapped into an Offer and a weak reference resolved to\nan image URL.\n\nGaps are the output rather than a failure. luxe:blogPost has no author\nand luxe:estate no currency; both are named instead of filled from\nsomewhere plausible, which is how structured data ends up disagreeing\nwith the page it describes. Contradiction is checked directly: the\ngenerated name against the title the page rendered, allowing for a\ntemplate''s suffix, so \"Fees\" and \"Fees | Demo Site Luxe\" agree while\n\"Fees\" and \"Our pricing\" do not.\n\nNothing is injected. The drawer shows the snippet and a person places it.\nThat is the module''s report-versus-write line, and it matters most here.\n\nOne bug worth naming: put() returned early on offers, so every Product\nemitted without its price while still reporting valid, because name and\nimage were all the type required. A dropped value is invisible behind a\nvalidity flag.\n\nAlso adds three drawer facts that existed on the dashboard but are about\none page: the site and section averages beside the page score, the\ninbound link counts unconditionally rather than only on failure, and\nwhether the page is in llms.txt - distinguishing \"regenerating would add\nit\" from \"the generator deliberately does not include it\". Freshness is\nleft out, as GEO-24 decided: an author editing a page knows its age.","tree":{"sha":"ad1c7ec8be9df89a0e3c12410625a4c5720a85ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/ad1c7ec8be9df89a0e3c12410625a4c5720a85ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/ef76a252449cb22b30b124cea7dce45ca146fe88","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/ef76a252449cb22b30b124cea7dce45ca146fe88","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGVmNzZhMjUyNDQ5Y2IyMmIzMGIxMjRjZWE3ZGNlNDVjYTE0NmZlODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/5db6f48970a906daae35b7e578210605c28d8ee8","sha":"5db6f48970a906daae35b7e578210605c28d8ee8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/5db6f48970a906daae35b7e578210605c28d8ee8"}],"sha":"ef76a252449cb22b30b124cea7dce45ca146fe88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/ef76a252449cb22b30b124cea7dce45ca146fe88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/5db6f48970a906daae35b7e578210605c28d8ee8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:54:14Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:54:14Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-20: report readiness one language at a time\n\nA single site-wide figure hides the market that is failing. The analysis\nthis module came out of found a brand answering perfectly in one language\nand not at all in another, and an average would have called that site\nfine.\n\nThe second acceptance criterion is the one that shaped the code: a\nlanguage nobody has scanned reports as unmeasured, never as zero, and is\nrendered as plain text rather than as a chip that could be mistaken for a\nlow score. A zero in a comparison table reads as \"this market is broken\"\nwhen it means \"nobody has looked\", and those call for opposite responses\n- one is a content problem, the other a scan that was never scheduled.\nThe spread between best and worst is emitted only when at least two\nlanguages have actually been measured: one measured language has a spread\nof zero arithmetically, and printing that would claim the languages agree\nabout a site where only one was ever examined.\n\nCoverage is a repository read and needs no scan at all. A node exists in\na language when it carries that language''s j:translation_<lang>, and the\ntwo workspaces separate translated from published, which is what gives\nthe three counts the story asks for. Counted over pages and content items\nalike, since on a site whose articles are content rather than pages the\narticles are most of what a market needs.\n\nVerified by publishing a page in English only: French coverage dropped to\n99% with 1 never translated while English stayed at 100%, and the drawer\nnamed fr as missing on that page and nothing on a translated one. The\npage was removed afterwards and both workspaces confirmed clean. A French\nscan was run so the comparison could be exercised with two measured\nlanguages rather than one.","tree":{"sha":"6c7d9abefd3854613dbeee75261caeb644552aef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/6c7d9abefd3854613dbeee75261caeb644552aef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/5db6f48970a906daae35b7e578210605c28d8ee8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/5db6f48970a906daae35b7e578210605c28d8ee8","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDVkYjZmNDg5NzBhOTA2ZGFhZTM1YjdlNTc4MjEwNjA1YzI4ZDhlZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/2b1cd885e7dd78b5f903b6ff7356171a9ed41a63","sha":"2b1cd885e7dd78b5f903b6ff7356171a9ed41a63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/2b1cd885e7dd78b5f903b6ff7356171a9ed41a63"}],"sha":"5db6f48970a906daae35b7e578210605c28d8ee8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/5db6f48970a906daae35b7e578210605c28d8ee8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/2b1cd885e7dd78b5f903b6ff7356171a9ed41a63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:44:06Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:44:06Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-24: report where the site has gone stale\n\nFreshness is one of the criteria a crawl-based tool scores a site on, and\none of the few it cannot compute properly: it sees the dates a site\nchooses to publish, on the pages it happened to crawl. The repository has\nthe real modification date of everything published, so the whole\ndistribution is one query and needs no scan at all.\n\nThe acceptance asks for evergreen content to be distinguished from\ntime-sensitive content by type. Nothing here tries to classify types,\nbecause deciding that a luxe:estate ages and a legal page does not is a\nguess at somebody''s content model, and it would be wrong on the first\nsite with different naming. Grouping is the distinction: each type is\njudged against its own list, which is exactly what stops a legal notice\nbeing flagged next to a news article, and a second breakdown by section\ncovers how the work is actually divided up.\n\nA group is flagged on its newest item, never its oldest or its average.\n\"Nothing in here has been touched in a year\" is a fact somebody can act\non; \"the oldest item is old\" is true of every site that has ever existed.\n\nThe threshold is a dropdown that recomputes rather than filtering a\nstored answer, and is remembered so the scheduled run measures against\nthe same line. Verified live: at a year, luxe flags luxe:realtor and the\nlanding-pages section; at six months it also flags blogPost, agency,\nestate and contents. Restored to a year afterwards.\n\nMeasured per language, like the link graph and for the same reason: a\ntranslation carries its own dates, and a French page left behind while\nthe English one is maintained is the finding worth having.\n\nNo drawer line, as the story asks. An author editing a page already knows\nhow old it is.","tree":{"sha":"de18d3c22a03c59dbdc9a69a7bb8a17ef294f461","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/de18d3c22a03c59dbdc9a69a7bb8a17ef294f461"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/2b1cd885e7dd78b5f903b6ff7356171a9ed41a63","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/2b1cd885e7dd78b5f903b6ff7356171a9ed41a63","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDJiMWNkODg1ZTdkZDc4YjVmOTAzYjZmZjczNTYxNzFhOWVkNDFhNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/24314845731c83e2d029f6bd09d11b15fe5b92a2","sha":"24314845731c83e2d029f6bd09d11b15fe5b92a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/24314845731c83e2d029f6bd09d11b15fe5b92a2"}],"sha":"2b1cd885e7dd78b5f903b6ff7356171a9ed41a63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/2b1cd885e7dd78b5f903b6ff7356171a9ed41a63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/24314845731c83e2d029f6bd09d11b15fe5b92a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:36:22Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:36:22Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Check llms.txt against the site, and report a redirecting sitemap\nentry as one finding\n\nTwo things that both came out of adding a vanity URL to a page.\n\nllms.txt is generated once and then served unchanged, so it goes out of\ndate silently: nothing fails, nothing errors, an assistant is just handed\na map of a site that has moved on. That is exactly what happened here -\nthe file kept pointing at /home/agencies.html after that address started\nredirecting, and nothing anywhere said so.\n\nIt is compared against the generator rather than against a second set of\nrules, because asking \"which pages belong in it\" a different way would be\nan implementation to keep in step, and the two would drift. The served\nfile is diffed against what regenerating would produce now, which makes\nthe finding exactly as trustworthy as the button offered to fix it. The\nreason is named, since it decides what an editor does: the address now\nredirects, the page is no longer generated, it is gone, or it is\npublished and missing.\n\nDeliberately not keyed to the readiness score, which was the original\nsuggestion. Regenerating llms.txt does not move that score - the score is\ncrawler access and what arrives in the HTML - so prompting there would\nsend somebody to do something that changes nothing they were looking at.\nDisagreeing with the site is the condition that means regenerating helps.\n\nSecond, the sitemap module does not use vanity URLs while the page does,\nso a page with one produced two unrelated-looking findings: its real\naddress missing, and the listed address unknown. That is one problem -\ncrawlers sent through a redirect to reach content that has a direct\naddress, when search engines want the final URL in a sitemap - and it now\nreports once, naming both addresses. On luxe: 2 missing + 2 unknown\nbecame 2 redirects.\n\nBoth proven to detect, not just to agree. The llms.txt check was made to\nfire by pointing one entry back at its pre-vanity address (addressChanged\nplus the new address not listed) and by removing an entry (not listed);\nthe file was restored byte-identically afterwards and verified with diff.\n\nTwo traps found on the way, both recorded. PublicUrls cannot be asked for\na page''s non-vanity address - the rewriter re-applies the vanity under\nthe scan''s mock request - so the pairing resolves from the path side and\nonly accepts a guess the repository confirms. And SiteFilesChecker stored\nrawBody for robots.txt but not llms.txt, so the new check read an absent\nfile and reported \"not outdated\": a missing input turning into a clean\nresult, the same class of fault as a node outliving its session.","tree":{"sha":"0a2209d6930481e408165291a6308a20855d1c7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/0a2209d6930481e408165291a6308a20855d1c7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/24314845731c83e2d029f6bd09d11b15fe5b92a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/24314845731c83e2d029f6bd09d11b15fe5b92a2","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDI0MzE0ODQ1NzMxYzgzZTJkMDI5ZjZiZDA5ZDExYjE1ZmU1YjkyYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/1b34b17bc1a40c72892075e7f645e8f4450620ed","sha":"1b34b17bc1a40c72892075e7f645e8f4450620ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/1b34b17bc1a40c72892075e7f645e8f4450620ed"}],"sha":"24314845731c83e2d029f6bd09d11b15fe5b92a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/24314845731c83e2d029f6bd09d11b15fe5b92a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/1b34b17bc1a40c72892075e7f645e8f4450620ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:24:40Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:24:40Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-25: report content reachable at several addresses\n\nJahia owns the vanity URL service, so every address a page answers on is\na repository fact rather than something to discover by crawling. Three\nfindings: an alias filed under a language the site does not serve, which\nreturns 404 to everybody; one page answering on several live addresses in\none language, loudest when none is marked default; and a page with\naliases whose canonical is missing or names something else.\n\nThree, not the four the story asks for. There is no collision check\nbecause a collision cannot happen: saving a second /blogs.html made Jahia\nrename it /blogs-1.html without comment, which is also where the -1\nsuffixes on imported sites come from. Shipping a check that can never\nfire is worse than shipping none, since it implies somebody is watching a\nrisk that does not exist. The language criterion also turned out to be\nthe same thing as the non-resolving one - an alias under a language the\nsite does not publish is exactly the alias that 404s.\n\nVerified by making each case on luxe and removing it afterwards: an alias\nunder de on a site serving en and fr was reported unresolvable and does\nin fact 404; a second live alias on one page was reported as a duplicate\nnaming both addresses. Only the two vanity URLs that were already there\nremain, and the check now reports agreement.\n\nThis also uncovered a defect in the module, fixed here, that the vanity\nURLs made visible. PublicUrls returned the page tree path, and Jahia 301s\nthat to the default vanity URL. Since the fetch does not follow\nredirects, every crawler received the redirect rather than the page: the\npage scored 7 of 18 reporting \"no text in the initial HTML\", the sitemap\ncomparison called it missing, and the link graph could not match the\nlinks pointing at it. Reading the default vanity from the repository\nfixed all three at once, and the page returned to 16 of 18.","tree":{"sha":"8abe72ed97715ec60ef8cc0274ecaa234ede110d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/8abe72ed97715ec60ef8cc0274ecaa234ede110d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/1b34b17bc1a40c72892075e7f645e8f4450620ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/1b34b17bc1a40c72892075e7f645e8f4450620ed","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDFiMzRiMTdiYzFhNDBjNzI4OTIwNzVlN2Y2NDVlOGY0NDUwNjIwZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/98a61b9ac7f8d0874481e3c32a7b0fb01f007a50","sha":"98a61b9ac7f8d0874481e3c32a7b0fb01f007a50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/98a61b9ac7f8d0874481e3c32a7b0fb01f007a50"}],"sha":"1b34b17bc1a40c72892075e7f645e8f4450620ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/1b34b17bc1a40c72892075e7f645e8f4450620ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/98a61b9ac7f8d0874481e3c32a7b0fb01f007a50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:07:15Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:07:15Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-22: report the pages nothing links to\n\nA crawler can tell you what it found. It cannot tell you what it missed,\nbecause it never knew the page existed. The repository knows what is\npublished, so the difference between that and what the site actually\nlinks to is knowable, and nothing outside Jahia can work it out.\n\nThe graph is read from the rendered HTML of each page the scan already\nfetches. That was not the obvious choice - the story says walk the link\ngraph - but on the test site the main navigation is built from the page\ntree and holds no link nodes at all, so a reference-only graph called\nevery page in the menu an orphan. Reading the output instead means a\nmenu, a listing, a rich text link and a configured button all count the\nsame, and it costs no request the scan was not already making.\n\nRepository references are added on top for sources the scan never\nrendered, and only those: counting a reference that already appeared in\nthe HTML added a footer menu entry to the content total and stopped a\npage linked solely from the footer menu being reported as nav-only.\n\nNavigation and content are counted apart, by whether the anchor sits\ninside <nav> or <footer>. Being listed in a menu that names every page is\nnot somebody choosing to link to you, and the two should not be summed.\nSo the finding splits: nothing links here and the sitemap does not list\nit is unreachable; reachable only through menus or only through the\nsitemap is the weaker finding.\n\nVerified both directions on luxe. A page published under home is reported\nas menu-only, correctly, because the menu renders home''s children. A page\npublished under landing-pages, which the menu does not reach, is reported\nas an orphan. Both probes removed afterwards with markForDeletion before\npublish, and confirmed gone from default and live.\n\nTwo limits found by the results disagreeing with reality. Only the\nscanned language is judged: the published map spans every language, and\njudging the rest reported all twelve French pages as weakly linked when\nthey had simply not been fetched. And the home page is never reported,\nsince every menu and logo points at it.\n\nAlso extracts PublishedMap, shared with the sitemap comparison rather\nthan duplicating a walk whose two subtleties - guest session, all\nlanguages - were each a live false positive; moves jcontentUrl to one\nmodule now three panels use it; and bumps the drawer CACHE_SCHEMA, which\notherwise restores a stale report into a UI expecting the new field and\nsilently never shows the new banner.","tree":{"sha":"26c5c493637bea8ba1f172a504e627f49e702d2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/26c5c493637bea8ba1f172a504e627f49e702d2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/98a61b9ac7f8d0874481e3c32a7b0fb01f007a50","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/98a61b9ac7f8d0874481e3c32a7b0fb01f007a50","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDk4YTYxYjlhYzdmOGQwODc0NDgxZTNjMzJhN2IwZmIwMWYwMDdhNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/11185b6caa6d4a8e53b062de394c8c502d37cfc8","sha":"11185b6caa6d4a8e53b062de394c8c502d37cfc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/11185b6caa6d4a8e53b062de394c8c502d37cfc8"}],"sha":"98a61b9ac7f8d0874481e3c32a7b0fb01f007a50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/98a61b9ac7f8d0874481e3c32a7b0fb01f007a50"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/11185b6caa6d4a8e53b062de394c8c502d37cfc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:44:59Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:44:59Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Sitemap gets its own tab, and a presence test worth trusting\n\nThe comparison was a section of the site score, which is the wrong place:\nnothing in it is a check a page passes or fails, and none of it moves the\npercentage. It is now its own tab with its own Check now, and the result\nis stored beside the score rather than inside it - a sitemap-only refresh\nwould otherwise have built a half-filled aggregate that the score panel\nrenders as \"undefined%\". The drawer reads the same stored value, so the\ntwo can never disagree, and refreshing the sitemap no longer requires\nwalking every page.\n\nWhile moving it, the presence test turned out to be wrong in a way that\nwould have been loud. It accepted any 200 whose body contained \"<\", which\nis every HTML page. Anything answering /sitemap.xml with a page - a proxy\ncatch-all, a vanity URL, an error page served with a success code - would\nparse to zero entries and report every published page as missing, on the\ndashboard and in every page drawer. It now requires <urlset or\n<sitemapindex, the same guard the llms.txt check already had.\n\nChecked against the real bytes this server returns: Jahia''s HTML error\npage passes the old predicate and fails the new one, while the real\nsitemap index and urlset both still pass. The live site is unchanged at\n378/378 with missing: 0, so the guard is not too strict.\n\nAbsence is also no longer one message. Nothing answers, something answers\nthat is not a sitemap, and could not be reached are three different\nproblems, and the banner now names which one it is, with the URL and the\nstatus it saw.","tree":{"sha":"4241c2b6798a33629d14a1fb9f74f244d05b09f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/4241c2b6798a33629d14a1fb9f74f244d05b09f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/11185b6caa6d4a8e53b062de394c8c502d37cfc8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/11185b6caa6d4a8e53b062de394c8c502d37cfc8","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDExMTg1YjZjYWE2ZDRhOGU1M2IwNjJkZTM5NGM4YzUwMmQzN2NmYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/90c13ccb1a5f54c2c3e139e2ba085c3756c21882","sha":"90c13ccb1a5f54c2c3e139e2ba085c3756c21882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/90c13ccb1a5f54c2c3e139e2ba085c3756c21882"}],"sha":"11185b6caa6d4a8e53b062de394c8c502d37cfc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/11185b6caa6d4a8e53b062de394c8c502d37cfc8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/90c13ccb1a5f54c2c3e139e2ba085c3756c21882/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:34:18Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:34:18Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-21: report sitemap findings in full, per page and per language\n\nThe comparison was doing the work and the interface was throwing most of\nit away. Four groups collapsed to a count and four titles joined by dots,\nwith no link, no URL and no sign of the actual disagreement - the two\ndates behind a wrong lastmod were computed, stored and never shown. The\ntotals appeared only when the sitemap agreed, so the failure case was the\none with no denominator.\n\nEach finding is now its own block: heading, reason, and rows carrying a\nlink to the node, its public URL and the detail. Totals show either way.\n\nThe drawer said one thing, whether the page was missing. It now says the\nother two facts it already had access to: listed while the page itself\nsays noindex, and listed with a date that no longer matches. Both are\nonly visible per page.\n\nMatching is on path and language. The stored scan covers every language,\nso the same node appears once per URL, and matching on path alone put the\nFrench page''s stale date on the English page. Entry now carries its\nlanguage. Verified with a post stale in French only - silent in English,\nwhile one stale in English reports - and with a page listed and noindex.\n\nAlso fixes jcontentUrl, which hardcoded the pages section. Content under\n/contents belongs to content-folders, and on a site whose articles are\njmix:mainResource that is most of these findings, so most of the new\nlinks would have resolved to nothing. Verified by following one.","tree":{"sha":"3a7678108fc3267d7ee0a41868e328ecd4c18ef0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/3a7678108fc3267d7ee0a41868e328ecd4c18ef0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/90c13ccb1a5f54c2c3e139e2ba085c3756c21882","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/90c13ccb1a5f54c2c3e139e2ba085c3756c21882","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDkwYzEzY2NiMWE1ZjU0YzJjM2UxMzllMmJhMDg1YzM3NTZjMjE4ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/639c532b0ccaeb3f5fbc0170a66ed5de00f6148f","sha":"639c532b0ccaeb3f5fbc0170a66ed5de00f6148f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/639c532b0ccaeb3f5fbc0170a66ed5de00f6148f"}],"sha":"90c13ccb1a5f54c2c3e139e2ba085c3756c21882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/90c13ccb1a5f54c2c3e139e2ba085c3756c21882"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/639c532b0ccaeb3f5fbc0170a66ed5de00f6148f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:20:20Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:20:20Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-21: compare the sitemap against what the site actually publishes\n\nResolves every sitemap.xml entry back to a repository node instead of\nfetching it, so checking a 378-URL site costs no outbound requests. Four\ndisagreements are reported: published pages the sitemap never mentions,\nentries resolving to nothing published, lastmod values contradicting the\nnode''s real modification date, and pages the sitemap advertises while\ntheir markup says noindex. The drawer adds one line per page.\n\nThe published set is built as guest and across every site language.\nEither omission produces confident nonsense: scanning one language\nflagged all 189 French URLs as unknown, and scanning as root reported a\ngated page as missing from a sitemap that correctly excludes it.\n\nVerified both directions on luxe. Agreement is 378/378 with missing: 0,\nand a page published after the sitemap was generated is detected as\nmissing and raises the drawer banner. The first result proves nothing on\nits own, which is why the second test exists.\n\nAlso fixes a scope bug found while testing: SiteScorer.publishedPages\nused isdescendantnode() alone, which excludes the node named. A scope of\n/sites/x/home silently skipped home itself, and a scope naming a leaf\npage reported 0 / 0 pages with status done.\n\nKnown limits, recorded in the backlog and changelog: resolution cannot\nsee redirects, and the site walk lists jnt:page while the sitemap lists\nevery public URL, so on a site whose articles are jmix:mainResource the\ntwo counts measure different things.","tree":{"sha":"fdcd725be26cd59cab517fcc97f4337dc6fd4140","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/fdcd725be26cd59cab517fcc97f4337dc6fd4140"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/639c532b0ccaeb3f5fbc0170a66ed5de00f6148f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/639c532b0ccaeb3f5fbc0170a66ed5de00f6148f","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDYzOWM1MzJiMGNjYWViM2Y1ZmJjMDE3MGE2NmVkNWRlMDBmNjE0OGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/645847b31a92b7725625625000126ab7813c8fcc","sha":"645847b31a92b7725625625000126ab7813c8fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/645847b31a92b7725625625000126ab7813c8fcc"}],"sha":"639c532b0ccaeb3f5fbc0170a66ed5de00f6148f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/639c532b0ccaeb3f5fbc0170a66ed5de00f6148f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/645847b31a92b7725625625000126ab7813c8fcc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:02:34Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:02:34Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Documentation: rewrite the README, restructure the changelog, add a reference\n\nThe README and changelog had grown by appending a section per feature, so\nneither read as a whole any more and the README still opened as though the\ncrawler check were the only thing here.\n\nREADME rewritten as a front door: what it does, the two entry points and\nwhy the scope is split that way, what each surface answers, the score and\nthe two rules that govern it, how to build and deploy, every configuration\nkey, and the known gaps. Depth moved out to docs.\n\nCHANGELOG restructured. Nothing has shipped, so a Fixed section listing\nbugs no user ever saw was noise. It now reads as a first release: what the\nmodule does, grouped by capability, then the behaviour notes that explain\nchoices the code cannot explain by itself, then the real gaps.\n\nTwo new documents. docs/checks.md is the reference for all eighteen checks,\ngenerated against the code''s own definitions and the shipped labels: what\neach means, when it fails, why it matters. docs/architecture.md is the\nshape of the module, opening with the one decision everything else follows\nfrom and covering both fetch strategies, every class, the storage and the\nwrite path.\n\nEvery factual claim was verified against the source rather than\nremembered: check count, crawler counts and their split, the template\nthresholds, endpoint aliases, config keys, and that no CND ships. All\ninternal links resolve. That check is now a rule in the harness, because a\nnumber in a README that has drifted from the code is worse than no number.","tree":{"sha":"90dd047e796db018f2bc89f6a14204f5e9830b25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/90dd047e796db018f2bc89f6a14204f5e9830b25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/645847b31a92b7725625625000126ab7813c8fcc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/645847b31a92b7725625625000126ab7813c8fcc","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDY0NTg0N2IzMWE5MmI3NzI1NjI1NjI1MDAwMTI2YWI3ODEzYzhmY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/4c4bf2e650b8bb1fc7d8d4e6c634334cdee7ed9f","sha":"4c4bf2e650b8bb1fc7d8d4e6c634334cdee7ed9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/4c4bf2e650b8bb1fc7d8d4e6c634334cdee7ed9f"}],"sha":"645847b31a92b7725625625000126ab7813c8fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/645847b31a92b7725625625000126ab7813c8fcc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/4c4bf2e650b8bb1fc7d8d4e6c634334cdee7ed9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:55:18Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:55:18Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-18: roll findings up to the template that produced them\n\nThe story that makes this a platform feature rather than a page tool. No\nexternal product can do it, because none of them know which template\nrendered a page.\n\nThe scan already recorded a template per page, so the work is a grouping\nand two pieces of UI. The dashboard ranks templates by pages rendered, so\nthe biggest single fix is first, and separates what the template is\nanswerable for from what merely happens on some of its pages. The drawer\nadds one line under the affected check: which template it comes from, how\nmany pages share it, and that fixing it there fixes all of them.\n\nThe whole difficulty is the fourth acceptance criterion, and it is settled\nstatistically rather than by guessing. A check is blamed on the template\nonly when it fails on nearly every page that template renders, over at\nleast three pages. Three failures out of four hundred is three authors;\nfour hundred out of four hundred is the template. Anything in between stays\na page finding, because a wrong accusation costs more than a missed\nroll-up: it sends somebody to edit a shared template over a colleague''s\ntypo.\n\nProven on a page that carries both kinds at once. Its missing meta\ndescription fails on 6 of 10 pages using that template and is left with the\nauthor; its missing structured data fails on 10 of 10 and is named as the\ntemplate''s, with the count of pages one fix would cover.","tree":{"sha":"9fd55b0a8a77e041955a3f59c8dfd227ff75f468","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/9fd55b0a8a77e041955a3f59c8dfd227ff75f468"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/4c4bf2e650b8bb1fc7d8d4e6c634334cdee7ed9f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/4c4bf2e650b8bb1fc7d8d4e6c634334cdee7ed9f","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDRjNGJmMmU2NTBiOGJiMWZjN2Q4ZDRlNmM2MzQzMzRjZGVlN2VkOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/39be78a8dc27673446dd0783dfe9c3021b3aa829","sha":"39be78a8dc27673446dd0783dfe9c3021b3aa829","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/39be78a8dc27673446dd0783dfe9c3021b3aa829"}],"sha":"4c4bf2e650b8bb1fc7d8d4e6c634334cdee7ed9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/4c4bf2e650b8bb1fc7d8d4e6c634334cdee7ed9f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/39be78a8dc27673446dd0783dfe9c3021b3aa829/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:49:12Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:49:12Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Explain why the dashboard counts 17 and the drawer counts 18\n\nNot a bug, but it looked like one, which is the same problem.\n\nThe site scan fetches each page once, so it cannot evaluate the check that\ncompares what a crawler receives against what a browser receives: that\nneeds a second fetch of the same page. It is dropped from the site score\nrather than allowed to pass for free, which would inflate every site''s\nfigure. The drawer, which fetches sixteen times by design, still evaluates\nit.\n\nSo the same page reads 15/17 on the dashboard and 16/18 in the drawer, and\nboth are reporting the same two failures. Nobody can know that by looking,\nso the panel now says it and names the missing check instead of leaving it\nto be noticed.\n\nThe rule generalises and is in the harness: any check evaluated in one\nsurface and not the other has to be named where the smaller number appears.","tree":{"sha":"ce9832ca9abdef69a41049abc8e2c3eda08ed732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/ce9832ca9abdef69a41049abc8e2c3eda08ed732"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/39be78a8dc27673446dd0783dfe9c3021b3aa829","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/39be78a8dc27673446dd0783dfe9c3021b3aa829","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDM5YmU3OGE4ZGMyNzY3MzQ0NmRkMDc4M2RmZTljMzAyMWIzYWE4Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/2075b93ebd88660ea67ab15068d7ad8215ae4d3a","sha":"2075b93ebd88660ea67ab15068d7ad8215ae4d3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/2075b93ebd88660ea67ab15068d7ad8215ae4d3a"}],"sha":"39be78a8dc27673446dd0783dfe9c3021b3aa829","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/39be78a8dc27673446dd0783dfe9c3021b3aa829"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/2075b93ebd88660ea67ab15068d7ad8215ae4d3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:45:15Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:45:15Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Put the header''s shadow back\n\nMoonstone''s Header already carries a bottom shadow. The scrolling content\ndiv is its next sibling and paints its own background over it, so the\nshadow was being covered the whole time. Against the grey ground the\ncontrast hid that; once everything went white the header lost its edge\nentirely and the title ran into the content.\n\nLifting the header with position relative and a z-index puts the shadow\nback on top, rather than drawing a second border of our own.\n\nA direct consequence of the white ground, so it is recorded next to that\ndecision in the harness.","tree":{"sha":"e9fff3f462865fc6ca534d3fbd429dc5c2aa374a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/e9fff3f462865fc6ca534d3fbd429dc5c2aa374a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/2075b93ebd88660ea67ab15068d7ad8215ae4d3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/2075b93ebd88660ea67ab15068d7ad8215ae4d3a","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDIwNzViOTNlYmQ4ODY2MGVhNjdhYjE1MDY4ZDdhZDgyMTVhZTRkM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/b4a6d0a1534ad04108617dea97891e3b4d04c49e","sha":"b4a6d0a1534ad04108617dea97891e3b4d04c49e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/b4a6d0a1534ad04108617dea97891e3b4d04c49e"}],"sha":"2075b93ebd88660ea67ab15068d7ad8215ae4d3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/2075b93ebd88660ea67ab15068d7ad8215ae4d3a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/b4a6d0a1534ad04108617dea97891e3b4d04c49e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:42:27Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:42:27Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Actually make the dashboard white\n\nThe last attempt did not work and the screenshot showed why. Two mistakes,\nboth worth writing down.\n\nLayoutContent renders a wrapper div that takes the className you pass, and\nan inner scrolling div that actually paints the ground. The class went on\nthe wrapper, so it changed nothing visible while the inner div stayed grey.\nThe inner one carries a plain moonstone-layoutContent class alongside its\nhashed module class, so it can be matched globally from a scoped rule.\n\nAnd the white that did appear stopped halfway down the page because the\ncontent carried min-height:100%. Inside a scrolling container that is one\nviewport, not the length of the content, so a long page went white at the\ntop and grey below the fold. Exactly what the screenshot showed.\n\nAlso separated the headline figure from the paragraph above it and gave it\nits own size and spacing. It was reading as another line of the intro.","tree":{"sha":"d1477e22b13dacd4345311d3aed59757009a4654","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/d1477e22b13dacd4345311d3aed59757009a4654"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/b4a6d0a1534ad04108617dea97891e3b4d04c49e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/b4a6d0a1534ad04108617dea97891e3b4d04c49e","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGI0YTZkMGExNTM0YWQwNDEwODYxN2RlYTk3ODkxZTNiNGQwNGM0OWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/e3263aba0f4079f9b11ee46a667f3977a12c99eb","sha":"e3263aba0f4079f9b11ee46a667f3977a12c99eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/e3263aba0f4079f9b11ee46a667f3977a12c99eb"}],"sha":"b4a6d0a1534ad04108617dea97891e3b4d04c49e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/b4a6d0a1534ad04108617dea97891e3b4d04c49e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/e3263aba0f4079f9b11ee46a667f3977a12c99eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:38:27Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:38:27Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Give the dashboard room, and one white surface instead of cards\n\nThe cards went in last commit and were wrong. Jahia''s settings panels are a\nsingle white ground, and boxing each section made a dense panel feel\ncramped and busy rather than organised.\n\nSo: no Paper, one white surface across the layout, and Separator with big\nspacing carrying the structure between sections. That is what a separator\nis for, and it costs no visual weight.\n\nEverything also has more room. Row padding, list margins, the gap between\na heading and what it introduces, and line height on every block of prose.\nThe panel was legible before and tiring to read.\n\nNeutral information blocks now use a left rule on white rather than a grey\nfill, so the only backgrounds left in the stylesheet are the amber and red\nthat carry meaning.\n\nChecked the endpoints still answer after the restyle: the site scan reports\nthe same 82 percent over three sections, and the drawer still fetches\nsixteen agents and scores 16 of 18.","tree":{"sha":"593fa6a850592c8e87db683a1651616f25cf0a60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/593fa6a850592c8e87db683a1651616f25cf0a60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/e3263aba0f4079f9b11ee46a667f3977a12c99eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/e3263aba0f4079f9b11ee46a667f3977a12c99eb","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGUzMjYzYWJhMGY0MDc5ZjliMTFlZTQ2YTY2N2YzOTc3YTEyYzk5ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/baa31757355283e20454bbdf9b56030d8890a126","sha":"baa31757355283e20454bbdf9b56030d8890a126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/baa31757355283e20454bbdf9b56030d8890a126"}],"sha":"e3263aba0f4079f9b11ee46a667f3977a12c99eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/e3263aba0f4079f9b11ee46a667f3977a12c99eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/baa31757355283e20454bbdf9b56030d8890a126/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:32:52Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:32:52Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Make the site score panel behave like the rest of jContent\n\nFive things, all of them the difference between a working panel and one\nsomebody wants to use.\n\nEach page with a finding now links to itself in jContent, so a finding is\none click from the page it is about rather than a path to copy.\n\nThe schedule is built from dropdowns rather than typed as a Quartz\nexpression. The shape is borrowed from jcustomer-sfdc-connector''s\nCronBuilder: two Jahia modules asking the same question should ask it the\nsame way, and nobody should need cron syntax to say \"every night at three\".\nIt states that times are the server''s, which is the trap that cost a\nconfused test while building the job.\n\nThe scope uses the content picker every other module uses,\nCE_API.openPicker with type editorial, instead of a text box someone has to\ntype a repository path into correctly from memory. Typing still works.\n\nEvery input sits in a Moonstone Field with a label and a helper. They had\nneither, which left a bare text box next to another bare text box.\n\nThe panels sit on Paper. Jahia''s settings panels are white, and the grey\ncard read as unfinished next to Robots.txt and Sitemap.\n\nVerified the expressions the builder produces are the ones Quartz accepts:\ndaily at three and weekly on Sunday at half past two both schedule to the\nright next run.","tree":{"sha":"2605edd3f2664d972fa8eee206fd20a6d8173e72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/2605edd3f2664d972fa8eee206fd20a6d8173e72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/baa31757355283e20454bbdf9b56030d8890a126","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/baa31757355283e20454bbdf9b56030d8890a126","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGJhYTMxNzU3MzU1MjgzZTIwNDU0YmJkZjliNTYwMzBkODg5MGExMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/ee9493e174ba83719326a7b9de45974e483b89de","sha":"ee9493e174ba83719326a7b9de45974e483b89de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/ee9493e174ba83719326a7b9de45974e483b89de"}],"sha":"baa31757355283e20454bbdf9b56030d8890a126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/baa31757355283e20454bbdf9b56030d8890a126"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/ee9493e174ba83719326a7b9de45974e483b89de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:23:47Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:23:47Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-17: score the whole site on a schedule\n\nTurns a page tool into a site tool. A Quartz cron job walks every published\npage, scores it, and stores the result on the site.\n\nOne fetch per page, not sixteen. The drawer fetches as every crawler\nbecause comparing them is the point there; site-wide that would be 800,000\nrequests and about fifteen hours for a 50,000 page site, against roughly an\nhour this way. The cost is the thin-content ratio, which needs a second\nfetch to compare against, so it stays a drawer diagnostic. A JavaScript-only\npage is still caught by the word-count check. The one check that genuinely\nneeds several agents is dropped from the site score rather than allowed to\npass for free, which is why a site score is out of 17 and a page score out\nof 18.\n\nA scanned page is scored by building a report shaped exactly like the\ndrawer''s and running the same GeoScore over it, so the two cannot drift.\n\nStorage is a hidden nt:unstructured node on the site. No CND ships, so\nnothing can fail to register or break Content Editor on a bad deploy, and\njmix:nolive keeps it unpublished. Aggregate plus the pages that failed\nsomething, never a row per page: 2.7 KB for 13 pages, about 2 MB\nextrapolated to 10,000. The previous aggregate is kept, which is all\n\"movement since the last run\" needs.\n\nThree things had to be solved and are now traps in the harness. A\nbackground job has no HTTP request and Jahia''s URL rewriter needs one, so\nMockHttp builds request and response as dynamic proxies rather than the two\nhand-written classes the sitemap module ships. Quartz reads cron in the\nserver''s timezone, which cost one confused test. And the status endpoint\nhad to be exempted from the rate limit, because a long scan plus a polling\ndashboard blew it in under a minute and would have shown as a failure.\n\nVerified on luxe: manual run and cron trigger both produce 13 of 13 pages,\na section breakdown, and movement between runs that traced to a page\ngenuinely being gated between them rather than to the scanner.\n\nAlso fixes the gated-page banner, which was titled with the score check''s\nlabel. Check labels are phrased as the passing condition because they sit\nbeside a pass mark, so as a failure banner it said a visitor could read a\npage it was reporting as unreadable.","tree":{"sha":"fb55d40770c855fde24b6f311efe6a287eb228f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/fb55d40770c855fde24b6f311efe6a287eb228f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/ee9493e174ba83719326a7b9de45974e483b89de","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/ee9493e174ba83719326a7b9de45974e483b89de","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGVlOTQ5M2UxNzRiYTgzNzE5MzI2YTdiOWRlNDU5NzRlNDgzYjg5ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/9fe0d9818e57d575a32987ed97ef38c95778f3e4","sha":"9fe0d9818e57d575a32987ed97ef38c95778f3e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/9fe0d9818e57d575a32987ed97ef38c95778f3e4"}],"sha":"ee9493e174ba83719326a7b9de45974e483b89de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/ee9493e174ba83719326a7b9de45974e483b89de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/9fe0d9818e57d575a32987ed97ef38c95778f3e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:54:55Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:54:55Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-3: say what each crawler is for, and warn about the blocks that cost\n\nThe panel listed fifteen opaque names and a toggle. Both remaining\nacceptance criteria on GEO-3 were unmet, and together they are the\ndifference between a list and a decision.\n\nEach crawler now carries a one-line description of what it does and what\nblocking it costs, and a purpose. Seven answer questions: OAI-SearchBot,\nChatGPT-User, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot, Perplexity-User, Bingbot,\nAmazonbot. Blocking one of those takes the site out of that assistant''s\nreplies. Seven only collect content to train models: GPTBot, ClaudeBot,\nGoogle-Extended, CCBot, Bytespider, Applebot-Extended, meta-externalagent.\nRefusing those is a normal decision that costs no visibility, and plenty of\norganisations want it.\n\nThat distinction is the one nobody makes and everybody needs. Google-Extended\nis the clearest example: it controls training and grounding for Gemini and\ndoes not affect Google Search ranking at all, which is the opposite of what\nmost people assume from the name.\n\nGoogleOther is classed as mixed rather than assigned a side, because its use\nis not published. Saying so is more useful than guessing.\n\nThe panel warns only when an answering crawler is blocked, by the file or by\nthe server, and names which ones. A warning that fired on every training\nblock would be noise, and the module already refuses to treat a deliberate\nrobots.txt disallow as a failure.\n\nVerified by blocking PerplexityBot through the panel''s own merge: the\nwarning inputs appear, and clear when the file is restored.","tree":{"sha":"99bac38e2fcdfc35b70f3ed7222e8e899720081c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/99bac38e2fcdfc35b70f3ed7222e8e899720081c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/9fe0d9818e57d575a32987ed97ef38c95778f3e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/9fe0d9818e57d575a32987ed97ef38c95778f3e4","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDlmZTBkOTgxOGU1N2Q1NzVhMzI5ODdlZDk3ZWYzOGM5NTc3OGYzZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/a332dea9d2f3f7db7c74fafc1c9159a6d4c24e3c","sha":"a332dea9d2f3f7db7c74fafc1c9159a6d4c24e3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/a332dea9d2f3f7db7c74fafc1c9159a6d4c24e3c"}],"sha":"9fe0d9818e57d575a32987ed97ef38c95778f3e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/9fe0d9818e57d575a32987ed97ef38c95778f3e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/a332dea9d2f3f7db7c74fafc1c9159a6d4c24e3c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:45:42Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:45:42Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Show page-level facts in the drawer, and honour role visibility in llms.txt\n\nThe noindex notice was not reaching the drawer, for two reasons that both\nmatter more than the notice itself.\n\nThe report grew a visibility section without a CACHE_SCHEMA bump. The API\nwas right, the code was right, and the feature was invisible to anyone who\nhad opened the drawer before, because their cached report predates the\nfield. That failure mode is quiet and expensive, so the harness rule now\nnames the symptom rather than just the rule.\n\nThe notice also sat inside the crawler tab while the drawer opens on the\nscore, so it needed hunting for. Whether a page is readable at all, and\nwhether it is marked noindex, are absolute facts that frame every number\nbelow them. They now render above the tabs.\n\nSeparately, the llms.txt generator now honours role visibility, which was\na stated acceptance criterion on GEO-2 that had never been met. The walk\nruns in a guest session, so a page an editor can see but a visitor cannot\nis simply not there to advertise. That is one source of truth rather than\na second per-page check, and it makes the noindex rule and the visibility\nrule fall out of the same mechanism.\n\nProven by gating one page: the generated file drops from 11 links to 10 and\nloses that page, then recovers both when the restriction is lifted.","tree":{"sha":"5c84dbed547f8c8996f3961b4303dc75613d53a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/5c84dbed547f8c8996f3961b4303dc75613d53a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/a332dea9d2f3f7db7c74fafc1c9159a6d4c24e3c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/a332dea9d2f3f7db7c74fafc1c9159a6d4c24e3c","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGEzMzJkZWE5ZDJmM2Y3ZGI3Yzc0ZmFmYzFjOTE1OWE2ZDRjMjRlM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/a062437f42c133a52399c19aa6d901e9fa555ee6","sha":"a062437f42c133a52399c19aa6d901e9fa555ee6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/a062437f42c133a52399c19aa6d901e9fa555ee6"}],"sha":"a332dea9d2f3f7db7c74fafc1c9159a6d4c24e3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/a332dea9d2f3f7db7c74fafc1c9159a6d4c24e3c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/a062437f42c133a52399c19aa6d901e9fa555ee6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:39:10Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:39:10Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Fix the panel crash, and count noindex pages as content AI will not use\n\nTwo reports, both real.\n\nThe settings panel threw \"Cannot access before initialization\" and never\nrendered. The effect that runs the access check when the panel opens sat\nabove the callback it calls, and a dependency array is evaluated during\nrender, before the const. Moved below the declaration; the rule is now in\nthe harness.\n\nA page marked noindex was missing from the invisible-content list. It is a\nmixin the community robots-noindex module sets, so reading it costs no\nfetch and needs no HTML parsing. Those pages are now listed under \"closed\non purpose\" rather than as findings: the page will not be cited, but an\neditor ticked a box to say so, and a tool that reports a deliberate choice\nas a defect is a tool people stop reading. The same rule already keeps a\nrobots.txt disallow out of the score.\n\nThe drawer states it for the page in view, as information rather than a\nfailure, and the deliberate list now shows each row''s reason since it holds\ntwo different ones.\n\nThis also closes a stated acceptance criterion on GEO-2 that was quietly\nunmet: the llms.txt generator is supposed to honour noindex and did not.\nHanding an assistant a map of the site that includes pages you have asked\nengines not to index contradicts itself. On the test site that drops the\ngenerated file from 13 links to 11.","tree":{"sha":"52a64a49ede07b834a09503a1f28f3c3cc2c34d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/52a64a49ede07b834a09503a1f28f3c3cc2c34d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/a062437f42c133a52399c19aa6d901e9fa555ee6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/a062437f42c133a52399c19aa6d901e9fa555ee6","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGEwNjI0MzdmNDJjMTMzYTUyMzk5YzE5YWE2ZDkwMWU5ZmE1NTVlZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/7407b67b7040d6d9a3a4e799b99f9c55b065ffe2","sha":"7407b67b7040d6d9a3a4e799b99f9c55b065ffe2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/7407b67b7040d6d9a3a4e799b99f9c55b065ffe2"}],"sha":"a062437f42c133a52399c19aa6d901e9fa555ee6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/a062437f42c133a52399c19aa6d901e9fa555ee6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/7407b67b7040d6d9a3a4e799b99f9c55b065ffe2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:33:45Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:33:45Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Show whether crawlers are actually served, and fix the empty stance column\n\nTwo problems in the settings panel, one cosmetic and one substantive.\n\nThe stance column rendered empty. A Moonstone Switch is a 38x20 box whose\ntwo children are both absolutely positioned, so it has no in-flow content\nand collapses to nothing inside the Typography that TableCell wraps its\nchildren in. The toggles were there and invisible. That panel is now a\nlist, like the score and the crawler results before it, which is the third\ntime this component has bitten us and is now a trap in the harness: Table\nis a display grid for short text, not a place for controls.\n\nThe substantive one: the panel stated a policy and never said whether the\nserver honours it. robots.txt saying a crawler is allowed means nothing if\nthe delivery tier refuses it, and that gap is what this module exists to\nclose. The panel now runs the crawler check against the site''s home page\nwhen it opens, through the same endpoint the drawer uses so there is one\nimplementation, and leads with a single line: all fifteen crawlers served,\nor how many are refused, plus whether policy and reality agree. Each row\ncarries what the server did and how long it took, beside the toggle.\n\npreviewRobots returns the site''s home page path so the panel knows which\npage to test. The check re-runs on demand from a button.","tree":{"sha":"7fcdc6a52a51a7a8a1f4bb4ee32b71a94c0197f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/7fcdc6a52a51a7a8a1f4bb4ee32b71a94c0197f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/7407b67b7040d6d9a3a4e799b99f9c55b065ffe2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/7407b67b7040d6d9a3a4e799b99f9c55b065ffe2","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDc0MDdiNjdiNzA0MGQ2ZDlhM2E0ZTc5OWI5OWY5YzU1YjA2NWZmZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/b69f88cb6be85f746070a21cd78304d5a34cc649","sha":"b69f88cb6be85f746070a21cd78304d5a34cc649","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/b69f88cb6be85f746070a21cd78304d5a34cc649"}],"sha":"7407b67b7040d6d9a3a4e799b99f9c55b065ffe2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/7407b67b7040d6d9a3a4e799b99f9c55b065ffe2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/b69f88cb6be85f746070a21cd78304d5a34cc649/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:23:12Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:23:12Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"GEO-19: list the content no AI can ever read\n\nA crawler served a login form gets a cheerful 200 and reports success, so\nan external audit counts a gated page as content that works. Only the\nrepository knows better, which is why this check cannot be bought.\n\nGuestVisibility lists published pages with a system session and then reads\neach one again in a session owned by guest. Readability is asked, never\nreasoned about from ACLs.\n\nThe value is in the second half of the story: closed on purpose is\nseparated from closed by accident. A page inside a branch that is closed as\na whole is a members area and is listed apart; a closed page inside an open\nsection is the finding. An expired visibility condition is read generically\noff any condition carrying j:end, so a custom condition with the same\nproperty is handled and an unknown one is ignored rather than guessed at.\n\nSurfaces: a scan on its own tab of the settings panel, and in the drawer a\ncritical score check plus a banner, because a gated page scores nothing\nwhatever else is right about it.\n\nTwo things had to be learned the hard way, and both are now traps in\n.agents/README.md.\n\ndoExecuteWithSystemSessionAsUser does NOT enforce ACLs. It is a system\nsession merely attributed to a user. The first version used it and reported\nevery page readable, which would have shipped a permissions check that could\nnever find anything.\n\nA DENY ace does not close a page against an inherited grant. Guest still\nread the page and hasPermission stayed true. setAclInheritanceBreak(true),\nwhat jContent''s restrict-access does, is what actually closes it, so a\nfixture built on the deny proves nothing.\n\nVerified on 8.2.3.2 by restricting one page: scan reported it as the only\nfinding, the drawer flagged it, all sixteen crawlers got 404, and the site\nwas restored to 13 of 13 readable afterwards.\n\nKnown limits, recorded in the backlog: the scan is synchronous and capped at\n2000 pages, so a large site needs GEO-17''s background job, and the\ncross-check against the crawler result is shown side by side rather than\nstated as one sentence.","tree":{"sha":"620635fc5e48ea41e36918ccd4c03a27e1bdc936","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/620635fc5e48ea41e36918ccd4c03a27e1bdc936"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/b69f88cb6be85f746070a21cd78304d5a34cc649","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/b69f88cb6be85f746070a21cd78304d5a34cc649","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGI2OWY4OGNiNmJlODVmNzQ2MDcwYTIxY2Q3ODMwNGQ1YTM0Y2M2NDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/45045505fc1af2443253af7dd592229b45879947","sha":"45045505fc1af2443253af7dd592229b45879947","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/45045505fc1af2443253af7dd592229b45879947"}],"sha":"b69f88cb6be85f746070a21cd78304d5a34cc649","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/b69f88cb6be85f746070a21cd78304d5a34cc649"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/45045505fc1af2443253af7dd592229b45879947/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:12:30Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:12:30Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Check every crawler we claim to have a policy for\n\nThe robots.txt checker evaluated fifteen crawler tokens and the settings\npanel offered a toggle for each, but the servlet only ever fetched eight.\nClaude-SearchBot, Perplexity-User, GoogleOther, Bytespider, Amazonbot,\nApplebot-Extended and meta-externalagent had a stated policy that nothing\nverified, which is precisely the gap this module exists to close: the\nmismatch between what robots.txt says and what the server does.\n\nBoth halves now read one registry, AiCrawlers, so the lists cannot drift\napart again. Adding a crawler is one entry there and nowhere else.\n\nSixteen sequential fetches at up to 8s each is over two minutes, so they\nnow run three at a time and are consumed strictly in order, keeping the\ncontrol first for the thin-content comparison. Three is the compromise the\nharness already called for: enough to be quick, far short of what a WAF\nreads as an attack. Measured at about a second against a local site.\n\nThe coverage paid for itself immediately. On the test site Amazonbot and\nGoogleOther are disallowed in robots.txt and served anyway; neither was\nbeing checked before.\n\ntest-fixtures/probe.py is regenerated from the same registry and agrees\nwith the servlet row for row.","tree":{"sha":"8882635328c9840b99eee2d6491eab1134744e39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/8882635328c9840b99eee2d6491eab1134744e39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/45045505fc1af2443253af7dd592229b45879947","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/45045505fc1af2443253af7dd592229b45879947","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDQ1MDQ1NTA1ZmMxYWYyNDQzMjUzYWY3ZGQ1OTIyMjliNDU4Nzk5NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/45ae8749dfa64f48e6efd224095b4ac8b39e75f8","sha":"45ae8749dfa64f48e6efd224095b4ac8b39e75f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/45ae8749dfa64f48e6efd224095b4ac8b39e75f8"}],"sha":"45045505fc1af2443253af7dd592229b45879947","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/45045505fc1af2443253af7dd592229b45879947"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/45ae8749dfa64f48e6efd224095b4ac8b39e75f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:57:46Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"SMO"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:57:46Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"SMO"},"message":"Add the BotRank backlog and a docs index\n\ndocs/botrank-backlog.md brings GEO-1 to GEO-16 into the repo. Until now they\nlived only in a published analysis page and two decks, so a session opening\nthis repo cold saw less than half the backlog.\n\nIt carries the 24-criteria comparison against page-audit, the jContent\nplacement map with a confidence column, the four waves, the deliberate\nexclusions, the open questions gating Wave 2, and the risk table. Wave 1\nstories are marked built, with the two places the implementation\ndeliberately departed from the original scope and the one thing that turned\nout to be impossible on this stack.\n\ndocs/README.md is a short index over the five docs with a read-first order.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DudRPKuf3b31XRYEWz2RPQ","tree":{"sha":"d055c82afba0f372009061280baab7594f9fe048","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/d055c82afba0f372009061280baab7594f9fe048"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/45ae8749dfa64f48e6efd224095b4ac8b39e75f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/45ae8749dfa64f48e6efd224095b4ac8b39e75f8","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDQ1YWU4NzQ5ZGZhNjRmNDhlNmVmZDIyNDA5NWI0YWM4YjM5ZTc1Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/72c8f62e4756efeeb91026f9aecfa8427929cf9b","sha":"72c8f62e4756efeeb91026f9aecfa8427929cf9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/72c8f62e4756efeeb91026f9aecfa8427929cf9b"}],"sha":"45ae8749dfa64f48e6efd224095b4ac8b39e75f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/45ae8749dfa64f48e6efd224095b4ac8b39e75f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/72c8f62e4756efeeb91026f9aecfa8427929cf9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:25:06Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"SMO"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:25:06Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"SMO"},"message":"Add Jahia-native GEO backlog, GEO-17 to GEO-25\n\nNine stories that need no external vendor. Each one exists because\nJahia knows something a crawler cannot, or can compute it at a scale a\nmetered tool cannot afford.\n\nStates the placement rule once and applies it to every story: the\ndashboard owns the list and the ranking, the drawer owns the one-line\nverdict about this page. Several stories have both halves, and each\nsays explicitly what the drawer shows, or that it shows nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DudRPKuf3b31XRYEWz2RPQ","tree":{"sha":"676ec56cc3f5fe6a84fb96d94e071dbf1247fcae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/676ec56cc3f5fe6a84fb96d94e071dbf1247fcae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/72c8f62e4756efeeb91026f9aecfa8427929cf9b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/72c8f62e4756efeeb91026f9aecfa8427929cf9b","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDcyYzhmNjJlNDc1NmVmZWViOTEwMjZmOWFlY2ZhODQyNzkyOWNmOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/900689c213c27a7e1b17974b358c71aa3180838a","sha":"900689c213c27a7e1b17974b358c71aa3180838a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/900689c213c27a7e1b17974b358c71aa3180838a"}],"sha":"72c8f62e4756efeeb91026f9aecfa8427929cf9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/72c8f62e4756efeeb91026f9aecfa8427929cf9b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/900689c213c27a7e1b17974b358c71aa3180838a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:59:58Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"SMO"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:59:58Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"SMO"},"message":"Fix public URL scheme and port; add a standalone probe\n\npublicUrlFor hardcoded https and dropped the port, so any site with a\nserver name on a local http instance would have been fetched at\nhttps://host with no port and failed every row. It now keeps the scheme\nand port the request arrived on.\n\ntest-fixtures/probe.py is the reference implementation, runnable from a\nmachine that can actually reach the site. Same logic as the servlet:\nper-agent fetch, no cookies, no redirect following, initial HTML only,\nplus robots.txt and llms.txt with the same cross-check. Use it to tell\nwhether the module is wrong or the site really is like that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DudRPKuf3b31XRYEWz2RPQ","tree":{"sha":"1fc3f6ff2486b8417a0857e3e7ef08182d2a32d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/1fc3f6ff2486b8417a0857e3e7ef08182d2a32d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/900689c213c27a7e1b17974b358c71aa3180838a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/900689c213c27a7e1b17974b358c71aa3180838a","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDkwMDY4OWMyMTNjMjdhN2UxYjE3OTc0YjM1OGM3MWFhMzE4MDgzOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/e2a30624984b561e894ae0b73a6876d4722f64cd","sha":"e2a30624984b561e894ae0b73a6876d4722f64cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/e2a30624984b561e894ae0b73a6876d4722f64cd"}],"sha":"900689c213c27a7e1b17974b358c71aa3180838a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/900689c213c27a7e1b17974b358c71aa3180838a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/e2a30624984b561e894ae0b73a6876d4722f64cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:40:07Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:40:07Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Stop the crawler results overlapping\n\nSame root cause as the score list, second symptom. Moonstone''s TableCell\nwraps its children in a Typography, so the wrapping row of markup\nindicators overlapped the line above instead of pushing it down, and the\nfixed row height meant hasMultipleLines only bought one extra line.\n\nThe crawler results are now a list: a head line per agent carrying the\nstatus chip, the name and the timing, with the indicators wrapping freely\nunderneath. Two things the table could not show are now visible: an agent\nthat received far less text than the browser is marked, and an agent that\nnever answered says so instead of showing a dash.\n\nTable is kept where it belongs, on the robots stance grid and the\nsite-files report, where every value is short and fits one line.","tree":{"sha":"071a8c2ffbb80590a5ba0c4b175f0b8ff993c32f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/071a8c2ffbb80590a5ba0c4b175f0b8ff993c32f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/e2a30624984b561e894ae0b73a6876d4722f64cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/e2a30624984b561e894ae0b73a6876d4722f64cd","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGUyYTMwNjI0OTg0YjU2MWU4OTRhZTBiNzNhNjg3NmQ0NzIyZjY0Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/bc5fca08bc196cc4593570d1bd2366f00f861a9b","sha":"bc5fca08bc196cc4593570d1bd2366f00f861a9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/bc5fca08bc196cc4593570d1bd2366f00f861a9b"}],"sha":"e2a30624984b561e894ae0b73a6876d4722f64cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/e2a30624984b561e894ae0b73a6876d4722f64cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/bc5fca08bc196cc4593570d1bd2366f00f861a9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:36:22Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:36:22Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Changelog: score list and wider drawer","tree":{"sha":"b997ddbeedc608b6014885cb6f0ebdeccab0ea42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/b997ddbeedc608b6014885cb6f0ebdeccab0ea42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/bc5fca08bc196cc4593570d1bd2366f00f861a9b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/bc5fca08bc196cc4593570d1bd2366f00f861a9b","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKGJjNWZjYTA4YmMxOTZjYzQ1OTM1NzBkMWJkMjM2NmYwMGY4NjFhOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/3cdf7bb717b2d66784f851b463ea8229f4f4406b","sha":"3cdf7bb717b2d66784f851b463ea8229f4f4406b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/3cdf7bb717b2d66784f851b463ea8229f4f4406b"}],"sha":"bc5fca08bc196cc4593570d1bd2366f00f861a9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/bc5fca08bc196cc4593570d1bd2366f00f861a9b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/3cdf7bb717b2d66784f851b463ea8229f4f4406b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:36:06Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T15:36:06Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"Stop the drawer clipping check explanations\n\nMoonstone Table rows are a fixed 48px, 64px with hasMultipleLines, and\nTableBodyCell scrolls its overflow. That is right for short tabular values\nand wrong for prose: each score check carries a one-line label plus a\ntwo-line explanation, so the explanation was being cut off with no way to\nread it.\n\n- The score is now a list rather than a Table, so its text wraps and the\n  item grows to fit. Still Moonstone inside: Chip for the verdict and the\n  severity, Typography for the text.\n- The crawler table stays a Table, since its values are short, but sets\n  hasMultipleLines because the marks column wraps to two lines and a 48px\n  row would clip the second.\n- Drawer widened from 620px to 820px, and max-width raised to 96vw. The\n  content is a label, an explanation and two chips on one line; 620 was\n  never enough for that.","tree":{"sha":"3b6b5b33e8f02b2cf529f6c8c3609190b86f7de3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/trees/3b6b5b33e8f02b2cf529f6c8c3609190b86f7de3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/git/commits/3cdf7bb717b2d66784f851b463ea8229f4f4406b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/3cdf7bb717b2d66784f851b463ea8229f4f4406b","node_id":"C_kwDOUVN91NoAKDNjZGY3YmI3MTdiMmQ2Njc4NGY4NTFiNDYzZWE4MjI5ZjRmNDQwNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/geo-readiness/commit/f5a98b9ffd61cf005749aaf6dcac03a0206f6c00","sha":"f5a98b9ffd61cf005749aaf6dcac03a0206f6c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/f5a98b9ffd61cf005749aaf6dcac03a0206f6c00"}],"sha":"3cdf7bb717b2d66784f851b463ea8229f4f4406b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/geo-readiness/commits/3cdf7bb717b2d66784f851b463ea8229f4f4406b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githu